\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICAN FREED AFTER AMMO ARREST RETURNS HOME AFTER 101 DAYS IN TURKS AND CAICOS\b0\par\par\uc2 536 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORMS, TRAVEL, WEIGAND\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 HAITI, LLOYD, BIDEN, RUTO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. MISSIONARIES KILLED IN HAITI GANG ATTACK\par \par \uc2 AUSTIN, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECY. AUSTIN UNDERGOING PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 TURKS AND CAICOS, HAGERICH, SENTENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN FREED AFTER AMMO ARREST\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the American father sentenced for bringing ammunition into Turks and Caicos. He was facing a possible 12 years in prison. Instead, he's now returning home after paying a fine. Tonight, what this could mean for the other Americans facing similar charges. Here's ABC's Matt Rivers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETURNS HOME AFTER 101 DAYS IN TURKS AND CAICOS\par \par \uc2 MATT RIVERS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Bryan Hagerich headed home to Pennsylvania as a free man, racing through the airport in Turks and Caicos, on his way to finally see his two children after spending 101 days on the islands where he faced a possible 12-year prison sentence for having ammo in his luggage.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN HAGERICH (FATHER)\par \par \uc2 We're on the airplane.\par \par \uc2 MATT RIVERS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A relieved Hagerich and his wife Ashley earlier today after a judge gave him a suspended 52-week sentence and a $6,700 fine, allowing him to go free.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN HAGERICH (FATHER)\par \par \uc2 It's the best day.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY HAGERICH (WIFE OF BRYAN HAGERICH)\par \par \uc2 God is so good.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN HAGERICH (FATHER)\par \par \uc2 Yes, all of our prayers have been answered.\par \par \uc2 MATT RIVERS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hagerich pleaded guilty, saying he'd forgotten the ammo was in the bag when he went on vacation back in February. Still, the crime carried a minimum of a dozen years in prison due to a strict new amendment to the island's firearms law. But the judge today finding exceptional circumstances in his case and determining that sentence to be "unjust and disproportionate to the crime committed." Tonight, Hagerich and his wife say they will continue to advocate for the other four Americans accused of similar charges.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN HAGERICH (FATHER)\par \par \uc2 We've set some precedent today. My work, our work is not done until all of them get home.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEY HAGERICH (WIFE OF BRYAN HAGERICH)\par \par \uc2 They're our family. We love them. And we can't wait till they're reunited with their families.\par \par \uc2 BRYAN HAGERICH (FATHER)\par \par \uc2 And we're all in this together.\par \par \uc2 MATT RIVERS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the big question, what happens to the other cases and sentences involving the other four Americans charged with similar things in Turks and Caicos? Does this ruling set a precedent? Meanwhile, the Turks and Caicos government saying that justice has been served in this case, as the law intended. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Matt Rivers, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LA GOVERNOR SIGNS ABORTION PILL BILL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to more breaking news tonight. Louisiana's governor signing a controversial bill reclassifying two abortion pills as controlled and dangerous substances.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Opponents say the new classification will make it harder to prescribe the pills. But supporters say it will protect pregnant women from coerced abortions. Possessing the drugs without a prescription could lead to possible jail time.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240529ek5o00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND ABORTION PILL BILL LOUISIANA BILL CLASSIFIES ABORTION PILL AS CONTROLLED SUBSTANCES\b0\par\par\uc2 632 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, STANTON, WHITAKER, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 SCHEFFLER, VILLAROEL, GILLIS, ROMINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE RELEASE SCHEFFLER VIDEOS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, BILL, PRESSLY, LUNEAU, LOUISIANA, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND ABORTION PILL BILL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the major new headline involving women and abortion rights in this country. Tonight, the Louisiana legislature has passed a first-of-its-kind bill classifying two abortion bills as dangerous controlled substances. Possessing the drugs without a prescription could lead to jail time. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOUISIANA BILL CLASSIFIES ABORTION PILL AS CONTROLLED SUBSTANCES\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Louisiana poised to become the first state in the nation to classify two abortion pills as dangerous controlled substances. The state legislature now sending the bill to the Republican governor who's expected to sign it into law.\par \par \uc2 POLITICIAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Twenty-nine yays and seven nays, and the bill has been concurred in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOUISIANA BILL\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion is already largely banned in Louisiana, but this bill would make even possessing the abortion pills without a prescription punishable by jail time and hefty fines. It's designed to crackdown on their illegal distribution.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR THOMAS PRESSLY (REP) (LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 These pills can be used for dangerous and harmful acts.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Drugs designated as dangerous controlled substances are typically ones with potential for addiction and abuse. Not abortion pills.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR W JAY LUNEAU (DEM) (LOUISIANA)\par \par \uc2 These medications are used in emergent situations for women all the time, and nobody disagrees with that.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion pills are used in more than half of abortions in the US. In Louisiana, doctors will now be required to get special licenses to obtain the drugs.\par \par \uc2 DR JANE MARTIN (MATERNAL FETAL MEDICINE SPECIALIST)\par \par \uc2 I worry there will be some stigma and some, you know, some taboo if the government is saying, this should be controlled.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Biden administration pointing the finger squarely at \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who appointed three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned roe versus wade. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  tweeting, "Absolutely unconscionable. Let's be clear, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this." Louisiana is one of 21 states to ban or severely restrict access to abortion since Roe was overturned. Trump has taken credit for sparking the change.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We broke Roe v. Wade, and we did something that nobody thought was possible, we gave it back to the states. And the states are working very brilliantly.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, Trump claimed weeks ago that he'd be releasing his position on the abortion pill, whether it should be further restricted, saying that he has strong views on that. But, David, tonight, we are still waiting on that announcement.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel, while we have you, the other headline tonight involving the race for president. Senate Democrats launching an investigation into a recent meeting that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  held with oil executives, and whether Trump made any promises to those executives?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And, David, sources tell us that the former president told these oil executives at Mar-a-Lago that they should donate a billion dollars to his campaign because, if he is re-elected, he would step up drilling and also rollback a series of environmental regulations. Many of which were put in place during the Biden administration. Senate Democrats are now looking into whether any of those promises amount to a quid pro quo. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott on that as well. Thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240528ek5n00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES HIGHEST-EVER EARLY FORECAST/STUDY ON CANCER AND PREGNANCY\b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, STANTON, WHITAKER, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 SCHEFFLER, VILLAROEL, GILLIS, ROMINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE RELEASE SCHEFFLER VIDEOS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, BILL, PRESSLY, LUNEAU, LOUISIANA, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND ABORTION PILL BILL\par \par \uc2 TICKETMASTER, LIVE NATION, LAWSUIT, AKMAKJIAN, GARLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ SUES TO BREAK UP TICKET GIANT\par \par \uc2 BURGLARY TOURISM, ABRAMYAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: HIDDEN CAMERA CRIME RING\par \par \uc2 NOAA\uc2 , HURRICANE, BREAST CANCER, PREGNANCY, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGHEST-EVER EARLY FORECAST\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight here, the new hurricane forecast. \uc2 NOAA\uc2  issuing its highest ever early forecast for the upcoming season, calling it, quote, "extraordinary."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2024 HURRICANE SEASON\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Seventeen to 25 named storms. The average is 14. Eight to 13 of those expected to be hurricanes, four to seven of them major. Scientists say the warming ocean temperatures from climate change likely fueling more powerful storms.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY ON CANCER AND PREGNANCY\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, new hope for women who have had breast cancer who want to have a child.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to a preliminary study, three-quarters of women 40 and younger with non-metastatic breast cancer who wanted children were able to become pregnant. About two-thirds had a baby. Scientists say fertility preservation such as egg freezing nearly tripled the odds of having a baby.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back here tonight, Celine Dion and what she's sharing. And your first look tonight, The Beach Boys, 60 years later, returning to a familiar spot.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240528ek5n00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news as we come on the air. The severe storms set to hit just as millions travel for the holiday. Ginger Zee is standing by. And the storm that blew through New York City already.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS THREATEN HOLIDAY TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the new line of storms from Texas all the way north.\par \par \uc2 RESIDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my God.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Possible tornadoes, damaging winds, and that thunderstorm moving over New York City, downing trees and power lines. Thousands of flights affected. And tonight here, the new outlook for Memorial Day across the country. Ginger is here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCOTTIE SCHEFFLER POLICE VIDEO REVEALED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, police releasing new video showing the confrontation between the world's number one golfer, Scottie Scheffler, and a police officer directing traffic around a deadly accident in Louisville. What the video shows.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND ABORTION PILL BILL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, women and abortion rights in this country. The Louisiana legislature passing a first-of-its-kind bill, classifying two abortion pills as dangerous controlled substances. Possessing the drugs without a prescription could lead to jail time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ SUES TO BREAK UP LIVE NATION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department filing about anti-trust lawsuit to break up the parent company of \uc2 Ticketmaster\uc2 , accusing Live Nation and \uc2 Ticketmaster\uc2  of monopolizing the concert industry.\par \par \uc2 CUSTOMER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I waited in line for, like, six hours.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You'll remember the Taylor Swift concert tickets, the fans so upset. Tonight, the DOJ says Live Nation driving up prices, listing the ways they allegedly do it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE SMASH ALLEGED CRIME RING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the groups allegedly targeting homes with Wi-Fi-jamming equipment to knock out home security systems. Authorities breaking up what they're calling burglary tourism. Where they were breaking in and how they were doing it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STAGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Horrific images, the deadly stage collapse during a rally in Mexico. At least nine people killed. Strong winds tearing down the stage.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREGNANCY AFTER CANCER STUDY\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, young women, breast cancer, and future pregnancy. What a new study reveals.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELINE DION'S PERSONAL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Celine Dion and her deeply personal battle. What she's revealing tonight. The new hurricane forecast is out tonight. \uc2 NOAA\uc2  issuing its highest ever early forecast for the upcoming hurricane season and what it shows. And the remarkable new documentary about The Beach Boys. From a garage band to music legends, and your first look right here tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240528ek5n00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP WALKS BACK CONTRACEPTION COMMENTS SAYS HE "WILL NEVER ADVOCATE IMPOSING RESTRICTIONS ON BIRTH CONTROL"\b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY TORNADO OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES, DAMAGE, RESIDENTS, DINK, FATALITIES\par \par \uc2 STORMS, WINDS, HAIL, THUNDERSTORMS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, DEFENSE, JUDGE, JURY, DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , CONTRACEPTION, RESTRICTIONS, ROE V WADE, STATES\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, almost certainly the only before the election. Okay, Aaron, thanks very much. The former President also playing cleanup yesterday after posting a Nazi phrase on his website and suggesting restrictions on contraception in an interview. Rachel Scott has the story. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP WALKS BACK CONTRACEPTION COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAYS HE "WILL NEVER ADVOCATE IMPOSING RESTRICTIONS ON BIRTH CONTROL"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning to you. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was asked directly whether he would support restrictions on birth control. The former President said it was something they were looking at, only to back track hours later.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  walking back his comments suggesting he's open to restricting birth control if re-elected.\par \par \uc2 TV HOST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you support any restrictions on a person's right to contraception?\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Well, we're looking at that, and I'm going to have is a policy on that very shortly. And I think it's something that you'll find interesting. It's another issue that's very interesting. But you will find it, I think, very smart. I think it's a smart decision. But we will be releasing it very soon.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In an interview with a local Pittsburgh TV station, the former President asked to clarify if that meant he would, in fact, support restrictions on contraception.\par \par \uc2 TV HOST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 You may want to support some restrictions? Like the morning after pill or something?\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We are also, you know, things really do have a lot to do with the states. And some states are going to have different policies than others.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Biden campaign seizing on those words saying "Women across the country are already suffering from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's post Roe nightmare. And if he wins a second term, it's clear he wants to go even further." And then hours later Trump backtracked, writing on social media he has "Never and will never advocate imposing restrictions on birth control or other contraceptives."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But that's something he never made clear in the interview. The former President often boasts about appointing three of the five Supreme Court Justices that overturned Roe verse Wade, clearing the way for 21 states to ban or restrict access to abortion.\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We broke Roe V. Wade.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just weeks ago Trump told "Time" magazine he wouldn't intervene if states wanted to monitor or punish pregnant women seeking abortion saying "It's irrelevant whether I'm comfortable or not, it's totally irrelevant, because the states are going to make those decisions."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is still major questions about whether the former President supports further restricting access to the abortion pill, Mifepristone, which is used in more than half of abortions in the United States. Trump said he would release his position weeks ago and he still has not done so, Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240612ek5m00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN'S CANCER FIGHT ACTRESS ON HER DIAGNOSIS & TREATING THE AGGRESSIVE BREAST CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 1,980 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ZELENSKYY, WAR, UKRAINE, RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, BIDEN, TRUMP, DEBATES\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, COHEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: \uc2 MICHAEL COHEN\uc2  BACK ON THE STAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: FORMER FIXER SET FOR SECOND DAY OF CROSS-EXAMINATION IN TRUMP CRIMINAL TRIAL\par \par \uc2 ARRESTS, COLLEGE PROTEST, GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: RIOT POLICE SWARM \uc2 UC IRVINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: NEW ARRESTS AS OFFICERS CLEAR OCCUPIED BUILDING & ENCAMPMENT\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , PIER, AID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: NEW HUMANITARIAN AID HEADING TO GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: TEMPORARY PIER BUILT BY U.S. SET TO RECEIVE FIRST SHIPMENT\par \par \uc2 BUTKER, ELLIS, COMMENCEMENT SPEECH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: CHIEFS KICKER UNDER FIRE FOR COMMENCEMENT SPEECH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: FACES BACKLASH FOR COMMENTS ON ABORTION, GAY RIGHTS & WOMEN\par \par \uc2 CRASH, BRANHAM, THOMAS, CARDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: NEW VIDEO OF DRAMATIC TRUCK CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: SHOWS MOMENTS SEMI NEARLY PLUNGES OFF BRIDGE\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM BROADWAY MUSICAL, "ALADDIN ON BROADWAY"\par \par \uc2 MUNN, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But right now, we have an ABC News exclusive. Michael, we know you sat down with Olivia Munn.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OLIVIA MUNN'S CANCER FIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTRESS ON HER DIAGNOSIS & TREATING THE AGGRESSIVE BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I sat down with Olivia. It is her first on-camera interview since revealing her most recent surgeries in her breast cancer battle. We discussed everything from treatment to fertility to her hopes for the future. And she wants to share her story to help others.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 You never know what's going on in someone's life.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 You know, that, that privately people are battling things that you would never know.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Actress Olivia Munn opening up about the private health battle she's been fighting after an unexpected breast cancer diagnosis last year.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Clear mammogram, clear ultrasound. Genetic testing, I have zero chance of having any cancer genetically. Then my doctor said, there us this lifetime risk assessment test, and I took it for you. And you were at 37.3%, which puts me into high risk. And she said, I want you to go get an MRI. And that's when they said, well, we found something.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you heard the word cancer, what went through your mind?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I mean, honestly, I just thought of my baby. You know, cancer is the, that's the word you don't want to hear. There's a lot of other things that you feel like you can beat by, you know, cancer take downs a lot of people. And I just thought about my baby.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OLIVIA MUNN DIAGNOSIS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Last April, Munn was diagnosed with stage 1 of the aggressive luminal B breast cancer in both breasts.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what did they explain to you about your prognosis?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 They said that if I was extremely aggressive that I could fight this and win. But at the same time, once they started finding all of these little spots in my breast, like, oh, there's another tumor, there's another tumor. There was such an urgency to it because we had to get in and make some really big decisions.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Munn getting a double mastectomy just 30 days after receiving the diagnosis. In March, the 43-year-old decided to open up about her experience on social media.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Do it for him. Do it for your baby.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Including this raw moment right before she went into surgery.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I'm ready.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How did you know you were ready?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I didn't. I just had to say it. You know, sometimes you just, you just say it and hope that your body will go with it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why did you want to document this journey that you're on right now?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Well, because if I didn't make it, I wanted my son, when he got older, to know that I fought to be here. That I tried my best.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're going to make me cry.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 You want the people in your life, you want the people that maybe don't understand what's going on right now to know that, like, you did everything you could to be here.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Munn shared a two-and-a-half-year-old son Malcolm with her partner, comedian John Mulaney.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And how has it been having John there to support you?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 He is, he's honestly just the best human being. He comes to everything in life with so much compassion and understanding. The one problem with that, he makes me laugh so much that I'm like, you have, there's times, I'm like, you have to leave the room, like this is insane.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that's what happens when you, when you're with a funny man.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I know.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 He's a funny guy.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I know. So, I just say, leave the room. You have to leave. And I was, you're going to make me angry now because it's going, I'm going to, you know, literally pop a stitch.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's going to hurt me.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 It's going to hurt.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Because of the potential impacts of cancer treatment on her future fertility, she decided to undergo egg retrieval, something Munn had done twice before in her 30s.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTRESS ON HER TREATMENT, FERTILITY & WHAT'S NEXT FOR HER\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 John and I had a long talk about it. We realized that we weren't done growing our family. So, right after the double mastectomy, I went through a round of egg retrieval. And that's a scary process because I have a cancer that feeds off of hormones. So, I knew there was a risk. And our doctor said, look, we're going to get one for you and then we are going to call it. And then doctor called and he said, hey, we got the results back, it's two healthy embryos. And I, we, I mean, just started bawling, crying, both of us.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And have you thought about, you know, that far ahead about what the future of your family looks like?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 We really just hope that it works out for us to have another baby. We just want one more. I'm not going to ask for too much more in this life, I promise. I just want, just want one more baby.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Because luminal B is a hormone-positive type of breast cancer, Munn's treatment involves suppressing production of the hormones that cause it to grow, putting her body into medically induced menopause.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 The hormone suppression therapy is brutal. And it gave me next-level debilitating exhaustion. I was just in bed all day long, all day long. My quality of life was so minimal, and I wasn't able to be there for my baby.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did he notice a change?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, yeah. I mean, whenever, whenever Malcolm would come into the home, he'd run straight to my bed because that's where he knows I am. Like that's what he associated with me, and that was just too difficult for me to take. I had to find out if there was another option. So, I opted to do the hysterectomy with the ovariectomy. And almost immediately after that, my energy just came back full force.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Soon, Munn says her doctor wants her to start another drug that will stop her body from producing the cancer-growing hormones elsewhere in the body.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I have been so aggressive. That is, you know, I did everything they told me to do. I did all the big surgeries. And now, I'm saying, do I have to do this extra drug?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) After all the steps you've taken, why do you think that was the one thing you questioned?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 It's just, it's so tiring. I just didn't, I, it's so, these drugs are so tiring. And I know that I'm going to stay aggressive. I know I'm going to do it. I'm just surprised that I'm even asking for anything less than aggressive because, I mean, as you know, it just feels nonstop.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It feels nonstop.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Because it is nonstop.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And going through all of this, have you learned anything new about yourself?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I've learned that I'm a lot braver than I thought I was. And I learned that the most important thing to me in life is my family. Everything else can go away. I don't have my career, I don't have my body the way that it looked before. But as long as the people that I love and care about are here and healthy and thriving, nothing else matters.\par \par \uc2 MALCOLM MULANEY (OLIVIA MUNN'S SON)\par \par \uc2 Mama.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Mama.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Olivia is amazing. She is a fighter. And she said she hopes that sharing her story will help other women will feel empowered to ask their doctors about having a risk assessment done. Olivia's doctors told her that she uses it on all of her patients because genetic screening don't fully capture a woman's risk of getting breast cancer. The score takes into account factors like weight, family history and the age you had your first child. And, of course, you always want to make sure you go over your results with a health care provider, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That message from her is definitely going to help countless people. And, you know first-hand, it's not easy to share and be as open as she has been. But she's gotten support. And she talked to you about that role has played?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She's gotten so much support. And it goes to show how important support is because she was fighting this battle alone, like not alone, but privately with her family. But since sharing her story, she said the support from the public, it puts a smile on her face. And she gave me something that was so inspirational. She told me that the whole experience, it has made her be kinder to herself. She said, all the things I regretted, all the other, I let it go. And I'm just kinder to myself. And she's taking everything, you know, day, minute, second at a time just enjoying life.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for sharing your conversation with her.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, thanks to Olivia for sharing it with me and everyone else.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And everyone can see it on "Nightline" tonight as well?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Yes, they can.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Great. Coming up next, how this family got away after coming within feet of a cougar in their backyard.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:43, COUGAR ENCOUNTER\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240606ek5g0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FIGHT OF HER LIFE ACTOR OLIVIA MUNN OPENS UP ABOUT BATTLE W/RARE AGGRESSIVE BREAST CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 1,936 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 MUNN, BREAST CANCER, LUMINAL B, ALIABADI, MULANEY, SON\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening, thank you for joining us. Tonight, actress Olivia Munn opens up about her harrowing fight against an aggressive form of breast cancer, which despite having been cleared through several common medical tests, she discovered only after her doctor took another more obscure screening for her. A move that might have saved her life. Here's ABC's Michael Strahan.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 It was a sunny day in California. I had gone to my doctor to actually get a blood test that day earlier and then I get a call to come back over. I had already had two mammograms. I'd had ultrasounds. I'd done genetic testing.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what were the results of those?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Clear. Then my doctor said, "There is this lifetime risk assessment test and I took it for you and you're at 37.3 percent," which puts me into the high risk. And then, she said, "I want you to go get an MRI." I went to go get the MRI and that's when they said, "Well, we found something."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you heard the word "cancer," what went through your mind?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I mean, honestly, I just thought of my baby. Cancer takes down a lot of people and I was just over, was overwhelmed with thinking about my baby but at the same time I just had to be so clearheaded, so that I could go off and, and fight this battle.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Actress Olivia Munn is opening up about her fight against Luminal B breast cancer, a fast growing aggressive type of cancer she was diagnosed with in April of last year.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 It's a more rare cancer that only happens to a small percentage of people who have cancer.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what did they explain to you about your prognosis?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 They said I had to be extremely aggressive, that if I was extremely aggressive, that I could fight this and win but at the same time, once they started finding all these little spots in my breast, like, "Oh, there's another tumor, there's another tumor," there was just, there was just so much and in both breasts, that made it all so much more scary. There was such an urgency to it because we had to get in and make some really big decisions.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Within 30 days of your diagnosis, you had the double mastectomy. How are you able to process everything when it's all moving so fast?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I don't think I really processed it.\par \par \uc2 PHOTOGRAPHER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Olivia, this way, please.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For more than 15 years, Olivia has lived her life in the spotlight.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: "THE DAILY SHOW"\par \par \uc2 JON STEWART ("THE DAILY SHOW")\par \par \uc2 For more we go now to Olivia Munn, she's live in the northern desert.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Rising to fame on \uc2 Comedy Central\uc2 's "The Daily Show," filing satirical reports for host Jon Stewart.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: "THE DAILY SHOW\par \par \uc2 JON STEWART ("THE DAILY SHOW")\par \par \uc2 This is an incredible story, Olivia, of survival.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, you are not kidding. I mean, primitive condition, tight quarters, no minibar, limited WiFi at best.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Starring in shows like \uc2 HBO\uc2 's "The Newsroom" as the ambitious financial analyst and anchor Sloan Sabbith.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: "THE NEWSROOM"\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 You know how there are tall women that don't mind dating shorter guys? I don't mind that you're dumb and, Don, I mean that.\par \par \uc2 THOMAS SADOSKI ("THE NEWSROOM")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in films like "X-Men: Apocalypse." In 2021, the star also became a mother, giving birth to son Malcolm who she shares with her Emmy winning comedian partner, John Mulaney. In March, Olivia decided to reveal her diagnosis on social media...\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: INSTAGRAM/@OLIVIAMUNN\par \par \uc2 DR. THAIS ALIABADI (OLIVIA'S OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Do it for him, do it for your baby.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...including the raw moment just before she went to surgery to remove both of her breasts.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: INSTAGRAM/@OLIVIAMUNN\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm ready.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the video you said, "I'm ready." How did you know you were ready?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I didn't. I just had to say it. You know, sometimes you just, you just say it and hope that your body will go with it. I may not want to be in that situation. I may not know what's on the other side, but I've been given this opportunity to fight and so here we go, but after my double mastectomy, they found a tangerine section size of more cancer in my breast. So, one, that's scary because you think, how, what else is in my body?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Following her surgery, Olivia soon started hormone suppression treatment to combat her form of cancer, but the medication took a toll.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 It gave me next-level debilitating exhaustion. I was just in bed all day long, all day long. My quality of life was so minimal and I wasn't able to be there for my baby.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did he notice a change?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Whenever Malcolm would come into the home he'd run straight to my bed because that's where he knows I am. You know, if you ask him, you know, "Where does Mommy work?" He says, "The bed." That's what he associated with me and that was just too difficult for me to take.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She sought help from Dr. Thais Aliabadi, her ob/gyn who initially performed the risk assessment that helped lead to her cancer diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 DR. THAIS ALIABADI (OLIVIA'S OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 So, in Olivia's case they started on her on Lupron medication and Lupron lowers our body's estrogen. By doing that, it gives us a lot of symptoms of menopause from hot flashes to mood changes to vaginal dryness to fatigue. One day she came to my office, and she said, "I feel so sick on these medications and I'd rather take my ovaries out than be on Lupron," and that's exactly what we did.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I opted to do the hysterectomy with the ovariectomy. It's a big decision because it takes out my ovaries.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Even though it's removing another organ it also took away my chance of having cancer in any of those areas.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Olivia completed the surgery last month.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Almost immediately after that my energy just came back full force. So, I have so much energy today. These things are being taken away and you don't really think about that. At least for me, I wasn't thinking about that at all while I'm going through it because it's just, I'm, I'm fighting, I'm fighting.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why did you want to document this journey that you're on right now?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Because if I didn't make it, I wanted my son, when he got older, to know that I fought to be here, that I tried my best.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're gonna make me cry.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 You want the people in your life. You want the people that maybe don't understand what's going on right now to know that, like, you did everything you could to be here.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Olivia hasn't had to navigate her journey alone. John is steady her side.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, how has it been having John there to support you?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 He's honestly just the best human being. He comes to everything in life with so much compassion and understanding. But the one problem is that after I have surgery, especially like a hysterectomy/ovariectomy, he makes me laugh so much that I'm, like, you have, there's times I'm, like, "You have to leave the room. This is insane."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, that's what happens when you're with a funny man.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I know.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, like, he's a funny guy.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I know. And he's the best daddy. He is the best daddy.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And another very personal thing, and I know you, you harvested eggs.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Yes, John and I had a long talk about it. We realized that we weren't done growing our family, so right after the double mastectomy, I went through a round of egg retrieval. We really just hope that it works out for us to be able to have another baby. We just want one more. I'm not gonna ask for too much more in this life, I promise. I just want, just want one more baby.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While Olivia's doctors say her surgery has significantly reduced the risk of her cancer progressing, her oncologist wants to start her on a new medication to stop cancer growing hormones elsewhere in her body.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I have been so aggressive. You know, I did everything they told me to do. I did all the big surgeries. And now I'm saying, do I have to do this extra drug? It's just, it's so tiring. I just am, I, it's so - these drugs are so tiring and I know that I'm gonna stay aggressive. I know I'm going to do it. Just, it's not, just feels nonstop.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It feels nonstop.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Because it is nonstop.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How do you hope sharing your journey, your story is gonna help others out there?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Well, I, I really hope that this empowers women to find out their lifetime risk assessment score and I really hope that it lets doctors know that, hey, we all know about this test, please take it seriously.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Going through all of this, have you learned anything new about yourself?\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I've learned that I'm a lot braver than I thought I was. I learned that the most important thing to me in life is my family. Everything else can go away. I don't have my career. I don't have my body the way that I looked before. But as long as the people that I love and care about are here and healthy and thriving, nothing else matters.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: INSTAGRAM/@OLIVIAMUNN\par \par \uc2 MALCOM (OLIVIA'S SON)\par \par \uc2 Mama.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Mama.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Michael.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  ON BROADWAY\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we return, \uc2 Disney\uc2 's live productions now mesmerizing audiences for 30 years around the world.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020240520ek5g00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POLITICAL HEADLINES CAMPUS CRACKDOWNS EXPAND NATIONWIDE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,353 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CATASTROPHIC FLOODING\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, STORMS, RIVER, FLOODING, TORNADOES, HAIL, RESIDENTS, HOMES, LAMBERT\par \par \uc2 CAMPUS, PALESTINE, PROTESTERS, \uc2 NYPD\uc2 , DAUGHTRY, VALDEZ, SHAFIK, COMMENCEMENT\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, HOSTAGE, CEASE-FIRE, DEAL, BURNS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, TESTIMONY, HICKS, DANIELS, COHEN, TAPE, "ACCESS HOLLYWOOD"\par \par \uc2 CONGRESS, CUELLAR, BRIBES, BANK, TEXTS, "EL JEFE"\par \par \uc2 SENTENCING, HAGERICH, TOURIST, AMMUNITION, LUGGAGE, AIRPORT, ISLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENTENCING HEARING FOR US TOURIST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWYERS ASKING FOR LIGHTER SENTENCE, FACING POSSIBLE 12 YEARS FOR AMMUNITION IN LUGGAGE\par \par \uc2 TEENS, BOAT, VIDEO, TRASH, ATLANTIC, OCEAN, FWC, FELONY\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, WINDS, HAIL, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 ANDREWS, CLARK, WNBA, \uc2 NBA\uc2 , CLIPPERS, MAVERICKS, MAGIC, CAVALIERS, \uc2 NUGGETS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP FROM \uc2 WALT DISNEY\uc2  STUDIES, "UP"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 DISNEY\uc2  IS THE PARENT COMPANY OF ABC NEWS\par \par \uc2 CAMPUS, PROTESTS, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , IPSOS, VOTERS, BIDEN, ABORTION, TRUMP, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're gonna start this half hour here with a closer look at the top political headlines this week. So much going on. Joining us are ABC News Deputy Political Director Averi Harper and contributing Political Correspondent Rachael Bade. (inaudible) Bade, sorry about that. Welcome to you both. So good it see you.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. Morning.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Averi, let's start with you because, obviously, we've seen all the protests happening this week. The Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  War very, very much in focus here. But you have some new insight into how Americans are feeling as a whole.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOU VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAMPUS CRACKDOWNS EXPAND NATIONWIDE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S MESSAGE AS LAW ENFORCEMENT DEPLOYED ON MULTIPLE CAMPUSES\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, we did ask about the Israel-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  War in our latest ABC News/\uc2 Ipsos\uc2  poll, and what we found is that four in ten Americans say that the US is doing too much to support Israel. That's actually up from our last poll in January and, of course, we saw the President address those college protests that we saw across the country. He says that violent protest is not protected, but peaceful protest is. He also said that none of these protests are leading him to reconsider his stance on the issue and so we've been talking a lot about any political implications that there could be for the President in November.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US IS DOING TOO MUCH TO SUPPORT ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 31% JANUARY, 38% NOW\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our poll also found out that less than half of Americans say that the war between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  is actually going to factor into their decision come election time, and only 12 percent of voters say that it's going to be one of the single most important issues as they decide who to vote for.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL-\uc2 HAMAS\uc2  WAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 48% IMPORTANT ELECTION ISSUE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's a really surprising number, only 12 percent.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It really is. It's an important one but not the most important for so many Americans. And, Rachael, what about the response to the protest from lawmakers on Capitol Hill? Because Democrats, they absolutely appear to be divided on this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAMPUS PROTESTS CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWMAKERS APPEAR DIVIDED AS DEMONSTRATIONS EXPAND\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's right. I mean, there was a vote in the House this week to expand the definition of anti-Semitism and discrimination cases. A lot of people thought this was going to be a broadly bipartisan vote. Instead, my Democratic sources on the Hill were shocked to see 70 House Democrats oppose this legislation because they're concerned about it infringing on free speech or criticism of Israel and how they're handling the Gaza situation on these college campuses.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the interesting thing is I'm hearing from Republicans that they believe this sort of feeds right into their hands, right. Speaker \uc2 Mike Johnson\uc2  has been relentless in attacking President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , saying he's not doing enough to protect Jewish students. He was at Columbia just a few days ago calling for the President to resign. He put up this vote this week to try to split Democratic Caucus. And this is just the beginning, right?\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're gonna have this long, summer-long investigation into how it's been handled on - college campuses. They're going to be putting up a bunch of votes that are once again gonna split Democrats between their support of Israel and what they're hearing from the base and their, their support and concern for the Palestinian people, so it's gonna be a tough position for them.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and Averi, let's, let's talk about another major topic in the headlines this week, of course, abortion. There were big developments in Florida and Arizona and recent comments from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  getting a lot of attention as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIGHT OVER REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA GOVERNOR SIGNS BILL TO REPEAL 1864 BAN, SIX-WEEK BAN TAKES EFFECT IN FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, lots of news on the abortion front. In Arizona, we saw state lawmakers there, a vote to repeal that 1864 near total abortion ban that did not have exceptions for rape or incest. The same day, we saw in Florida the six-week abortion ban go into effect. That's before many women even know that they're even pregnant. And we could see abortion on the ballot on both states come November. We also saw former President Trump.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He did an interview with "Time" Magazine, in which he said and suggested that he would allow for states to monitor women's pregnancies and to prosecute women and people who violate those state abortion bans. Of course, the Biden campaign has seized on these comments. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  dubbing Trump the architect of the health care crisis.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  & VEEP SWEEPSTAKES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOOKING AT POSSIBLE RUNNING MATES, WHO COULD BE THE FRONT RUNNERS?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and let's stay on Trump right now, Ra - Rachael, because we're, we're looking at him hosting these events in Palm Beach. We're taking about 400 donors, high-profile politicians but also possible running mates. So, do we have any frontrunners right now?\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, everybody wants to know who is \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gonna choose as his running mate, but I can tell you that there's a reason he has a vast short list with a lot of people on it and he's gonna wait as long as he can to pick someone. And it's because of weekends like this. He needs campaign money and he's bringing these guys down to Florida to say, look, you want to be my running mate, let's see how much money you can raise for me, so he's gonna be bringing in the cash that way. I think, one of the interesting thing is that, is actually who is not in attendance, \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , the South Carolina, South Dakota governor.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She was actually considered a top frontrunner for this job and she was actually invited to this event but then there was all this blowback when news came out that she brags in a new book that she shot her own dog. We reported yesterday that in the book she claimed to have met with the leader of North, I'm sorry, North Korea, and it turns out she actually didn't. So, the Trump people are trying to make distance with her right now. She is no longer on the short list.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, a lot of questions coming out for that book.\par \par \uc2 RACHAEL BADE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Rachael, as always, we appreciate it. Averi Harper, too, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240528ek540000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HALLE BERRY ON CAPITOL HILL OSCAR WINNER AIMS TO BRING ATTENTION TO & DESTIGMATIZE MENOPAUSE\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADO TOUCHDOWN\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO, RAIN, FLOODING, DAMAGE, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, WINDS, HAIL, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TESTIMONY, DANIELS, COHEN\par \par \uc2 I-95, FIRE, CRASH, TRAFFIC, SHUTDOWN, SHAY, EUCALITTO\par \par \uc2 COLLEGES, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, JEWISH\par \par \uc2 POLL, WAR, GAZA, ISRAEL, UNITED STATES\par \par \uc2 BERRY, MENOPAUSE, SENATORS, CAPITOL, DESTIGMATIZE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, George. Now to Halle Barry on Capitol Hill. The Oscar winner is hoping to put the spotlight on menopause. Eva Pilgrim is here with more. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALLE BERRY ON CAPITOL HILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OSCAR WINNER AIMS TO BRING ATTENTION TO & DESTIGMATIZE MENOPAUSE\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Halle Barry shouting about menopause on the steps of the Capitol. The actress in DC trying to drum up support and bring attention to a bill that would fund research and education on menopause. Now the legislation introduced by a bipartisan group of female senators.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Berry sharing her own story, struggling to deal with the hormonal shift going through perimenopause, saying this female rite of passage needs to be destigmatized and better understood.\par \par \uc2 HALLE BERRY (OSCAR WINNING ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I'm in menopause. Okay. The shame has to be taken out of menopause. We have to talk about this very normal part of our life that happens. Our doctors can't even say the word to us, let alone walk us through the journey of what our menopausal years look like or our years after that.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So how much money are we talking about for this bill? $275 million. Those dollars would go to clinical trials on menopause as well as a hormone therapy to deal with the symptoms. Will this happen? Yes, they have bipartisan support. But these female senators will need their male colleagues to sign on if they have any hope of getting it passed, Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And hopefully, they get that right, guys?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, hopefully, they do. Eva, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What else are we going to say?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240523ek5300030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION BATTLE STANDS BY SUPPORT FOR LETTING STATES MAKE THEIR OWN DECISIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, COLLEGES, ARRESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAMPUS TENSIONS BOILING OVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE PROTESTS & ARRESTS AT COLLEGES ACROSS U.S.\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, CEASE-FIRE, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CEASE-FIRE TALKS HIT NEW HURDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  SAYS IT'S "NEGATIVE" ON ISRAEL'S OFFER, BUT NEGOTIATIONS COULD CONTINUE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TORNADOES, FLASH FLOOD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TORNADO THREAT FOR THE HEARTLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER TARGETING AREAS STILL RECOVERING FROM OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP REFUSES TO COMMIT TO ACCEPTING 2024 ELECTION RESULTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT: "IF EVERYTHING'S HONEST, I'LL GLADLY ACCEPT THE RESULTS"\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CRIMINAL TRIAL RESUMING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT ACCUSED OF VIOLATING GAG ORDER AGAIN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS, TIEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STANDS BY SUPPORT FOR LETTING STATES MAKE THEIR OWN DECISIONS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  also weighed in on the battle over abortion and defending his support of state-based restrictions, as Florida's six-week ban takes effect and Arizona lawmakers vote to repeal their strict Civil War-era ban. Rachel Scott is in Detroit this morning with the latest. Rachel, good morning.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Whit, good morning. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been focused on his criminal trial. It's the first time that we've seen him out on the campaign trail in weeks. He's really tried to put this issue of abortion to rest. But Democrats not only seizing on his recent comments, but also his record, appointing three of the five Supreme Court justices that overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For the first time since his criminal trial began, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  returned to the campaign trail, forced to defend his record on an issue that could define this election. Abortion.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I always say, it's up to the states. They'll ask me a question about it. I say that's up to the state. So, I say to you, I think we did a very good job and that a lot of people are very happy with it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump standing by his comments that he won't object if states monitor pregnant women to make sure they comply with abortion bans or prosecute women who violate them. The former president often brags about appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade, clearing the way for 21 states to severely restrict access to abortion. But now, sensing police call vulnerability, Trump is warning Republicans not to go too far.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You have to have what your heart determines and you have to fight for what's in your heart and what's the right thing to do. But remember, you also have to get elected.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both the Trump and Biden campaigns are well aware abortion rights has won in every state where it has appeared on the ballot. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  visiting Florida just hours after the state enacted a six-week ban, placing the blame on Trump.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 As of this morning, 4 million women in this state woke up with fewer reproductive freedoms than they had last night. This is the new reality under a Trump abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Virtually every state in the south has now banned or restricted abortion. Dr. Shelley Tian telling our Selina Wang it will have a devastating impact.\par \par \uc2 DR SHELLY TIEN (PLANNED PARENTHOOD OF SOUTH EAST & NORTH-FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 To not be able to provide that care that we are trained to provide for patients is really, really, it's terrible. It's horrible.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, some states are reversing course under growing public pressure. Arizona lawmakers, including two Republican state senators, voting to repeal an 1864 near-total abortion ban, passed a half century before women had the right to vote.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion rights could be on the ballot in as many as 13 states this November, including right there in Arizona and Florida, where voters could ultimately have the final say either way, Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Certainly will be one that we are watching. Rachel, thanks for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek520002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MENOPAUSE & DEPRESSION STUDY: PERIMENOPAUSAL WOMEN HAVE 40% HIGHER RISK\b0\par\par\uc2 672 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, COLLEGES, ARRESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAMPUS TENSIONS BOILING OVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE PROTESTS & ARRESTS AT COLLEGES ACROSS U.S.\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, CEASE-FIRE, NEGOTIATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CEASE-FIRE TALKS HIT NEW HURDLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  SAYS IT'S "NEGATIVE" ON ISRAEL'S OFFER, BUT NEGOTIATIONS COULD CONTINUE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TORNADOES, FLASH FLOOD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TORNADO THREAT FOR THE HEARTLAND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER TARGETING AREAS STILL RECOVERING FROM OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP REFUSES TO COMMIT TO ACCEPTING 2024 ELECTION RESULTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT: "IF EVERYTHING'S HONEST, I'LL GLADLY ACCEPT THE RESULTS"\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP CRIMINAL TRIAL RESUMING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT ACCUSED OF VIOLATING GAG ORDER AGAIN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS, TIEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP WEIGHS IN ON ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STANDS BY SUPPORT FOR LETTING STATES MAKE THEIR OWN DECISIONS\par \par \uc2 SCHOOL SHOOTING, MCCARTHY, KAUL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE SCHOOL SHOOTING THWARTED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE TAKE DOWN 14-YEAR-OLD ALLEGED GUNMAN OUTSIDE WISCONSIN MIDDLE SCHOOL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR PROTEST CLASH AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE POLICE PRESENCE MOVES IN ON CAMPUS DEMONSTRATORS\par \par \uc2 READ, TRIAL, LALLY, YANNETTI, JACKSON, SARAF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUILTY OR FRAMED?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSACHUSETTS WOMAN ACCUSED OF KILLING BOYFRIEND CLAIMS COVER UP\par \par \uc2 GRATUITIES, O'BRIEN, VIRAL VIDEO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIPPING POINT?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIRAL POST RAISES QUESTIONS ABOUT GRATUITIES\par \par \uc2 "BABY REINDEER", GARDNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIT SHOW "BABY REINDEER" SPARKS FIRESTORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FANS TRYING TO EXPOSE REAL-LIFE PEOPLE WHO INSPIRED CHARACTERS\par \par \uc2 NBA PLAYOFFS, RUTLEDGE, JONES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS, 8:20\par \par \uc2 PROTEST, CLASH, UCLA, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR PROTEST CLASH AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE POLICE PRESENCE MOVES IN ON DEMONSTRATORS\par \par \uc2 MENOPAUSE, DEPRESSION, RISK, STUDY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MENOPAUSE & DEPRESSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: PERIMENOPAUSAL WOMEN HAVE 40% HIGHER RISK\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do turn now to two new headlines about menopause, including new research that finds women approaching menopause may be at higher risk for depression. Rhiannon Ally is here with details on that. Good morning, Rhiannon.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Janai. The study in "The Journal of Affective Disorders" looked at depression and found women in midlife who were approaching the average age when perimenopause starts, around their 40s, were at a 40 percent greater risk of depression or having depressive symptoms, compared to premenopausal women. It also found depressive symptoms were twice as common in men, women, rather, versus men.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the good news is that researchers found no associated risk of depression in women after menopause. Experts say if you are feeling signs of depression, like persistent sadness, anxiety or fatigue, you should see your healthcare provider for a complete evaluation. They suggest lifestyle changes, like exercise, consuming less caffeine and sugar, getting better sleep and quitting smoking. All of those have been found to help with depression, Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it's important, those little things that can make a big difference. And there's another menopause-related study, Rhiannon, this one about hormone replacement therapy. Tell us about that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MENOPAUSE & HORMONE THERAPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPERTS NOW SAY IT CAN BE SAFE FORM OF TREATMENT\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm glad you asked because this one might be some good news. Research published in "JAMA" took another look at findings that were published 20 years ago that suggested an increased risk of cancer, stroke and heart attack with hormone therapy. Now, these findings swayed some women and even some doctors away from using hormone therapy. But now this new study found that that reaction may have been overblown. So, experts now say hormone therapy can be safe to treat hot flashes, trouble sleeping and other symptoms that come with menopause for women under the age of 60, giving many renewed hope for relief. And we know women have so much to deal with. Hopefully, this can help some of them, guys.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Certainly good to be talking about this and getting it out there.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek520003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 603 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MORE IMPACTING CHOICES\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, PRINCESS KATE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, MAMMOGRAM, GUIDANCE, 40, ARCILA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 VERGARA, BEYONCE, SHABOOZEY, PANERA\par \par \uc2 KNIVES, CONDIMENTS, BRAS, COOKWARE, COFFEE, SKINCARE\par \par \uc2 ICELAND, TRAVEL, BUDGET, ROSEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPERIENCE ICELAND!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL THE WAYS TO SAVE ON YOUR TRIP\par \par \uc2 POLITICS, CULTURE, AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRIDGING THE AMERICAN DIVIDE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE EXCHANGE PROGRAM CONNECTING STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go back to Ginger in Boston.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, hey, George. Yes, we are celebrating here, Boston, the town that I'm getting a little time in, with chief meteorologist Cindy Fitzgibbon here, from WCVB. You know, we're both meteorologists, so we know a lot about weather, but I'm not exactly the sports aficionado. So, you've been schooling me. Let's go, let's go through. Catch me up on what's happening.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL FORECAST\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 We need to win this game.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Celtics.\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 If we do, we're moving on.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, \uc2 Bruins\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 Well, last night wasn't so great, but we're hoping for a win the next go-around, yes.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And finally, the \uc2 Red Sox\uc2  play tonight.\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 Yes they do. And unfortunately, weather-wise, what you see is what you get. It's not going to warm up too much. But forecast for the game looking okay. I mean, it's not going to rain, but it's just not going to be that warm. So, you want to make sure you're dressed for it. Temperatures either side of 50 over the course of the game.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At least it's not windy.\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 At least it's not windy. And I have a gift for you, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Boston bringing gifts.\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 I know that your no new clothes\u160\'00\'A0pledge, so, rather than getting you a new shirt, I am gifting you my \uc2 Bruins\uc2  shirt, and I'm hoping it's going to bring us luck.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is huge. I am going to wear it, and we are going to do our best with that because no new clothes continues on. Thank you very much. That was so thoughtful.\par \par \uc2 CINDY FITZGIBBON (WCVB)\par \par \uc2 You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is my kind of gift. All right, let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "GMA" is boosting your business. It's a special event featuring some of the most exciting companies all in Atlanta. We'll have the story coming up on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MO