oking for some dishes. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COPPER COW COFFEE\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Can't beat that. Okay, how bad are you looking for the best cup of coffee anywhere? Because if so, we've got, Debbie's (PH) got it for you from Copper Cow Coffee, inspired by both your mom's love of Vietnamese coffee and your dad's love of the pour-over.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE (COPPER COW COFFEE)\par \par \uc2 Yes, so, we make it easy for you to have a beautiful cup of coffee for anybody. And we do so by brewing actual herbs and spices into the coffee, like our churro coffee, that has whole-ground cinnamon in it, no artificial flavors. And it even comes in our single serve pour-overs.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So that you can take this literally anywhere, travel, from your desk to your plane.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm getting on a plane today. You've got to give me a few. This is delicious. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got it. These start at $8.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then finally today, we've got (inaudible) Tinted, the, to me, some of the best skincare around.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE (TINTED)\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Do you wear SPF?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE (TINTED)\par \par \uc2 You absolutely should be. This one goes on completely invisible. It makes it so easy to use on the go, anywhere you're at.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, check that out.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That will be packed in your bag.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE (TINTED)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This concealer is on both of our faces right now.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE (TINTED)\par \par \uc2 It's amazing because it's packed with skincare, and it makes it so your dark circles go away over time.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amazing products.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Starts at $11.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Use that QR code. We'll be right back here. Stick around.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\b0\par\par\uc2 962 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MORE IMPACTING CHOICES\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, PRINCESS KATE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, MAMMOGRAM, GUIDANCE, 40, ARCILA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And welcome back to "GMA." Tomorrow, Brooke Shields is going to be here live. She's talking about her new movie. And Rebecca, welcome. You're here with more on the new breast cancer screening guidelines.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So important, George. Guys, the "GMA" Cover Story now on breast cancer screening. The \uc2 United States Preventive Services Task Force\uc2  finalizing their recommendation that all women should begin receiving them by the time they hit 40.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning the \uc2 US Preventive Services Task Force\uc2  announcing their final recommendation on screening for breast cancer, suggesting all women with average risk begin screening with mammograms at the age of 40 and continue every other year until the age 74.\par \par \uc2 DR. WANDA NICHOLSON (THE US PREVENTIVE SERVICES TASK FORCE)\par \par \uc2 The latest science clearly shows that by screening every other year beginning at age 40, that we can save even more lives, in fact up to nearly 20 percent more lives can be saved from breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Prior recommendations from the task force said women should start screening no later than age 50, but more women are being diagnosed with breast cancer at younger ages.\par \par \uc2 DR. WANDA NICHOLSON (THE US PREVENTIVE SERVICES TASK FORCE)\par \par \uc2 The national data showed that from, since, from 2015 to 2019, there was an increase in breast cancer diagnoses in women ages 40 to 49. And, in fact, it increased about two percent every year.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Olga Arcila said a mammogram at 45 saved her life.\par \par \uc2 OLGA ARCILA (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 They told me that I have breast cancer. I couldn't believe it. I am a very healthy person, very active, very positive.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Following a double mastectomy and 16 rounds of chemotherapy, she's now helping her Latin community stay informed about the importance of mammograms.\par \par \uc2 OLGA ARCILA (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Very important to start at the of 40. But if the cancer is in your family, you have to do it every year.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So important. So, we want to bring back ABC News chief medical correspondent Dr. Jennifer Ashton to break this down. I'm so glad you're here, 240,000 women a year are getting breast cancer. This is so important.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's very important. And these headlines and these recommendations are always confusing and controversial because not every professional organization agrees. Part of the motivation with them changing from 50 to 40 is because we've been watching rates of breast cancer, particularly in younger women, 40 to 49, go up, go up about two percent every single year, and those women tend to have more aggressive types of breast cancer. So, you know, for the historical context, it's important to remember that back in 2009, this very same group, the US Preventive Service Task Force, changed the age and made it 50.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, over that last period of time, we've been watching more cases, more aggressive cases, more deaths. That was the concern then. That's why people today are applauding this, this change. But there are still those people, and I am one of them medically, who thinks that screening a woman every two years is not the proper interval, so we haven't heard the end of it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW LOWERING THE RECOMMENDED AGE WILL HELP SAVE MORE LIVES\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, and the recommendation is now also different from the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 's, and as a patient, this is so confusing.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, it's confusing, and also remember these recommendations pertain to women at average risk. The majority of women diagnosed with breast cancer were average until the day they get that diagnosis. So, also remember that mammography is the gold standard. It is not perfect. It misses some breast cancers, particularly in young women with dense breasts, so ultrasound is often used, MRI is recommended for women at high risk.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But the bottom line is you want to talk to your healthcare provider, and particularly women who are Black or who are afraid of getting screened or who don't have the same access, this will hopefully save lives.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I talked to my doctor. My mom is a breast cancer survivor. I did my first mammogram at 38, as a result, after that conversation.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's usually 10 years younger than your first degree relative was diagnosed.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dr. Jen Ashton, as always, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MORE IMPACTING CHOICES\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, PRINCESS KATE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, MAMMOGRAM, GUIDANCE, 40, ARCILA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 VERGARA, BEYONCE, SHABOOZEY, PANERA\par \par \uc2 KNIVES, CONDIMENTS, BRAS, COOKWARE, COFFEE, SKINCARE\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA," live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 May is Asian American and Native Hawaiian Pacific Islanders Heritage Month. We're going to be celebrating all month long. And this morning, you see them right there, we are joined by Lei Pasifika. They were founded in 2007. The group shares the music and dance of the Pacific Islands with classes and performances that celebrate the culture of Tahiti and Hawaii.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEI PASIFIKA\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's so beautiful.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 They are so talented.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POP NEWS\b0\par\par\uc2 951 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MORE IMPACTING CHOICES\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, PRINCESS KATE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, MAMMOGRAM, GUIDANCE, 40, ARCILA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 VERGARA, BEYONCE, SHABOOZEY, PANERA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...filled "Pop News."\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do. We do. That's the tease, everybody. We're going to begin first, though, with a very big exclusive from "People" magazine and their annual beautiful issue. We have the honor of revealing their cover choice. You guys ready?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go. Let's see.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh yes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOFIA VERGARA COVERS PEOPLE'S "THE BEAUTIFUL ISSUE"\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is our friend, Sofia Vergara, gracing the cover of the annual issue, and in a revealing article inside the magazine, she explains what makes her feel beautiful at the age of 51 years young. She also shares the reason for her divorce from actor Joe Manganello after seven years. She says it was not wanting to have more kids. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 SOFIA VERGARA (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I was a mother already. I know what it means to be a good mother or to try to be the best mother that you can, and that takes a lot of sacrifices. It takes a lot of energy. I didn't think, because of my career, the way I live my life and the way my marriage was, that it was fair to bring a kid to this world.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Vergara has been photographed lately with Dr. Justin Saliman for the past few months. She will not confirm her dating status. She does admit to one new love in her life, though, a Chihuahua puppy named Amore. There is little Amore with her on the cover of "People's" "The Beautiful Issue." That's available on newsstands nationwide Friday, and you can see more at people.com. What a great choice.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Beautiful inside and out.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) One hundred percent. And on a roll with "Griselda," as well, really. Love it.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, yeah, people are obsessed with that show.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEYONCE & SHABOOZEY MAKE BILLBOARD COUNTRY CHART HISTORY\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're going to move on right now to music news. Queen Bey has spent 10 weeks on top of the "Billboard's" Hot Country Song Chart with her smash hit, "Texas Hold Em." I mean, it is a great song. And this morning, she has been dethroned by this song.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's Shaboozey and his number one hit, "A Bar Song (Tipsy)." It marks the first time that two Black artists have topped the Hot Country Chart back to back in the history of the charts. And these two are pals. Shaboozey actually appears on two tracks on Beyonce's recent album, "Cowboy Carter," the song "Spaghetti" and also "Sweet Honey Buckin'." He was, according to the artist, that experienced a Beyonce boost, if you will, after she entered her country era, getting a streaming bump from first-time listeners. Shaboozey telling "Billboard" magazine he's so happy to have such a powerhouse artist choose country. Shaboozey's own album, "Where I've Been isn't Where I'm Going," that will be out on May 31st. Take a listen. He's so talented.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PANERA BREAD BOWL HAT IS A HOT COMMODITY\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then finally, George, thank you for teasing that special something, here it is, something to satisfy the appetites of all the fashionistas and carb lovers out there. It's a new accessory courtesy of an unlikely source, Panera bread, but it's true, the chain revealing their bread head hat. Thank goodness it's here just in time for the Kentucky Derby. Panera teamed up with (inaudible) studio for the already-sold-out creation. It was listed at 21 bucks on the Panera website. It came with a gift card. We couldn't get one. But since we have the best props department in the business, Billy, bring it on out, they made one. They made a dupe for us. Look at this beauty.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is that sourdough?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look at that gorgeous gem. There you go. There you go. Anybody who doesn't have their hat yet for derby, come on over. One important note, Panera says you cannot use this hat as a bread bowl. Thank you, Panera, for that PSA.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Disclaimer.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For that disclaimer. They also say that while they are currently sold out, they do plan to restock, so check the Panera website tomorrow. You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, thank you. You're going to put that on.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE US TASK FORCE: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That video was something else, Victor, thank you. Now we have a game changer when it comes to screening for breast cancer with newly released guidance. Our chief medical correspondent Dr. Jennifer Ashton is here with the details. So the big guidance here, dropping the age.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: US TASK FORCE: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and of course, sure to get a lot of attention on this. Let me take you through the newest recommendations set forth by the US Preventive Service Task Force. Age is the big one. This is for average risk women, they recommend starting mammogram screening at age 40, to screen every two years until age 74.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very important to note screening for high risk women is different. These recommendations pertain to the average risk woman. That key word, average, is the issue because majority of women are, in fact, considered average until the day they get their diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there's a reason why this is the right time.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. In order to appreciate that you need some historical perspective. Back in 2009, the US Preventive Service Task Force made big news with a lot of controversy because they dialed the age up from 40 to 50. Now they're seeing an increase in breast cancer rates, particularly in women in their 40s.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So that's part of the reason they're moving that age back down to 40. But oncologists, radiologists, OB/GYNs, still kind of weighing in on the issue of every two years and is that frequency too spaced out. So we haven't heard the end of the controversy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is in your wheel house once again. I know there is so much more to discuss on this. So we're gonna bring you back 8:00 hour.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) See you again in the 8:00 hour.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, thank you. Because there's some conflicting things here.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Correct.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, Jen.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRINCE WILLIAM ON KATE'S HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROYAL: WIFE & CHILDREN "ARE ALL DOING WELL"\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such important information. And coming up here, for the first time Prince William is opening up about how his wife, Princess Kate, is doing after her cancer diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ALERT ABOUT "GRANDPARENT SCAMS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ CHARGES 16 AS FBI WARNS BILLIONS BEING STOLEN FROM SENIORS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, the new alert about grandparent scams. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  warning some seniors are losing their life savings.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRITTNEY GRINER BREAKS HER SILENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WNBA STAR ON HER ARREST & 10 MONTH DETAINMENT IN RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And more from my exclusive interview with Britney Griner. What she says made her feel like less than human. But first, let's go to Ginger. Good morning, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek5100009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BOOSTING YOUR BUSINESS NATIONAL SMALL BUSINESS WEEK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,674 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MORE IMPACTING CHOICES\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, PRINCESS KATE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, MAMMOGRAM, GUIDANCE, 40, ARCILA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 VERGARA, BEYONCE, SHABOOZEY, PANERA\par \par \uc2 KNIVES, CONDIMENTS, BRAS, COOKWARE, COFFEE, SKINCARE\par \par \uc2 ICELAND, TRAVEL, BUDGET, ROSEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPERIENCE ICELAND!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL THE WAYS TO SAVE ON YOUR TRIP\par \par \uc2 POLITICS, CULTURE, AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRIDGING THE AMERICAN DIVIDE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE EXCHANGE PROGRAM CONNECTING STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 SMALL BUSINESS, ENTREPRENEURS, EXPERIENCE ATLANTA\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're celebrating National Small Business Week with our series, "GMA's" Boosting Your Business. And this morning "GMA" lifestyle contributor Lori Bergamotto is in Atlanta at a special event highlighting local entrepreneurs. Hey, good morning, Lori.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Lara, good morning to you. That's right, I'm here at the Experience Atlanta, yes, where small businesses are getting ready for a busy day of showcasing their products. We're going to get to meet some of those talented people in just a moment. This segment is sponsored by... and their CEO, Ben Walter, is giving us an early look at this signature event. Good morning, Ben.\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, Lori. Thank you for being here.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm so excited to be here. Tell us a little bit about what this event is.\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 Today is really a day all about small businesses, all over Atlanta. It's a chance for them to invest, to invest in themselves, we're going to have some thought leadership here today, to invest in their network, they'll meet up to 800 of their colleagues in their community, and really to invest in everything that's going on around their business and promote their businesses. You'll see them here later today, and we might even have a special local star coming later today.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exciting. Are you guys excited? Okay, well, let's get to meet some of those incredible companies and businesses. We're going to start over here, Ben, and we're going to start with a company called Xocolatl. Did I say that correct.\par \par \uc2 ELAINE READ (XOCOLATL)\par \par \uc2 You got it.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, and their co-founder, Elaine Read. Elaine, tell us a little bit about how this company got started.\par \par \uc2 ELAINE READ (XOCOLATL)\par \par \uc2 Well, in 2013, my husband and I quit our jobs, and we packed up our small kids and moved to the jungles of Costa Rice. When we were there, we fell in love with the locally produced dark chocolate, and we knew that if we learned how to make this type of chocolate, Atlanta would love it.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I'm sure Atlanta will love it. Ben, I got to taste the crackle and crunch earlier. It is delicious, and I'm definitely taking this with me.\par \par \uc2 ELAINE READ (XOCOLATL)\par \par \uc2 Awesome.\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 I'm a sucker for salt, for that would be it for me.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ooh, yeah, there's a lot of good sweet and salty. Thank you so much, Elaine.\par \par \uc2 ELAINE READ (XOCOLATL)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, we're going to move here to the Dope Pieces puzzle company, love the name, and their CEO, Kris Hale. Good morning Kris.\par \par \uc2 KRIS HALE (DOPE PIECES)\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, tell us, what is the mission that drives your business?\par \par \uc2 KRIS HALE (DOPE PIECES)\par \par \uc2 Positive representation. We are committed to connecting people, art and culture through the artwork of artists of color who positively represent the Black (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, these puzzles really, truly are artwork. They're amazing.\par \par \uc2 KRIS HALE (DOPE PIECES)\par \par \uc2 They are, thank you.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're welcome.\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 They're beautiful, and they're so intricate.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, definitely. We've got the 500 piece there, but these little guys are just for today, is that right?\par \par \uc2 KRIS HALE (DOPE PIECES)\par \par \uc2 They're just for today, yes. We custom made them for y'all.\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 Might have to take one home.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, definitely. Thank you so much, Kris.\par \par \uc2 KRIS HALE (DOPE PIECES)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, and now we're going to move on to our next company that's more than just skincare. We have owner and entrepreneur Sherri Dindal. Good morning. Tell us a little bit about Wholesome Hippy.\par \par \uc2 SHERRI DINDAL (WHOLESOME HIPPY)\par \par \uc2 Good morning. Well, we're an all-natural, affordable beauty and wellness brand made with high-quality, clean ingredients that give your skin and your piece of mind a little TLC. And we have beauty regimens and wellness products to help with pain and stress and anxiety, and we try to make something for everybody in your family.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I think for pain, stress, anxiety, that's something for everybody, right? We could all...\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 I think we all have a little bit of that.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and I feel like you had me at affordable and high quality. We love that. Thank you so much for being here. Can't wait to check this all out.\par \par \uc2 SHERRI DINDAL (WHOLESOME HIPPY)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. Okay, and next up, this is a company that's dedicated to promoting diversity, something we can all get behind. Leah Hernandez, good morning. She's the creator and CEO of Young Authors Publishing. Leah, tell us a little bit more about everything you have here. There's so much fun stuff to look at.\par \par \uc2 LEAH HERNANDEZ (YOUNG AUTHORS PUBLISHING)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, so, we're a traditional book publisher. And in fact, a lot of the picture books that you see here are actually written by young people. So, we have authors as young as eight, that range all the way to 18, and our mission is to create a platform for diverse authors to share their stories.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that.\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 I mean, I feel so inadequate. I'm a bit older than eight, and I've never written a book.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's hope for you yet. And I'm definitely taking this, "Little Stella." My daughter's name is Stella. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 LEAH HERNANDEZ (YOUNG AUTHORS PUBLISHING)\par \par \uc2 I love that. Of course.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is\u160\'00\'A0great. Well, Ben, everybody here was so great, such inspiring stories, and it's really great to meet some of the founders behind these brands. What do you hope that they get out of working with you?\par \par \uc2 BEN WALTER (CHASE FOR BUSINESS)\par \par \uc2 We hope that they get the best for their business. It's really all about them. You meet people who will start these businesses, they put their entire heart and soul into it, and that's why we're so proud to do this. We'll be doing it later this year in DC and in Philly, and we get to bring the best of these local small businesses communities into the community and share it around. And if you want your kid to get some job, get a job someday, support a small business because that's the company that's going to hire them some day.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's great, and we all want that, right? We all need to support these small businesses and these communities. So, a huge thanks to you, Ben, and to all of our guests here today. For more information on upcoming events, go to our "GMA" \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and \uc2 Instagram\uc2  pages. Guys, thanks so much for having us. Back to you guys, Lara.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Lori. Love supporting all those great small businesses. And we will be right back.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "GMA" Boosting Your Business is sponsored by...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're talking vacations, but it was a busy morning. We were thinking about it because we want to thank our team in Iceland for that Bucket List on a Budget.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we also want to thank all of our fabulous AANHPI small business owners. We have partnered with those companies on those "Deals & Steals," so don't forget to check them out on goodmorningamerica.com.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And it's been so, so great to have Lei Pasifika with us this morning. The group provides workshops and classes that celebrate\u160\'00\'A0the culture...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I am in.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...of all levels. Let's go take a class together, Lara. And these are just some of the students. Have a great day, everyone. Don't worry, Lara and I won't show you our class.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You want George and I dancing?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Do not want to see that. Gorgeous.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Have a great day, guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION SHOWDOWN TAKES CENTER STAGE BIDEN BLAMES TRUMP AS SIX WEEK FLORIDA BAN TAKES EFFECT\b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Aaron Katersky, thanks. The latest now on abortion rights as a six week ban on the procedure takes effect in Florida today. The Biden administration is blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  heading to Florida. Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce has the story. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION SHOWDOWN TAKES CENTER STAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN BLAMES TRUMP AS SIX WEEK FLORIDA BAN TAKES EFFECT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well the Biden campaign is eager to put the issue of abortion front and center in this campaign, and today sending the Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , their chief messenger on this, down to Florida to mark the state's new six week ban going into effect.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's before many women even know they are pregnant, and she will blame \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  directly for this as he brags about overturning Roe. She will also call him out for his recent comments. Trump telling "Time" magazine that he would not stand in the way if states want to monitor women's pregnancies or punish those who violate abortion bans.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) President Biden calling that shocking and reprehensible. Saying in a video this morning, quote, "There seems to be no limit to how invasive Trump would let the state be." Now all eyes will today will also be on Arizona, the state senate there expected to repeal that Civil War era ban on abortion, returning the state to a 15 week ban.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now overall, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has really avoided taking specific positions on the issue of abortion, deferring instead to the states which he says are handling this issue brilliantly, while the Biden campaign is hoping all of this will drive voters to the polls for them in November. Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek5100005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BRIDGING THE AMERICAN DIVIDE THE EXCHANGE PROGRAM CONNECTING STUDENTS\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 BEES, MLB, MOUND, SWARM, HILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, WAR\par \par \uc2 UCLA, POLICE, PROTEST, PALESTINE, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIOLENT CLASHES BREAK OUT AT UCLA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE IN RIOT GEAR DESCEND ON CAMPUS\par \par \uc2 COLLEGE, FINANCIAL AID, FAFSA, DECISION, PROTESTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COLLEGE DECISION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROTESTS, FINANCIAL AID & MORE IMPACTING CHOICES\par \par \uc2 PRINCE WILLIAM, PRINCESS KATE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, MAMMOGRAM, GUIDANCE, 40, ARCILA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN SHOULD GET MAMMOGRAMS STARTING AT 40\par \par \uc2 VERGARA, BEYONCE, SHABOOZEY, PANERA\par \par \uc2 KNIVES, CONDIMENTS, BRAS, COOKWARE, COFFEE, SKINCARE\par \par \uc2 ICELAND, TRAVEL, BUDGET, ROSEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPERIENCE ICELAND!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL THE WAYS TO SAVE ON YOUR TRIP\par \par \uc2 POLITICS, CULTURE, AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRIDGING THE AMERICAN DIVIDE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE EXCHANGE PROGRAM CONNECTING STUDENTS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're back now with a look at the American Exchange Project. It's a program on a mission to bridge the divide across the country by allowing students an opportunity to visit places different from their home town.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We all crave connection. We all need to know we belong.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Founded in 1029, the American Exchange Project says their mission is to connect the divided country by sending high school seniors in the summer after they graduate on a free, week-long trip radically different from their own.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MCCULLOUGH III (AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 It's about of all the diversity that is in America, political, cultural, socio-economic, racial, ethnic. We live in a massive and diverse country, and unless we can learn to socialize and connect with people who are different from us, our democratic project is really going to be in trouble. We're seeing that manifest itself\u160\'00\'A0every day.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In 2022, 20-year-old Cornell Horner traveled from his home outside of Boston to Lemon, South Dakota, a town of roughly 1,000 people.\par \par \uc2 CORNELL HORNER (AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT PARTICIPANT)\par \par \uc2 We had many activities from, you know, going to a bison ranch and seeing how that process worked to going to town fairs to even being part of the town fair. Going to a meat, like a processing facility was really cool. It was something I would never do out here.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Last summer, 19-year-old Bryce went from his home town of 13,000 in Kilgore, Texas, to New York City.\par \par \uc2 BRYCE BORDERS (AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT PARTICIPANT)\par \par \uc2 I had this conception that New York was this really busy, grungy, dirty place, full of really busy and grumpy people. And when I got there, it was very different from that. We got to meet a lot of very nice people, and despite living very busy lives, fast-paced lives, the people that I experienced wanted to give their time to get to know us.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Since the program began, the American Exchange Project has run trips to 75 towns across 35 states.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MCCULLOUGH (AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT)\par \par \uc2 It's your chance to truly test your own political ideas and actually talk to people and humanize those said people. It's very easy to put people in boxes and not truly understand their totality. And I think the American Exchange Project gives you a chance to do that. It's also a chance to just get practice of going outside of your bubble that you grew up in and experience a different reality.\par \par \uc2 BRYCE BORDERS (AMERICAN EXCHANGE PROJECT PARTICIPANT)\par \par \uc2 We're all the same, despite our differences. We're all people. We all live very interesting lives. And we can all learn from each other. I think this is one of the biggest ways that you can solve the current split in the country, just by simply knowing each other better.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What a fantastic idea. Great to see it in action.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW ALERT ABOUT "GRANDPARENT SCAMS" DOJ CHARGES 16 AS FBI WARNS BILLIONS BEING STOLEN FROM SENIORS\b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COAST TO COAST CAMPUS CLASHES\par \par \uc2 COLUMBIA, PROTESTERS, POLICE, ENCAMPMENT, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, UCLA, CLASHES, POLICE, PALESTINIAN, ISRAELI\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, GAG ORDER, FINES, DAVIDSON, TESTIMONY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, FLORIDA, BAN, BIDEN, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARIJUANA, RECLASSIFY, BIDEN, DOJ, REVIEW\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, HOUSE, DEMS, GOP, GREEN, OUST\par \par \uc2 BOATERS, TRASH, OCEAN, MATTHEWS, OUTRAGE, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, GUIDANCE, AGE, MAMMOGRAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, PRISON, CANNABIS OIL, "COMING HOME"\par \par \uc2 SCAM, ALERT, GRANDPARENTS, DOJ, CHARGES, SELLINGER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with the new alert about grandparents scams. 16 people arrested for scams targeting the elderly. \uc2 FBI\uc2  is warning some seniors are losing their life savings. Chief justice correspondent Pierre Thomas is in Washington with the details. Good morning, Pierre.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ALERT ABOUT "GRANDPARENT SCAMS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ CHARGES 16 AS FBI WARNS BILLION BEING STOLEN FROM SENIORS\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning. There's no comforting way to put this, the \uc2 FBI\uc2  says seniors are increasingly the targets of a multibillion dollar black market scams, hunting their life savings.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning that disturbing video of a senior fatally shooting an unsuspecting Uber driver who he allegedly believed was part of a scam, evidence of an explosion in schemes targeting the elderly. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  calling such scams an epidemic, warning that many senior citizens are having their entire life savings drained.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Scammers so brazen they often post photos of themselves waving their stolen cash. The elderly losing a stunning $3.4 billion to scams in 2023. $300 million more than the previous year.\par \par \uc2 VICTIM OF SCAM (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We went to the bank, got the money.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This \uc2 FBI\uc2  public service announcement featuring real victims.\par \par \uc2 VICTIM OF SCAM (MALE)\par \par \uc2 And then she took off.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just yesterday, DOJ charging 16 suspects in the Dominican Republic and the US with a so called grandparents scam, stealing millions of dollars from hundreds of victims. Here's how it worked, an opener, someone pretending to be a distressed grandchild, calling their grandparents, claiming they need thousands of dollars because they've been in a car accident where a pregnant woman had been injured, causing a miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then a closer would call posing as a defense attorney or a court official to convince the panicked grandparent to pay. Scammers in the Dominican Republic would even recruit couriers here in the US to collect the money from victims homes or the elderly were told to mail the cash.\par \par \uc2 PHILIP SELLINGER (US ATTORNEY DISTRICT OF NEW JERSEY)\par \par \uc2 They're susceptible and not as familiar with technology as younger people and, therefore, they're most likely to be impacted by this type of fraud.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The \uc2 FBI\uc2  says don't be embarrassed, report it if you think you've been the victim of fraud. And here are a few tips so seniors can avoid being victimized. Destroy old bank statements and credit card receipts. Be extremely cautious of unsolicited phone calls, mailings, and door to door offers.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And whatever you do, do not give out your personal information unless you know exactly who you're dealing with. And do not pay in advance for services. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BREAST CANCER SCREENING GUIDANCE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those are great, great suggestions for not just for seniors, but for all of us. Hey, Pierre, thank you so much for that reporting. So important. Coming up later, more on the new breast cancer screening guidance and why it can help save many lives.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And next it is our "Play of the Day." Come on back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240524ek510000d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FLORIDA 6-WEEK ABORTION BAN IN EFFECT TRUMP DOUBLES DOWN: "IT'S UP TO THE STATE"\b0\par\par\uc2 737 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 KHALIDI, JEAN-PIERRE, ADAMS, PROTESTS, WAR, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 WAR, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , CEASE-FIRE, BLINKEN, NETANYAHU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLINKEN: "TIME IS NOW" FOR TRUCE\par \par \uc2 SCHOOL SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCES: TEEN SUSPECT KILLED OUTSIDE SCHOOL\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS FACE NEW TORNADO THREAT\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, TRUMP, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA 6-WEEK ABORTION BAN IN EFFECT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to Florida tonight, where, this evening, that state's six-week abortion ban has taken effect. Tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  defending states that have taken their own action on abortion rights. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Florida, saying she and President Biden believe these decisions should be made by women and not the government. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP DOUBLES DOWN: "IT'S UP TO THE STATE"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After spending Tuesday stuck in Manhattan courtroom, tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  parachuting into key battlegrounds Wisconsin and Michigan, before he has to fly right back to New York, where his criminal trial resumes tomorrow. In Waukesha today, Trump veering off teleprompter to defend himself on an issue that could decide the election, abortion.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Basically, the states decide on abortion. And people are absolutely thrilled with the way that's going on.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just this week, Trump telling "Time" magazine he won't object if states monitor pregnant women to make sure they comply with abortion bans and prosecute women who violate them. Today, he doubled down.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Now, I say, it's up to the state. They'll ask me a question about it, I say that's up to the state. So, I say to you, I think we did a very good job and that a lot of people are very happy with it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  firing back in Florida, where the state's new abortion law just went into effect, banning abortion at six weeks, before most women even know they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Basically, under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , it would be fair game for women to be monitored and punished by the government, whereas \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and I have a different view. We believe the government should never come between a woman and her doctor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ACCESS BANNED RESTRICTED\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Florida's near total ban means abortion access is now largely cut off across the entire south.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 As of this morning, 4 million women in this state woke up with fewer reproductive freedoms than they had last night. This is the new reality under a Trump abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You have to have heart. You have to have...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, the Biden campaign is counting on abortion rights to galvanize voters this November. Both campaigns keenly aware that this issue could be on the ballot in as many as 13 states, including several key battlegrounds, and that abortion rights has won every single time it has appeared on the ballot. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Both campaigns know this. And you're right there live at a Trump event in Michigan tonight at this hour. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAWMAKERS VOTE TO REPEAL ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, on the issue of abortion rights, the Arizona State Senate approved to appeal that Civil War-era abortion ban passed in 1864.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Two Republicans today voting with the Democrats, one week after the Arizona House approved the repeal. Tonight, Arizona Governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  says she will sign the repeal tomorrow into law, but repeal won't take effect until some time in the fall unless a court intervenes now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEINSTEIN BACK IN COURT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, in New York, disgraced movie mogul \uc2 Harvey Weinstein\uc2  was back in court for the first time since an appeals court overturned his 2020 rape conviction.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Weinstein arriving in a wheelchair. We learned today Weinstein is now set to be retried on sex assault charges sometime after Labor Day. He does remain in custody. His legal team also appealing a separate conviction in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240503ek5100006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION RIGHTS BATTLEGROUNDS FLORIDA 6-WEEK ABORTION BAN IN EFFECT\b0\par\par\uc2 1,389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 May 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 WEINSTEIN, GUTIERREZ, BRAGG, JUDD, AIDALA, ALLRED\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION, BAN, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. A big day for the fight for abortion access as multiple states become flashpoints for one of the most crucial issues on the ballot this fall. We found out tonight with correspondents reporting from battlegrounds in Arizona and Florida, but we begin with ABC's senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott on the ground in Michigan. Rachel, we know abortion is the central campaign issue in the presidential election. You're covering former President Trump's rally today, he also spoke earlier in Wisconsin. What's he saying or not saying about abortion?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I'll tell you, Byron, what he is saying is that he's often boasting about how he appointed three of the Supreme Court justices that overturned Roe versus Wade. And, of course, that cleared the way for 21 states to either ban or severely restrict access to abortion. But what he doesn't talk about really is the specifics of the impact that we are seeing ripple across the nation. Trump was asked directly whether or not he believes that states with abortion bans should be allowed to monitor women who are pregnant to make sure they're complying with the abortion laws in that state or whether women should be prosecuted if they do not comply and ended up seeking terminations for their pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Then he said it should be up to the states. Well, he doesn't really have that answer directly when he's talking about Arizona's near-total abortion ban. He said that was a state that went too far. So, what is clear here is that we heard from the former president today. He says that he wants to be on the winning side of this issue. And this is an issue that Republicans largely stayed away from in the midterm election. They saw that this was a very sensitive, touchy issue. They thought that this would really energize Democrats. They didn't want to talk about it at all. So, the fact that the former President has talked about this at both his stops today is a sign that he knows that this is going to be very important this election, Byron.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Rachel, a follow-up to the point you just made, if I may, abortion will be on the ballot in 13 states this November.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've been on the ground covering this issue. What are voters saying?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Look, voters see this as an important issue. When abortion is on the ballot, in every single election that it has been on the ballot, the side of abortion rights has won even in red states like Ohio and Kansas. So, both the Trump and Biden campaigns know that. They are watching this across the nation. And the Biden campaign is looking for this to energize their voters, to really galvanize voters. I will tell you, traveling across this country, I speak with voters at all of these rallies, but also in coffee shops, in supermarkets, and restaurants. And what I find is this is an important issue especially among the independent voters in some of these critical swing states that could ultimately decide this election.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that is why we are hearing the former president really hone in on this, saying that it should be up to the states, of course. And we're seeing the Biden campaign fire right back, blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for what we are seeing (inaudible) across the nation.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our Rachel Scott on the campaign trail. Thank you so much, my friend. Stay safe. Florida now has one of the most restrictive abortion bans in the country going into effect just today. Senior White House correspondent Selina Wang is in Jacksonville.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Byron, that six-week abortion ban in Florida just went into effect today. And I'm inside a planned parenthood in Jacksonville, Florida, where abortion providers are already turning patients away. This ban is sending shockwaves not just here in Florida but across the entire south. Now, women in the south, they have almost no options when it comes to abortion access.\par \par \uc2 DR SHELLY TAN (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 This has devastating and profound effects for women and girls and patients and families here in the south.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST 17 STATES HAVE CEASED NEARLY ALL ABORTIONS\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before today, Florida was one of the only states in the south where women could get an abortion.\par \par \uc2 DR SHELLY TAN (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 Currently right now, patients can have an abortion in North Carolina till 12 weeks. After that, Virginia. After that, Illinois, Kansas. And then the East Coast and West Coast.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  has emerged as a key anti-abortion proponent since the Supreme Court decision overturning Roe versus Wade ended the constitutional right to abortion.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 We have unprecedented success that we've had in this state. We do have some threats to that success on some of the things that will be on the ballot. And those will be things in these constitutional amendments.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Jacksonville, Florida.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Basically, under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , it would be fair game for women to be monitored and punished by the government. Whereas \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and I have a different view. We believe the government should never come between a woman and her doctor.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Voters in Florida eager to weigh in.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE LOVELL (FLORIDA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 I believe it should be a state's issue. Even though I, at the end of the day, believe that it's a human rights issue, so it goes beyond that. But if it were up to me, there would never be an abortion.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN WILSON (FLORIDA RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 I would like to have a choice in the matter. They went ahead and passed the bill. And we, as Floridians, didn't have a voice.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Florida, there are exceptions for rape, incest, and to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, if a woman now comes into this clinic seeking an abortion, she's past six weeks what do you tell her?\par \par \uc2 DR SHELLY TAN (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 You know, unfortunately, I have to tell her, "I'm so sorry, you know, because of this new law, this new ban, we cannot care for you." I can give her resources, you know, to travel out of state.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Selina. Several states away in Arizona, Republicans reversing course, repealing the state's recently reintroduced 160-year-old law which banned virtually all abortions. Jaclyn Lee was at the Capitol in Phoenix as the vote went down.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Byron, it came down to two. Senate Democrats only needed two Republicans to join their ranks to successfully repeal the 1864 abortion ban law. That is exactly what they got. The bill successfully passing both the House and the Senate and will head to the governor's desk for signature.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There on the ground, it is heated. Supporters of the repeal say women's health and livelihoods are at stake.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The appeal won't take effect until sometime in the fall. And unless the court intervenes, the 1864 abortion ban law will go into effect June 27th, putting pregnant women who need abortions in a very difficult position. Byron?\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Jaclyn, thank you. We will continue to bring you coverage of the fight over abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RETURN CAT\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, a cat is reunited with her owners after an Amazon return went awry.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020240503ek5100003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP ON ABORTION MONITORING SAYS IT IS UP TO STATES TO MONITOR PREGNANCIES\b0\par\par\uc2 659 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HOCHUL, SEARS, ALWAN, VALENCIA, PROTESTS, ARRESTS, ADAMS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, HUGHES, JENNINGS, CHHOEUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILLING VIDEO OF DEADLY SHOOTOUT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, FINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE HOLDS TRUMP IN CONTEMPT\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING NEW TORNADO THREAT\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON ABORTION MONITORING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the race for the White House. And tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's new comments on abortion, saying that some states might choose to monitor women's pregnancies to possibly prosecute women who violate abortion bans. Tonight, President Biden responding. And here's Mary Bruce.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAYS IT IS UP TO STATES TO MONITOR PREGNANCIES\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he won't stand in the way if states want to monitor pregnant women to make sure they comply with abortion bans, and he won't step in to prevent states from prosecuting women who violate those bans by ending their pregnancies. In an interview with "Time" magazine, Trump was asked, "Do you think states should monitor women's pregnancies, so they can know if they've gotten an abortion after the ban?" Trump saying, "I think they might do that. Again, you'll have to speak to the individual states." Trump then asked if he'd be comfortable with states prosecute women who get abortions. His response, "It's irrelevant whether I'm comfortable or not. It's totally irrelevant, because the states are going to make those decisions."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAYS IT IS UP TO STATES TO PROSECUTE ABORTIONS\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the 2016 campaign, Trump said women who have abortions should be punished.\par \par \uc2 JOURNALIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you believe in punishment for abortion? Yes or no? As a principle.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 And the answer is that there has to be some form of punishment.\par \par \uc2 JOURNALIST (MALE)\par \par \uc2 For the woman?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. There has to be some form.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He quickly backtracked. As president, he appointed three of the justices who overturned Roe versus Wade, something he continues to brag about.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We broke Roe v. Wade. And we did something that nobody thought was possible, we gave it back to the states and the states are working very brilliantly.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden calling Trump's comments today "reprehensible," saying "\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doesn't trust women. I do."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION OR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS COULD BE ON BALLOT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both Biden and Trump well aware that abortion could be on the ballot in 13 states this November, including critical battlegrounds like Pennsylvania, Nevada, Arizona, and Florida. And that every time abortion has been on the ballot since Roe was overturned, even in red states, abortion rights have won.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Biden team is trying to seize on this issue with the Vice President taking on a stepped-up role. She will be down in Florida tomorrow as the state's six-week abortion ban goes into effect. Now, Trump has said that ban is too severe, but he still won't say how he will vote on the issue when it's on the ballot in November. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce live at the White House for us. Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CAR CRASH INTO STORE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are learning more tonight, after some terrifying moments, an SUV crashing into a thrift store in Las Cruces, New Mexico.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities say the SUV crashed right through the class doors, killing one person and injuring more than a dozen others, including customers and employees. Police say the 69-year-old driver was pulling into a parking space when she mistakenly pressed on the accelerator instead of the brake.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240502ek4u00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POLITICAL HEADLINES FIRST WEEK OF TESTIMONY IN TRUMP CRIMINAL TRIAL\b0\par\par\uc2 1,043 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 NEBRASKA, TORNADOES, RESIDENTS, HOMES, SCHMADERER\par \par \uc2 SEVERE, THREAT, TORNADOES, RAINS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 CAMPUS, PROTESTS, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, USC, AL-SHAHABI, DEMANDS, FAY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TESTIMONY, DANIELS, PECKER, GRAFF, "APPRENTICE", MCDOUGAL\par \par \uc2 MCCLAIN, HOMICIDE, COOPER, PROBATION\par \par \uc2 KING, CHARLES, CANCER, TREATMENT, DUTIES\par \par \uc2 SOUTHWEST, AIRPORTS, FLIGHTS, STAFF, SEATING, BOEING\par \par \uc2 REPORTS, STORM, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 HURTS, EAGLES, DONATION, PHILADELPHIA, SCHOOLS, AC, WATLINGTON\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM STAGECOACH FESTIVAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, CAMPAIGN, VOTERS, BIDEN, ABORTION, \uc2 UAW\uc2 , DEAL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And we do start this half hour with a closer look at the top political headlines this week. And joining us are our Deputy Political Director Averi Harper and ABC White House Correspondent MaryAlice Parks. Good morning to both of you. So, Averi, let's start with you. Because we know former President Trump has been in a New York City courtroom all week for his hush-money trial. It's keeping him off the campaign trail. So, how are voters reacting to all this?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST WEEK OF TESTIMONY IN TRUMP CRIMINAL TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COULD HIS LACK OF CAMPAIGNING BE AFFECTING VOTER DECISIONS\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. Well, certainly not doing anything to expand his base of support. While he's in the courtroom, the longer he's there in the courtroom, the longer he's not able to be on the campaign trail sharing his vision for the country with voters. We've seen him try to take advantage of the media attention on the trial, speaking to cameras every single day but that's just not the same as being out in some of these big battleground states. So next week, Wednesday, court is slated not to be in session so he is going to make his way to both Michigan and Wisconsin, an effort to make up for some lost time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ON THE CAMPAIGN TRAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAWING CONTRASTS BETWEEN HIMSELF AND TRUMP\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, some lost time when he's in the courtroom but still dominating the news. So, MaryAlice, let's turn to President Biden and his campaign because he is out there, and he's really trying to draw a contrast between himself and Trump.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. Look, President Biden's campaign, they don't think that they have to talk too, too much about this New York criminal trial. One Biden campaign source told me just this week, they said that one of the best things they can do is actually say very little. Look, they think that it's really hard for former President Trump to look like a presidential candidate when he also looks like a criminal defendant. I mean, the Biden campaign talks a lot about this one kind of voter, this former Republican, kind of Conservative voter, who, in the last few years, has been turned off by Trump, turned off by some of the extremism, some of this chaos.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the Biden campaign claims that they are finding more and more of these voters. And so, even though they don't think that the average voter cares that much about the ins and outs maybe of this trial, they but care about own lives, paying their own bills. They think that they can capitalize on this just looking like, so messy for Trump and that that's the message they really wanna send home to those, sort of, former Republican voters that they're trying to win over.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the President making sure to point out that he's not watching the trial, he says, because he's out there campaigning. And Averi, another major issue playing out right now, abortion, of course, lots happening on the issue next week. What do you expect?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA LAWMAKERS TO VOTE ON REPEAL, FLORIDA'S SIX-WEEK BAN TO TAKE EFFECT MAY 1\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. In Arizona, we're gonna see lawmakers there potentially vote to repeal that 1864 abortion ban. A reminder, that law does not have exceptions for rape or incest. And then in Florida, on the same day, we're going to see that six-week abortion ban go into effect. Earlier this week, President Biden was out in Tampa. He was speaking about reproductive rights. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is going to be there in Jacksonville this week speaking about the issue, highlighting the issue.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And both of them putting the blame squarely on former President Trump for these state abortion bans that we've seen pass across the country. The Biden campaign really hoping that this issue is going to drive voters to turn out to the polls in November.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 UAW\uc2  WORKERS AT DAIMLER TRUCK REACH DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THE AVERTED STRIKE COULD IMPACT THE PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and MaryAlice, shifting gears here, let's talk about those auto workers in North Carolina reaching an 11th-hour deal overnight. A strike there could have, could've had big implications for the election.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Huge. North Carolina is a major battleground state, one the Democrats are hoping to pick up this year. You know, interesting to see that union really flex its strength in the South, not traditionally their strong turf. The, the union workers there, the, part of the \uc2 Daimler\uc2 , sort of, truck manufacturing plant, they want a 25 percent raise increase, also some health care benefits. So really a big victory. Like you said, it was the 11th hour, just minutes before thousands were potentially going to go on strike.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this comes just after last week. We saw workers at a plant in Tennessee vote to unionize. And this is definitely a big moment for auto workers but obviously, we've been talking so much about the labor union just across the country. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) MaryAlice Parks and Averi Harper, thank you so much for joining us as always. Great insight there.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240521ek4r0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA HOUSE VOTES TO REPEAL 1864 ABORTION BAN BILL ADVANCES TO STATE SENATE AFTER WEEKS OF STALEMATE\b0\par\par\uc2 692 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, MAYES, ELECTION INTERFERENCE\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , SUPREME COURT, PRESIDENTIAL IMMUNITY\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, ARRESTS, ASKANASE, PUTZEL, JOHNSON, SCHOOLS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE CLASH WITH PROTESTERS ON CAMPUSES ACROSS U.S.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOZENS ARRESTED AMID NEW WAVE OF DEMONSTRATIONS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, HAMILTON, KAGAN, SOTOMAYOR, BARRETT, TURNER, ALITO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA HOUSE VOTES TO REPEAL 1864 ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILL ADVANCES TO STATE SENATE AFTER WEEKS OF STALEMATE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the battle over abortion rights in Arizona. The state's House of Representatives voted to repeal the 1864 law banning the procedure, but the fight is not over yet. Rachel Scott is at the Supreme Court with more. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. It's been nearly two years, but the nation is still grappling with the impact of Roe versus Wade being overturned. The issue of abortion is now back in front of the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2  as Arizona takes one step to repealing their near-total abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Arizona is one step closer to repealing a near-total ban on abortion, written into law before it was even a state.\par \par \uc2 POLITICIAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 You passed House Bill 2677.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After two weeks of stalemate, the state legislature advancing a bill with three Republicans joining all Democrats.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE STEPHANIE STAHL HAMILTON (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 I think the political will is there to get this through both chambers and on to the governor's desk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BANNED FROM POINT OF CONCEPTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fourteen states have banned abortion from the point of conception since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hands off our bodies.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And for the first time, the justices weighing the impact of one of the new state abortion bans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO ABORTION BAN BEFORE THE SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The question now, whether hospitals in Idaho, which has a near total ban, can refuse to provide abortions in an emergency if the health of a woman is at serious risk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPARTMENT ARGUMENT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Justice Department arguing, federal law mandates they have emergency care even if that means an abortion. The liberal justices insisting Idaho's ban has a dire impact on patients.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE ELENA KAGAN (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Within these rare cases, there's a significant number where the woman is, her life is not in peril but she's going to lose her reproductive organs.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Many of the conservative justices seemed inclined to support Idaho's position.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE SAMUEL ALITO (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The statute imposes on a hospital a duty to the woman certainly and also a duty to the child. And it doesn't tell the hospital how it is to adjudicate conflicts between those interests. And it leaves that to state law.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , a staunch opponent of abortion rights, said she was shocked by Idaho's argument that women who may need emergency care could be turned away.\par \par \uc2 JOSHUA TURNER (ATTORNEY REPRESENTING STATE OF IDAHO)\par \par \uc2 It is very case by case.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE SONIA SOTOMAYOR (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 That's the problem.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE AMY CONEY BARRETT (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 I'm kind of shocked actually because I thought your own expert had said below that these kinds of cases were covered. And you're now saying they're not?\par \par \uc2 JOSHUA TURNER (ATTORNEY REPRESENTING STATE OF IDAHO)\par \par \uc2 No, I'm not saying that. That's just my point, your honor, is that...\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE AMY CONEY BARRETT (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Well, you're hedging.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A decision in that case is expected sometime in June. As for Arizona, that bill still needs to clear the State Senate before it hits the governor's desk. State lawmakers expected to return back to session next week. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thanks, Rachel. Appreciate you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240516ek4p0005p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION IN FRONT OF SUPREME COURT FIRST TIME COURT CONSIDERS ABORTION SINCE OVERTURNING ROE V WADE\b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, PECKER, TESTIMONY, GAG ORDER, PROSECUTION, JUDGE\par \par \uc2 SENATE, TIKTOK, ULTIMATUM, RICKETTS, WARNER, DONHURST\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, PRO-PALESTINIAN, UNIVERSITIES, POLICE, HUNTER, ALWAN\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, IDAHO, ABORTION, JUSTICES, BAN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Glad those talks are continuing. Stephanie, thank you. Now to the abortion rights showdown at the Supreme Court. The Justices will hear arguments about a near total ban in Idaho. Rachel Scott is there for us. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION IN FRONT OF SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST TIME COURT CONSIDERS ABORTION SINCE OVERTURNING ROE V WADE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. And the stakes here are high. This is the first time that the Supreme Court is considering the scope of a state's abortion ban since Roe versus Wade was overturned. At the center of the case is Idaho. The state bans abortions in nearly all cases. It does include a narrow exception to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT HEARS ABORTION RIGHTS CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS IDAHO'S NEAR TOTAL BAN BEING CHALLENGED\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But the Justice Department is arguing that even in states where abortion is banned, under federal health care law hospitals are still required to terminate pregnancies if the patient's life or health is at serious risk. The Justice Department is pointing to a law from decades ago, before Roe versus Wade was overturned, that was originally created to ensure that patients who do not have insurance aren't turned away from hospitals.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Anti-abortion rights advocates argue that the Biden administration is misusing this law to try to justify abortions. On the other side of this, though, we have talked to doctors and patients who have told us they are caught in a web of what they call confusing laws. Some doctors have told us they have questioned whether or not their patient is sick enough before they can even provide any lifesaving care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And doctors, of course, face serious penalties. Loss of license, fines, in some cases even prison time. And all of this is playing out in the back drop of an election year where the Biden administration is hoping to use this to energize voters ahead of a very critical election. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240516ek4o0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP ON ABORTION RIGHTS IN FLORIDA DEMOCRATS HOPING ISSUE WILL TURN SUNSHINE STATE BLUE\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, PECKER, TESTIMONY, GAG ORDER, PROSECUTION, JUDGE\par \par \uc2 SENATE, TIKTOK, ULTIMATUM, RICKETTS, WARNER, DONHURST\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, PRO-PALESTINIAN, UNIVERSITIES, POLICE, HUNTER, ALWAN\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, IDAHO, ABORTION, JUSTICES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ABORTION, TRUMP, BANS, VOTING\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rachel. On that point, President Biden is targeting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  over abortion rights, blasting him yesterday at a Florida campaign event over a six week abortion ban that's going into effect in the state next week.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP ON ABORTION RIGHTS IN FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS HOPING ISSUE WILL TURN SUNSHINE STATE BLUE\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 For 50 years the court ruled that there was a fundamental constitutional right to privacy. But two years ago that was taken away. Let's be real clear, there's one person responsible for this nightmare and he's acknowledged it and he brags about it, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce traveled with the President. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well President Biden is eager to put the issue of abortion front and center in this campaign. As you heard there, he is trying to make \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  own this, blaming him for the new restrictions and bans that we are seeing across the country.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yesterday in that speech in Florida the President's first major campaign address on this issue by our count at least a dozen times the President argued Trump should be held accountable and is to blame for this. Now \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has bragged about overturning Roe versus Wade, appointing the three Justices who helped strike it down.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP ON ABORTION RIGHTS IN FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLAMES FORMER PRESIDENT FOR RESTRICTIVE LAW GOING INTO EFFECT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And since then 21 states have now enacted tough new restrictions and bans. The former President, though, says this should be up to the states. He says they are handling it brilliantly. President Biden obviously strongly disagrees. He says Trump has to be held accountable. And he is hoping that this issue will drive voters to the polls in November. He is well aware that every time this issue has been on the ballot since Roe was struck down, even in red states, abortion rights have won. Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240516ek4o0002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JUSTICES APPEAR DIVIDED IN ABORTION CASE SUPREME COURT WEIGHS EMERGENCY ABORTION CARE\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, PROTESTS, JOHNSON, SHAFIK\par \par \uc2 GOLDBERG-POLIN, ISRAEL, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN-ISRAELI HOSTAGE VIDEO RELEASED\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, UKRAINE, FOREIGN AID, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. SECRETLY SHIPPED LONG-RANGE MISSILES\par \par \uc2 KAGAN, ALITO, TURNER, ABORTION, PRELOGAR, SOTOMAYOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICES APPEAR DIVIDED IN ABORTION CASE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For the first time since overturning Roe versus Wade, the justices at the Supreme Court today hearing arguments about Idaho's near-total abortion ban. What happens if a woman in desperate need seeks help in the ER? Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT WEIGHS EMERGENCY ABORTION CARE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, for the first time since overturning Roe versus Wade, the Supreme Court weighing the impact of one of the new state abortion bans, whether hospitals in Idaho, which has a near total ban, can refuse to provide abortions in emergency if the health of a woman is at serious risk.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH PRELOGAR\uc2  (SOLICITOR GENERAL OF THE US)\par \par \uc2 If a woman comes to an emergency room facing a grave threat to her health, but she isn't yet facing death, doctors either have to delay treatment and allow her condition to materially deteriorate or they're airlifting her out of the state, so she can get the emergency care that she needs.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Justice Department today arguing that, if a woman's health is at risk, federal law mandates that they receive emergency care, even if that means an abortion. The liberal justices on the court, all women, making it clear Idaho is putting doctors and patients in untenable positions.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE ELENA KAGAN (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Within these rare cases, there's a significant number where the woman is, her life is not in peril, but she's going to lose her reproductive organs.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But many of the conservative justices on the court seemed inclined to support Idaho's position. Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  noting the federal law mandating emergency care also cites a responsibility to an unborn child.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE SAMUEL ALITO (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The statute imposes on the hospital a duty to the woman certainly and also a duty to the child. And it doesn't tell the hospital how it is to adjudicate conflicts between those interests, and it leaves that to state law.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Still, even among conservatives, there was some concern about Idaho's position. In one remarkable moment, Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2 , a staunch opponent of abortion rights, exclaimed she was shocked by Idaho's argument that women in crisis could be refused an abortion in an emergency room on a case-by-case basis.\par \par \uc2 JOSHUA TURNER (ATTORNEY OFFICE OF THE IDAHO ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 It is very case by case. The examples, the prong...\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE SONIA SOTOMAYOR (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 That's the problem, isn't it?\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE AMY CONEY BARRETT (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Counsel, I'm kind of shocked actually because I thought your own expert had said below that these kinds of cases were covered.\par \par \uc2 JOSHUA TURNER (ATTORNEY OFFICE OF THE IDAHO ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE AMY CONEY BARRETT (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 And you're now saying they're not?\par \par \uc2 JOSHUA TURNER (ATTORNEY OFFICE OF THE IDAHO ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 No, I'm not saying that. That's just my point, your honor, is that...\par \par \uc2 JUSTICE AMY CONEY BARRETT (\uc2 US SUPREME COURT\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Well, you're hedging.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A decision on that case is expected in June. Meanwhile, tomorrow, the justices will consider whether or not former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  should have absolute immunity in his federal case surrounding his efforts to try to overturn the 2020 election. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All eyes on that case as well. Rachel Scott at the Supreme Court, thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240426ek4o00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PRESIDENT BIDEN HEADING TO FLORIDA STATE'S NEW ABORTION BAN TAKES EFFECT IN ONE WEEK\b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, ARRESTS, UNIVERSITIES, HOCHUL, GERBER, NORTO\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, PECKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER NATIONAL ENQUIRER PUBLISHER DAVID PECKER ON WITNESS STAND\par \par \uc2 SWISS AIR, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , FATIGUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLOSE CALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FAA\uc2  INVESTIGATING INCIDENT AT JFK AIRPORT\par \par \uc2 FOREIGN AID, JOHNSON, SENATE, VOTE, TIKTOK, BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE CONSIDERS MAJOR FOREIGN AID PACKAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INCLUDES $60 BILLION IN MILITARY AID FOR UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ABORTION ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN HEADING TO FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE'S NEW ABORTION BAN TAKES EFFECT IN ONE WEEK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, George, now this morning, President Biden taking his message about a woman's right to choose to Florida exactly one week before the state's new law outlawing most abortions goes into effect. Our chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce will be traveling today with the President. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Well, the Biden campaign is trying to seize this moment, blasting new abortion restrictions across the country and urging that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this as he boasts of appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, in Tampa today, President Biden will hold his first major campaign event on the issue one week before Florida is set the ban most abortions after six weeks, before most women even know that they are pregnant. Now, so far, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , the vice president, has been leading the charge on this issue.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The President, of course, is a staunch defender of abortion access. But as a catholic, he's had a complicated evolution on the issue. But the campaign knows this is going to be a defining issue for this campaign, and they're eager to put it front and center, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Mary, thank you. And safe travels today.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240516ek4n00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BIDEN TAKES ON TRUMP OVER ABORTION VISITS FLORIDA DAYS BEFORE 6-WEEK BAM TAKES EFFECT\b0\par\par\uc2 590 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRIAL, TRUMP, PECKER\par \par \uc2 WAR, HUNTER, ALWAN, ADAMS, PROTESTS, GAZA, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARRESTS SOAR AS CAMPUS PROTESTS SPREAD\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, KIDNAPPING, HUIZAR, GREGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE MANHUNT FOR FMR. OFFICER\par \par \uc2 SETTLEMENT, NASSAR, MARONEY, RAISMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $138 MILLION+ SETTLEMENT WITH NASSAR VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ABORTION, 2024 ELECTION, TRUMP, JOSHUA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN TAKES ON TRUMP OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to President Biden tonight helping to put the state of Florida back in play this November. Tonight, the President's major abortion rights speech in Florida with that state's new six-week abortion ban just days now from going into effect. Mary Bruce in Florida.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VISITS FLORIDA DAYS BEFORE 6-WEEK BAM TAKES EFFECT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden today traveling to Florida, just days before the state's strict new abortion law goes into effect, banning the procedure at just six weeks, when many women don't even know they're pregnant.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 There's one person responsible for this nightmare, and he's acknowledged and he brags about it, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's Biden's first major campaign speech on abortion, an issue he's putting at the center of his re-election bid.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE THAT BAN OR RESTRICT ABORTION\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Florida, one of 21 states to ban or severely restrict abortion since the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade. Trump boasts of appointing three of the justices that struck Roe down.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We broke Roe v. Wade, and we did something that nobody thought was possible, we gave it back to the states. And the states are working very brilliantly.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Biden calling Trump out.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Individual state laws are working, in his words, brilliantly. Brilliantly. It's a six-week ban in Florida, it's really brilliant, isn't it? Even before women know they're pregnant. Is that brilliant?\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Biden is counting on the issue to energize voters, especially women. He was introduced today by Kaitlyn Joshua of Louisiana. She was almost 12 weeks pregnant when she suffered a miscarriage. And when she showed up at the hospital bleeding, doctors refused to treat her, afraid of running afoul with Louisiana's near total abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 KAITLYN JOSHUA (ABORTION RIGHTS ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 Another hospital basically just told me they would send me home with prayers, but were not able to medically diagnose miscarriage.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They said they would send you home with prayers, but couldn't give you medical advice?\par \par \uc2 KAITLYN JOSHUA (ABORTION RIGHTS ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 Correct. That's correct.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her message to voters tonight...\par \par \uc2 KAITLYN JOSHUA (ABORTION RIGHTS ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 So, abortion is absolutely on the ballot this year. If this is not a topic that you think is going to touch you or it doesn't touch you currently, it absolutely will.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Florida is one of 14 states where abortion could be on the ballot in November. The Biden campaign hoping that could put this state in play for them. They know every time the issue's been on the ballot, even in red states, abortion rights have won. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce traveling with the president in Florida. Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240425ek4n00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THREE MAJOR SUPREME COURT CASES AHEAD THIS WEEK WHETHER CITIES CAN PUNISH PEOPLE WHO LIVE ON THE STREET\b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $95 BILLION AID BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOREIGN AID APPROVAL\par \par \uc2 FOREIGN AID, TIKTOK, JOHNSON, MASSIE, GREENE, NEHLS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, WEST BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAELI FORCES CONDUCT OPERATIONS IN SOUTHERN GAZA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOCAL HEALTH OFFICIALS SAY AT LEAST 13 KILLED INCLUDING NINE CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 CAR, CRASH, ARREST, GOODNOUGH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CAR CRASH IN MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VEHICLE SLAMS INTO BIRTHDAY PARTY IN KILLING TWO CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPENING STATEMENTS TO BEGIN MONDAY IN TRUMP TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROSECUTORS REFUSING TO NAME FIRST WITNESS FEARING ATTACKS FROM TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, FOREIGN AID, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPENING STATEMENTS TO BEGIN MONDAY IN TRUMP TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE IMPACT THE CASE COULD HAVE ON THE PRESIDENTIAL RACE\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL IMMUNITY, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, HOMELESSNESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THREE MAJOR SUPREME COURT CASES AHEAD THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHETHER CITIES CAN PUNISH PEOPLE WHO LIVE ON THE STREET\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And speaking of the Supreme Court, we've got three major cases this week before the court dealing with abortion rights, homelessness, and presidential immunity. ABC's Devin Dwyer is in Washington with more on this. Good morning, Devin.\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Gio. It's the last week of oral arguments in the Supreme Court's term, and it will be historic. Tomorrow here at the Supreme Court, the biggest case on homelessness in 40 years. At issue is, can cities punish people, homeless people, who sleep outside?\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're talking about tickets, fines, jail time possibly for people camping in public parks. A growing number of cities are using laws to crack down on those homeless encampments. But is it cruel and unusual punishment when people have nowhere else to go? The case could have sweeping implications for cities nationwide as they grapple with the surge in homelessness.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BANS & EMERGENCY CARE FOR WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On Wednesday, the court will take up, for the first time since overturning Roe vs. Wade, the scope of a state abortion ban, specifically whether hospitals have to allow abortion access to women in emergency situations. And on Thursday, the biggest case of the week, perhaps of the term, a landmark case on presidential immunity. Can prosecutors bring criminal charges against former President Trump for his efforts to overturn the 2020 election?\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Obviously, huge stakes in that case. And decisions in all of these cases are expected by the end of June. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Jam-packed schedule at the High Court. Devin Dwyer, thank you.\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240515ek4l0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW ROADBLOCK IN ARIZONA ABORTION SHOWDOWN GOP LAWMAKERS BLOCK DEMOCRATIC EFFORT TO REPEAL CIVIL WAR-ERA LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 911 OUTAGES\par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADO, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADO THREAT ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS ON ALERT FOR SEVERE WEATHER AS NEW STORM HEADS EAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, JURY SELECTION, JOHNSON, FOREIGN AID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY SELECTION RESUMES IN TRUMP'S "HUSH MONEY" TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SELECTION COULD WRAP BY END OF WEEK WITH SEVEN JURORS ALREADY SEATED\par \par \uc2 BOEING, SALEHPOUR, BLUMENTHAL, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING FIRES BACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMPANY RESPONDS TO WHISTLEBLOWER'S TESTIMONY ABOUT SAFETY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, ARIZONA, TOMA, BURCH, TAYLOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW ROADBLOCK IN ARIZONA ABORTION SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP LAWMAKERS BLOCK DEMOCRATIC EFFORT TO REPEAL CIVIL WAR-ERA LAW\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the abortion rights showdown in Arizona. Republicans in the state legislature once again blocked a Democratic effort to repeal the Civil War-era law that virtually bans abortion in the state. Elizabeth Schulze is in Phoenix. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. This is the second time that Arizona's legislature has failed to repeal that Civil War-era abortion ban after it was upheld last week by the State Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Arizona Republican lawmakers defiant, refusing to repeal a 160-year-old law banning nearly all abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE BEN TOMA (REP) (ARIZONA HOUSE SPEAKER)\par \par \uc2 Legislatures are not built for knee-jerk reactions.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) All but one Republican in the statehouse declining to join Democrats to fast-track legislation that would roll back the law.\par \par \uc2 POLITICIAN (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of time to work on this issue.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) State senators are now trying to move forward with their own bill to repeal it, but that process could take weeks.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR EVA BURCH (DEM) (MESA ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 This is a stain on our history that this ban even exists from a time when the age of consent was 10, from a time when women didn't have the right to vote.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The law prohibits abortion in every instance except for one, to save the life of the mother. If no repeal is passed, the ban could take effect as soon as June.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER IN ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Effectively, our ability to provide abortion care goes away.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, if this law stands, you can no longer provide abortions here.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER IN ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 That is correct.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 At her clinic in Phoenix, Dr. DeShawn Taylor is telling patients they might not be able to get the care they need.\par \par \uc2 DR DESHAWN TAYLOR (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER IN ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 We are having conversations with them, letting them know that we're going week by week, because there will come a time when we'll have to stop.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The House and the Senate here are not expected to meet again until next Wednesday. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Elizabeth, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240514ek4i00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN OPENS UP ABOUT BREAST CANCER JOURNEY "IT WAS A LOT TOUGHER THAN I EXPECTED"\b0\par\par\uc2 758 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, JURORS, JUDGE, MCGEE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, VALUES, TRUMP, BATTLEGROUND\par \par \uc2 TORNADOES, OUTBREAK, DAMAGE, KEMP\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES, ALERTS, WINDS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, REPUBLICANS, FOREIGN AID, MAYORKAS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, RESPONSE, SANCTIONS, GAZA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, RIGHTS, VOTE, LEGISLATURE, CIVIL WAR\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, JAN 6TH, JUSTICES, DIVIDED\par \par \uc2 CAPITOL HILL, HEARINGS, WHISTLEBLOWER, BOEING, \uc2 FAA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APRIL RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 KOHBERGER, ALIBI, JUDGE, MURDERS, LLOYD\par \par \uc2 WNBA\uc2 , PAY, DISPARITY, CLARK, BRENNAN, ENGELBERT\par \par \uc2 DAVIS, HOCKEY, PUCK, PODOLAK, HERO\par \par \uc2 ORANGUTAN, BABY, LUNA, WENDZEL, ENDANGERED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTIVE PATTERN\par \par \uc2 JURY, VOIR DIRE, TRUMP, TRIAL, BUSINESS RECORDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST SEVEN JURORS SELECTED FOR TRUMP TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE SIGNALS OPENING STATEMENTS COULD BE MONDAY\par \par \uc2 ZEPBOUND, OBESITY, DRUG, SLEEP APNEA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BENEFIT OF WEIGHT LOSS DRUG ON SLEEP APNEA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROMISING RESULTS IN NEW REPORT ON ZEPBOUND\par \par \uc2 PHONES, RESTAURANT, AL CONDOMINIO, WINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FREE WINE? HAND OVER YOUR PHONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESTAURANT'S ENTICING OFFER TO DO AWAY WITH PHONES\par \par \uc2 MUNN, ACTOR, BREAST CANCER, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OLIVIA MUNN OPENS UP ABOUT BREAST CANCER JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "IT WAS A LOT TOUGHER THAN I EXPECTED"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nice shot there of New York City. And we're back now with our "GMA" cover story, Olivia Munn sharing details about her breast cancer journey, the actress telling "People" magazine that it was a lot tougher than she expected. Eva Pilgrim is here with more details. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. When Olivia Munn found out she had breast cancer, she says her mind immediately went to her son and how she would tell her partner. And then she went into action mode, determined to fight this.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Olivia Munn revealing the new details of her breast cancer journey, opening up the "People" magazine about her fight.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 Having, you know, a little baby at home made everything much more terrifying. It makes you realize that, like, cancer does not care who you are. It comes at you, and you have no choice but to face it head on.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One year ago, Munn was diagnosed with luminal B, a fast-growing and aggressive type of breast cancer. The diagnosis, she says, was a complete shock. Just three months prior, she'd gotten an all clear during her annual mammogram, but when her OB/GYN asked her if she's ever gotten her lifetime breast cancer risk score, she filled out a questionnaire, discovering her score was high due to family history and having her first child over 30. Her doctor ordering an MRI and an ultrasound of the breast, finding multiple tumors. Tissue samples revealed stage 1 breast cancer. Within 30 days, she underwent a double mastectomy, where she says doctors found another cancer mass the size of a tangerine.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 I really tried to be prepared, but the truth is that nothing, nothing could prepare me for what I would feel like, what it would look like.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While many breast cancers can be found through a screening mammogram, some 20 percent of breast cancer cases, like Munn's, are missed.\par \par \uc2 ANDREA MANDELL ("PEOPLE")\par \par \uc2 She said she feels grateful that she was given the opportunity to fight. And as she underscores, the reason she was able to fight this fight is because of a prevention\u160\'00\'A0tool that her OB/GYN utilized.\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA MUNN (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 It's a very profound journey to find out how much strength and resilience I have.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She tells us that she's now on hormone suppression therapy, which she says has put her into a medically induced menopause. Her story a reminder that it's important to talk with your doctor about your personal risk to know what imaging test is right for you. And, guys, so many people have said to me, "A tangerine-size cancer. How did the mammogram miss that?" But this story is a reminder that you really need to know what imaging is the best one to look at. And you need to talk to your doctor about that.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, we're fortunate she's willing to share this story so other people can see her fight, her journey and hopefully help them, yes.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Conversations just like this.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All right. Thank you so much for that, Eva. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240531ek4h0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS FIGHT LEGISLATURE EXPECTED TO VOTE ON REPEALING CIVIL WAR ERA LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, JURORS, JUDGE, MCGEE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, CAMPAIGN, VALUES, TRUMP, BATTLEGROUND\par \par \uc2 TORNADOES, OUTBREAK, DAMAGE, KEMP\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TORNADOES, ALERTS, WINDS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, REPUBLICANS, FOREIGN AID, MAYORKAS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, RESPONSE, SANCTIONS, GAZA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, RIGHTS, VOTE, LEGISLATURE, CIVIL WAR\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Matt, thank you. We turn now to the abortion rights fight in Arizona. A key vote is set for today on repealing the 160-year-old law that virtually bans abortion in the state. Elizabeth Schulze is in Phoenix. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS FIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEGISLATURE EXPECTED TO VOTE ON REPEALING CIVIL WAR ERA LAW\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Rebecca. This is a critical moment here in Arizona's capital, as some lawmakers seek to roll back that controversial civil war abortion ban. The state supreme court last week reinstated the law from 1864, that bans abortion in every instance except to save the life of a mother. Democratic lawmakers immediately tried to pass legislation to repeal the ban but they were blocked by Republicans.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, today Democrats in the state house are set to try again. They'll need the support of at least two GOP lawmakers for the repeal of the law to pass. It would then head to the state senate, where it would also need two Republican votes. Arizona's Attorney General says if legislation isn't passed the soonest the ban will take effect is this June.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Arizona is one of 21 states to forbid or severely restrict access to an abortion since the end of Roe V Wade. The issue will likely be put directly to voters in November. Arizona is among up to 14 states expected to include an abortion measure on the ballot. And we are told that activists on both sides of the debate will hold rallies here today. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240531ek4h00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 REPEAL OF AZ ABORTION BAN BLOCKED GOP LAWMAKERS REJECT EFFORTS TO RESCIND CIVIL WAR-ERA LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, WEATHER, TRACK, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 MAYORKAS, SENATE, IMPEACHMENT, JOHNSON, AID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAYORKAS IMPEACHMENT CHARGES DISMISSED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, HERNANDEZ, TOMA, FARNSWORTH, KOLODIN, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPEAL OF AZ ABORTION BAN BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The major headline tonight involving the issue of abortion as well. In Arizona tonight, the near total ban on abortion dating back to the Civil War, before women had the right to vote, before Arizona was even a state, this ban will move forward. Republicans in that state today blocking efforts to repeal it. ABC's Elizabeth from Phoenix tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP LAWMAKERS REJECT EFFORTS TO RESCIND CIVIL WAR-ERA LAW\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Arizona Republican lawmakers refusing to repeal one of the toughest abortion laws in the country. A law written during the Civil War more than 160 years ago, banning abortion in all cases except to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE BEN TOMA (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 The last thing we should be doing today is rushing a bill through the legislative process.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democrats outraged.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE ALMA HERNANDEZ (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 We're talking about a bill that was passed before Arizona was even a state, before women had the right to vote.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Republican lawmakers tonight defending the law.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE DAVID FARNSWORTH (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 We have the best law possible on the books right now.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The 1864 law is the best law possible?\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE DAVID FARNSWORTH (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A law that is, makes abortion impossible for women in every circumstance except for, to save a mother's life?\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE DAVID FARNSWORTH (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Arizona is a pro-life state. That law was put into place by people that believe in the sanctity of life.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona, one of 21 states to ban or severely restrict abortion since the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has boasted of nominating three of the five justices who overturned Roe.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We broke Roe v. Wade. And we did something that nobody thought was possible, we gave it back to the states. And the states are working very brilliantly.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Still, Trump says, Arizona went too far. He knows that voters will likely have the last word on the matter. Arizona one of 14 states where abortion could be the ballot this fall.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ON REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS COULD BE ON BALLOT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion rights has won wherever it's gone before voters, even in conservative states like Kansas, Kentucky, and Ohio. Today, Republican lawmakers told me, they're not worried.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE ALEXANDER KOLODIN (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Voters are smart. They would rather vote for somebody that they respect and disagree with than somebody who doesn't believe in anything.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (BC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, Arizona is, of course, a key battleground in the presidential election. But it is not just the candidates on the ballot. Arizona, again, one of 14 states where voters are expected to decide on abortion. We know in the past when it's on the ballot, turnout has gone up. And in every instance, the abortion rights position has won. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It will be a major issue in November along with the presidential race indeed. Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240419ek4h00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION SHOWDOWN ARIZONANS BRACE FOR POSSIBLE TOTAL BAN ON ABORTION CARE\b0\par\par\uc2 2,356 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 AZ, ABORTION, BAN, PROVIDERS, PATIENTS, TAYLOR, GOODRICK, FEIRING, MAYES\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. Thank you for joining us. All eyes are on Arizona, as tomorrow could be a pivotal day in the fight for abortion access. As the clock counts down to a total ban going into effect, the state legislature is scheduled to meet and could possibly decide the future of abortions in the state. In the midst of the uncertainty, patients and providers in Arizona are scrambling. Here's ABC's senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At clinics across the state of Arizona, there is a growing sense of urgency and anger in the air.\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 I didn't go to medical school to go to jail.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 If this law goes into effect, we have to legally cease providing all abortions.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For doctors trying to avoid arrest...\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 All right.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...then patients seeking care...\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 The person left. Hi.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...it's now become a race against time again.\par \par \uc2 ANONYMOUS PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's pretty scary. I don't want other women to suffer.\par \par \uc2 PENELOPE (PATIENT/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 The women who might not have the opportunity to get abortion care in a, in a few weeks, I feel a profound amount of sadness.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEIGH FEIRING (NURSE/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 I'm angry. This is a fight we need to not give up.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The confusion and chaos kicked off just days ago, after the State Supreme Court ruled that an abortion ban from 1864, before Arizona was even an official state, could go into effect.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 The law is confusing, and vague. It was written 160 years ago.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona is just the latest state to institute a highly restrictive abortion ban, but this particular law is sparking backlash and could signal a turning of the tide.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When the Dobbs decision came down, Conservatives and Republicans said they supported laws like this one because it made abortion harder to obtain. But perceptions have changed. Most major Republicans in Arizona are now against this law.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the timing is key. Arizona has become one of the most crucial swing states, helping tip the 2020 election for President Biden. Both sides are now wondering if this is all a warning sign of voters bucking abortion bans come November.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Please, can we help you keep your baby in any way, shape, or form?\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 What happened?\par \par \uc2 CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We saw some boyfriend walk up and was, like, arguing with the protesters as (inaudible) .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since the court decision, Dr. Gabrielle Goodrick hasn't taken a day off.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 How you guys doing?\par \par \uc2 CLINIC VISITOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Good.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She owns Camelback Family Planning in Phoenix, the state's busiest abortion provider.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 Abortion care is not gonna go away, no matter what the laws are or the restrictions. Half of all pregnancies are unplanned and half of those pregnancies end in an abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the nearly two years since Roe versus Wade was overturned, uncertainty and confusion have almost become the norm in Arizona. Clinics like Goodrick's have periodically had to halt services. The state went from allowing abortions at 24 weeks to 15 weeks, and soon, not at all.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION LIMITS\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 The law that they want to enforce was written by one single white man in 1864, during the Civil War. Many of those laws would make our stomach curl. The age of consent is the age of 10. A person of color can't testify against a white man. Women had no vote. Slavery was legal.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So far, no one can say exactly when the ban will go into effect. Is it two weeks? Is it 45 days? Sixty days? No one knows.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 What we're hearing from patients is fear, calling, "when is this effective? Oh, my gosh, can I get the care I need?" I mean, one patient called, she didn't even have a positive pregnancy test yet, but her period was late, and she was panicking. "What if it's positive, where am I gonna go? What's gonna happen?" This is causing a lot of chaos, and not only for staff, but obviously for patients.\par \par \uc2 PENELOPE (PATIENT/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 It would be financially irresponsible to have a child right now for us.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At Dr. Goodrick's clinic, we met a young woman who asked us to call her Penelope. She just moved from Indiana, a state with an abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 PENELOPE (PATIENT/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 The law being from 1864, it's hard to really articulate how I feel about that. The fact that the law is so old, it proves to me just how archaic our government can be sometimes.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEIGH FEIRING (NURSE/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 So, do you have any questions about when you go home?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We also met Amaretta, a single mom of one. She doesn't feel like she can put her body through another pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 AMARETTA (PATIENT/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 For me to carry another baby would be a lot of wear and tear on my body, and I want to raise a daughter that I have now.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She told us if this happened after the ban, she would not have the money to travel out of state.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 Getting transportation, time off work, child care, gas money, a car that works, I mean, it's, you know, it's hard.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With so many states restricting or outright banning abortion, especially across the South, abortion providing states are hard to find. Arizona was one of them.\par \par \uc2 ASHLEIGH FEIRING (NURSE/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 We've gotten patients from Texas. We've gotten patients from the Deep South, from states like Idaho and Ohio.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just a few miles away, Dr. DeShawn Taylor is also working nonstop. She's a board certified OB-GYN and the sole owner and CEO of the Desert Star Institute for Family Planning.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do bans like this one really stop abortions from happening?\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 Bans don't stop abortions. My biggest concern is the criminalization piece.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Taylor's clinic is smaller, but no less important, especially since she's one of the few Black providers in the state. Despite her convictions, she says she has to abide by the laws. She can't risk going to prison.\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 I feel that I just want to be real about my intention to stay free. Black women physicians are two percent of the physician workforce here in the United States. So, my existence matters. They come here because I'm here. And I don't take that for granted.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona's Democratic Attorney General Kris Mayes says she won't enforce the 1864 law, but she acknowledges she can't stop local prosecutors from doing so.\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 I would urge Arizonans who are pregnant to make a plan. And I can't believe I'm having to say that. Start thinking about California and Nevada and New Mexico or Colorado.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Taylor is focused on keeping her doors open, even if the ban goes into effect.\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 At this point, the goal is to provide abortion care until we can't legally do it anymore.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are you now preparing that that reality might be sooner than you think?\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 We are prepared for that reality. And then, I, I think about the staff, you know, they could work anywhere, but they choose to work here.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If the clinic can't provide abortions, that means women like this 23-year-old would have no place to go. She showed up relieved that she made it before the ban goes into effect. She asked us not to show her face.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Were you confused when you saw the news that the Supreme Court is allowing this abortion ban to go into effect?\par \par \uc2 ANONYMOUS PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I thought, "What's gonna happen when I come into my appointment? Am I just gonna be told, 'no, we can't do it anymore, unfortunately.' And I thought, "What's gonna happen now?"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You are here now and you have access to abortion care, but you would not have had access to that in a couple of weeks when this law goes into effect. What do you make of that?\par \par \uc2 ANONYMOUS PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's scary. I feel like the child would just suffer if it came into this life, because, because of the economy right now, I'm not financially good enough to even take care of a child and I can barely take care of myself at this point.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Unlike in previous years, when the issue of abortion was more likely to draw Conservatives to the polls, since the fall of Roe, it has been driving Democrats to vote more than Republicans.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Virtually every single poll across any jurisdiction in the United States comes back with a similar result. Most people think that abortion should be available at least some, if not most of the time. That's true in very red states like Montana and Kentucky, very blue states like Vermont.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Doctors like Taylor and Goodrick are worried that state bans like Arizona's are just paving the way for a larger national play.\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the plan is for a national abortion ban. Real people, lives, are impacted by these policies.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who appointed three of the five Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe, had at one time supported a federal ban on abortion. He's now backtracking on that promise.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why should Americans trust your word that you would not do it now if you were reelected?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REP) (FMR. UNITED STATES PRESIDENT/PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Because we don't need it any longer, because we broke Roe v. Wade. And we did something that nobody thought was possible, we gave it back to the states. And it's working the way it's supposed to.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is an outright flip-flop with this Arizona decision. He's had to come out further and say that he actually doesn't think this Arizona law should stand, that it should be repealed and revised.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just said, the collection of state bans is, quote, "working the way it is supposed to."\par \par \uc2 RALLYGOERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Boo!\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democrats appear to be banking on the backlash to drive voters all across the country.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 This is 2024, not the 1800s. And we're not going back.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Arizona State Legislature was expected to swiftly repeal the law. Even Kari Lake, a Republican candidate for \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , recognizing this could be a lightning rod for voters.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF DIALOGUE\par \par \uc2 REP. KARI LAKE (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 What's really coming in harm's way is this mission on the ballot, so I think our lawmakers need to do something quickly.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But at the last minute, Republicans blocked that effort. Democrats say they will try to repeal the law again this week, but it could be voters who have the final say. An initiative to protect abortion rights is expected to be on the ballot here in November.\par \par \uc2 DR. GABRIELLE GOODRICK (OWNER & MEDICAL DIR./CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 This ballot initiative is gonna be successful here. Because the people of Arizona want people that can get pregnant to have bodily autonomy and get the Government out of the doctor/patient relationship.\par \par \uc2 PENELOPE (PATIENT/CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 I will be going through the steps to register to vote in Arizona, and it absolutely will impact how I vote.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion rights has won in all six states where it has appeared on the ballot so far. Does that give you hope?\par \par \uc2 DR. DESHAWN TAYLOR (CEO/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 I do have hope, but honestly, ballot initiative is not a solution. It's not a 50-state solution.\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHERYL CROW\par \par \uc2 BYRON PITTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 When we come back, Sheryl Crow sits down with my "Nightline" co-anchor Juju Chang and reveals what makes her happy.\par \par \uc2 MUSIC VIDEO CLIP FROM SHERYL CROW/"IF IT MAKES YOU HAPPY"\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020240418ek4g00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 2,468 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 IRAN, MISSILES, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , US, DRONES, KIRBY, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, ZAKARIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN ATTACKS ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 COHEN, TRUMP, TRIAL, DANIELS, BRAGG, JURY\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM SATURDAY\par \par \uc2 SUNUNU, TRUMP, TRIALS, 2024, RACE, VOTE, JANUARY 6\par \par \uc2 2024, AZ, ABORTION, BAN, HARRIS, TRUMP, GIBSON, TAYLOR, MAYES, STATES, BALLOT\par \par \uc2 SMITH, ABORTION, 2024, ROE, COMSTOCK, ACT, BIDEN, ELECTION, TRUMP, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, TRUMP, ARIZONA, ABORTION, BAN, TRIAL, 2024, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE MIKE JOHNSON (SPEAKER OF THE HOUSE)\par \par \uc2 With President Trump as our nominee in the party, we are very much looking forward to that historic day in November. Because we are going to grow the House majority. We're gonna win the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  and we're gonna win back the White House as well.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REP) (FMR. UNITED STATES PRESIDENT/PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We're getting along very well with the Speaker, and it's not, not an easy situation for any speaker. I think he's doing a very good job. He's doing about as good as you're going to do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Former President Trump, Mike Johnson, Speaker of the House, on Friday at Mar-a-Lago. Let's talk about this and many other things along on the Roundtable with former DNC Chair Donna Brazile, former RNC Chair, Trump White House Chief of Staff, Reince Priebus, the Executive Editor of the \uc2 Associated Press\uc2 , Julie Pace, and "\uc2 Washington Post\uc2 " Congressional reporter Mariana Sotomayor. And Mariana, let me begin with you. You cover Congress every single day. Speaker Johnson has been in some trouble. Got that lifeline from President Trump, is it enough?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP VOUCHES FOR JOHNSON: 'I STAND WITH THE SPEAKER'\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 We're about to find out this week. It's gonna be a consequential week for the Speaker as well as House Republicans. They were always going to tackle question of whether to send funding to Ukraine and Israel, given just the developments of the last 24 hours. It is imperative now for many House Republicans, who were trying to potentially delay that question, to address it. \uc2 Marjorie Taylor Greene\uc2  has said before that if Johnson sends any funding bill to Ukraine, that that is what's going to trigger this motion to vacate, even though Trump has already said, you know, "I stand with the Speaker. I think he's doing a good job in a very tough situation." We're really gonna see all of this play out by the end of the week.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you think he ended it?\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think so. I think two things. One, Republicans almost all of us, understand that getting rid of Speaker Johnson is complete stupidity, number one. And the Republicans would risk losing the House Majority. And third, I think we've had enough of the circus in the House with this stuff, and President Trump knows it. His campaign knows it. And that's why he's putting a lid on it.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What a week in abortion politics, Donna Brazile, with that decision from the Arizona Supreme Court. Is this the magic bullet the Democrats believe it is?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA HIGH COURT RULES IN FAVOR OF STRICT ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's something that all women should be concerned about. George, I've never heard from my nieces the way I've heard from them over the last couple of months, 'cause they live in the south, and where, where will women go when their IVF is banned? When they are worried about birth control, when they're worried about whether or not, if something, God forbid, is to happen, could they receive medical care?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMS HOP ABORTION GALVANIZES VOTERS IN POST-ROE AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Is it a galvanizing issue for Americans who can, who are concerned about reproductive rights and freedom? Absolutely. Will Democrats make sure that those victims, those women who are having these horrifying experiences get to tell their story? Absolutely. And who's responsible? \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He owns it. He brags about it and we're gonna remind the American people.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The former president thought he put this behind him by coming out of this, by coming up with this states' rights solution according to him.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SAYS 'STATES WILL DETERMINE' ABORTION LAWS\par \par \uc2 JULIE PACE (ASSOCIATED PRESS EXECUTIVE EDITOR)\par \par \uc2 Well, the, the timing is remarkable because just a few days later you see what happens when you leave this issue to the states, which is what he says he wants to do. And you have a state that take this position, which is objectively far outside of the mainstream of where most Americans are, even those who support restrictions on, on abortion, and then to have it happen in a state that is going to be so consequential to this election. And I think if you look at the map that you showed earlier, of where the politics and where voters have been on this, you know, really they have come down on one side over the course of the last several months, which is on upholding rights for, for abortions.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You have seen two elections in a row where this abortion issue seemed to really repelled Democrats, Reince.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME REPUBLICANS BACKTRACK ON ABORTION AHEAD OF ELECTION\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a lifeline to the Democrats. There's no doubt about it. And Republicans have not been able to get themselves out of the mud. I think President Trump did take the, the - the position that he had to take, and Republicans have to do a better job of winning the hearts and minds of these voters. Because where the Democrats have had success is convincing people that any regulation on abortion is an affront to their civil rights when 80 percent of the American people believe that abortion in a third trimester is wrong.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sixty-six percent off the American people think abortion after the first trimester is wrong. That's where Republicans need to be. But until they can get their message together, this has been a lifeline to the Democrats. And I think President Trump, what you saw, is that he understood it, and he wanted to move on from it.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, it's punishment. When a, when a 12 or 13-year-old...\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the third trimester.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When a 12 or 13-year-old girl, who didn't know she was pregnant, is raped, is raped...\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're talking about the third trimester here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW WILL FIGHT OVER ABORTION RIGHTS IMPACT THE 2024 ELECTION?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You want to get third, second trimester? Let women make this decision. Trust women to make this decision.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So what...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this is not a Democrat or Republican. This is an American freedom issue for women.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We fought for this right to be able to make a decision based on our own bodies.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Donna, here's the question...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you wanna get into the technicality. That's it. You men want to tell us what to do with our bodies.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No. No.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You want to tell us how long our period should last. You want to tell us how long we should be pregnant, where we can go if we need IVF treatment. No, I'm hearing it. Now, thank God that I'm not Sarah in the Bible. She had a baby in her 60s. So, I, I am grateful that I'm beyond those ages, but I am concerned that my nieces are being given less rights to choose and to go back to an 1860 era when my great-grandmother barely just got her freedom. Hell no. We're not going back.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nobody, okay, right.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this is gonna be like a MAGA movement. It's a movement where women are sick and tired of men telling us what to do with our bodies.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. No, no one wants to go back to 1864. But the question for Democrats are...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, the Arizona Supreme Court just did it.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you're going back.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The question for Democrats is, at what point should there be a regulation? Is it halfway through the pregnancy? Is it two-thirds? Is there any place in this conversation where there is a moment in time that abortion should be regulated?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Her health should be the priority. Her health! Reince, what's so hard about the health of a woman?\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so...\par \par \uc2 JULIE PACE (ASSOCIATED PRESS EXECUTIVE EDITOR)\par \par \uc2 right now, though...\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...their health. So, 30th week...\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The health.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Julie?\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...is it a health issue?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The health of a woman.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Julie, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 JULIE PACE (ASSOCIATED PRESS EXECUTIVE EDITOR)\par \par \uc2 The challenge that Republicans have right now is that when you do look at polls, you're, you're right, there are, the majority of Americans supports, are, are opened to some restrictions. But you're talking about third trimester and you look at Florida, six-week ban. You look at what happened in Arizona.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) True.\par \par \uc2 JULIE PACE (ASSOCIATED PRESS EXECUTIVE EDITOR)\par \par \uc2 These are positions that are outside of the, the, the, where most Americans are right now.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Republicans have not been able to get out of the ditch on this issue because they're framing it in these early stages, and they're not finding a position that the majority of Americans support.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You see anything happening in Congress this year on this, or is this all about November?\par \par \uc2 MARIANNA SOTOMAYOR (WASHINGTON POST CONGRESSIONAL REPORTER)\par \par \uc2 No. I mean, Republicans especially in the House, who have the majority have been saying for a long time, since the moment that they did not win in 2020 with the bigger margins that they thought they would, we cannot have a vote on any kind of federal legislation on abortion because they will lose the majority.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Julie, we enter a new world tomorrow. First former president ever to face a criminal trial. What should we expect?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST OF FOUR TRUMP CRIMINAL TRIALS SET TO BEGIN MONDAY\par \par \uc2 JULIE PACE (ASSOCIATED PRESS EXECUTIVE EDITOR)\par \par \uc2 It's pretty remarkable. We're gonna go through this procedural act of selecting a jury, and, and something that many of us have sat through, being on a jury before, and yet it's going to be for a trial of a former president of the United States. We've literally never seen this before. And Trump is gonna use this courtroom and other courtrooms to come as really the center piece of his campaign. It's worked for him through the primary. I think the question now will be, how that sliver of Moderate voters, that sliver of persuadable voters will react to seeing him in this setting.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's what I don't (PH) want to bring to Reince. Reince, do you believe the former president needs either an acquittal or a mistrial? Or, do you think a conviction won't matter either?\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think in this case, in particular, it's the most political case of them all, and I think people see that. The - US Attorney didn't take it, previous DA didn't take it, \uc2 Federal Election Commission\uc2  didn't move forward with it. And it only takes one juror. And the question that I don't think a lot of people are talking about is (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, but that's what I'm asking you. I, I understand, I understand what happens if there's a mistrial.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If it's...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, and I understand what happens if he's acquitted. I think you're right then. Both of those could potentially help him politically. I'm asking you about a conviction.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I don't think in this particular case it's gonna move much. But again, when there's only 100,000 people deciding the outcome of an election, I don't think anyone can say with definitive proof, one way or the other.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Donna?\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I think all of these trials are important, and this is the first time, we've never been here before, George. I don't know the playbook. But I understand that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is gonna come out every day and just, you know, try to, you know, pour hot water on, on the proceedings. Look, I, I don't want to get into the lurid details of what may or may not have happened, and what records might have been falsified, but to have a sitting president of the United States in court for three or four days a week when you should be out there meeting the voters, talking to the people about the issues that, that they're concerned about, that is a loss, a net loss.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's why Joe Biden is making tremendous gains in the polls. Not enough to overtake anybody, but enough to show that he's ready to compete.\par \par \uc2 REINCE PRIEBUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He can compete all day.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Completely uncharted territory.\par \par \uc2 DONNA BRAZILE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank God.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you all very much. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That is all for us today. Thanks for sharing part your Sunday with us. Check out "World News Tonight," and I'll see you tomorrow on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK: DOWNLOAD THE APP\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020240419ek4e00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MINNESOTA SEN. TINA SMITH ON ABORTION RIGHTS AND THE ELECTION DEMS HOPE ABORTION GALVANIZES VOTERS IN POST-ROE AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 902 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 IRAN, MISSILES, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , US, DRONES, KIRBY, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, ZAKARIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN ATTACKS ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 COHEN, TRUMP, TRIAL, DANIELS, BRAGG, JURY\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM SATURDAY\par \par \uc2 SUNUNU, TRUMP, TRIALS, 2024, RACE, VOTE, JANUARY 6\par \par \uc2 2024, AZ, ABORTION, BAN, HARRIS, TRUMP, GIBSON, TAYLOR, MAYES, STATES, BALLOT\par \par \uc2 SMITH, ABORTION, 2024, ROE, COMSTOCK, ACT, BIDEN, ELECTION, TRUMP, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're joined now by Senator \uc2 Tina Smith\uc2  of Minnesota. Thank you for joining us this morning, Senator. You know, we just heard what's happening in Arizona based on this Comstock law. You're leading an effort in the House to repeal it. Any prospects for success?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MINNESOTA SEN. TINA SMITH ON ABORTION RIGHTS AND THE ELECTION\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, first of all, I just want to say, George, that American women are not gonna be conned by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his comments about abortion. We know that he is the one who is responsible for what's going on in Arizona and all over the country. So, that's the bottom line, I think, as we think about the election coming up. With regard to the Comstock Act, okay, so this is a 150-year-old law that has been long relegated to the dust bin of history, and yet we can see Trump judges and even the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2  raising this up as a reason why people shouldn't be able to get medication abortion through the mail.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMS HOPE ABORTION GALVANIZES VOTERS IN POST-ROE AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 So, we have to pay attention to this and make sure that we are doing everything that we can to protect people's rights to make their own decisions about their own bodies and their own lives.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is there anything more that President Biden could be doing now with executive action to protect those rights?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 I'm really grateful that the President has done everything that he possibly can to protect people's rights, and he's fighting right now to make sure that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's authority to make decisions about whether medications like Mifepristone are, that, that their decision-making is what rules and not the decision of some Trump judge from Texas, which is what's happening before the Supreme Court right now. So, I think that they're doing everything that they can. What we need to do is to win these elections so that we can put the protections of Roe in law.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW WILL FIGHT OVER ABORTION RIGHTS IMPACT 2024 ELECTION?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You, you say that the American people will not be conned by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but his position now is relatively clear, isn't it, saying this should be a state by state issue?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SAYS 'STATES WILL DETERMINE' ABORTION LAWS\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 Well, so think about what that means exactly. First of all, he said that he is the person who is proudly responsible for overturning Roe. That is what has caused all of this chaos and cruelty to the one in three American women who live in states where abortion is now basically banned. The other thing he said just a couple of days ago is that these state bans are working the way they should. So, ask a woman in Arizona or Texas whether she thinks this is working for her because for her, this isn't a political discussion.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 This is about her personal life and her decisions that she can make for herself about her own life. So, I think that his position is totally clear. He is responsible for these abortion bans, and I think he's gonna be held accountable for that come the election in November.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Given what you think is the power of this issue and everything else we've seen over the course of this election, how do you explain the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is either tied or ahead of President Biden in most polls?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, there's so much talk about these polls right now. I've been working, you know, I started out in politics working as an organizer and going door to door, talking to my community, and so, I know that what matters is the choice that people are faced with when they actually cast their vote, and that is what's gonna make all the difference in the world. And on this issue, on the issue of abortion rights, the choice couldn't be more clear, right? You have \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  who are fighting to protect people's freedom, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was responsible for taking it away.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator Smith, thank you for your time this morning.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR TINA SMITH (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Roundtable's up next. We're back in a moment.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Roundtable's here. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM FRIDAY\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020240419ek4e00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA'S BAN PUTS ABORTION CENTER STAGE IN CAMPAIGN VP HARRIS BLASTS TRUMP OVER ABORTION DURING ARIZONA TRIP\b0\par\par\uc2 793 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 IRAN, MISSILES, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , US, DRONES, KIRBY, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, ZAKARIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN ATTACKS ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 COHEN, TRUMP, TRIAL, DANIELS, BRAGG, JURY\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM SATURDAY\par \par \uc2 SUNUNU, TRUMP, TRIALS, 2024, RACE, VOTE, JANUARY 6\par \par \uc2 2024, AZ, ABORTION, BAN, HARRIS, TRUMP, GIBSON, TAYLOR, MAYES, STATES, BALLOT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Arizona Supreme Court's decision to uphold a near total ban abortion sent shockwaves across the country. Rachel Scott was on the ground in Arizona, has the latest on the fallout for the 2024 elections.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA'S BAN PUTS ABORTION CENTER STAGE IN 2024 CAMPAIGN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's already one of the most closely watched Arizona battleground states but a consequential ruling in Arizona upholding 160-year-old near total ban on abortion now putting the issue at the center of the 2024 race.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 This is 2024, not the 1800s, and we're not going back.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democrats trying to seize momentum, putting these billboards up around the state. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  once bound to sign a federal abortion ban, but now he says it's not necessary.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why should Americans trust your word that you would not do it now if you were reelected?\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REP) (FMR. UNITED STATES PRESIDENT/PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Because we don't need it any longer because we broke Roe v. Wade and we did something that nobody thought was possible. We gave it back to the states, and it's working the way it's supposed to.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS BLASTS TRUMP OVER ABORTION DURING ARIZONA TRIP\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  firing back, saying Trump cleared the way for 21 states to ban or restrict access to abortion by appointing three of the five Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just said the collection of state bans is, quote, "working the way it is supposed to."\par \par \uc2 RALLYGOERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Boo!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP ON ABORTION: 'WE GAVE IT BACK' TO THE STATES\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump has acknowledged abortion was a losing issue for Republicans in the midterm. And despite saying the issue should be left up to the states, Trump on Friday also writing in a social media post that the Arizona ruling went too far, and calling on state leaders to remedy what has happened.\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA HOUSE REPRESENTATIVE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Shame on you!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA HIGH COURT RULES IN FAVOR OF STRICT ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Arizona State Legislature was expected to swiftly repeal the law, but Republicans blocked that effort. Doctors describing chaos and confusion.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JILL GIBSON (CHIEF MEDICAL DIRECTOR/PLANNED PARENTHOOD ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 I'm having patients who have received abortions last week call and say, "Am I still gonna be able to receive my follow-up care?"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Providers who perform abortions could face up to five years in prison.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is there a sense of fear among abortion providers?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DESHAWN TAYLOR (OWNER/DESERT STAR INSTITUTE FOR FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 I, I would say undoubtedly. I didn't go to medical school to go to jail.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona's Democratic Attorney General, Kris Mayes, says she won't enforce the law, but concedes she can't stop local prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (DEM) (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 I would urge Arizonans who are pregnant to make a plan, and I can't believe I'm having to say that. But it's time to make a plan for 60 days from now. If something goes wrong, if you need an abortion, if you want an abortion, start thinking about California and Nevada and New Mexico or Colorado.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UP TO 14 STATES COULD HAVE ABORTION BALLOT MEASURES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES WITH ABORTION ACCESS ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now voters could ultimately decide this issue in November when Arizona and as many as 13 other states have abortion measures on the ballot, including in Florida, where a six-week ban is set to become law on May 1st. Abortion rights has won in all six states where it has been on the ballot, including Conservative states like Ohio, Kansas, and Kentucky.\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (DEM) (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 I will promise you this, the people of Arizona are gonna make sure that this 1864 ban is buried forever in November when they pass a ballot initiative to enshrine abortion rights in our Constitution.\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020240419ek4e00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA SUPREME COURT ABORTION BAN THE IMPACT THE DECISION IS HAVING ON POLITICAL RACE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,135 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS: SYDNEY STABBINGS\par \par \uc2 STABBING, MALL, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, TEHRAN, MISSILES, ATTACK, WARNING\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, TRUMP, SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 BUS, HONOLULU, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, CARJACKING, POLICE\par \par \uc2 TEEN, OFFICER, SHOT, FAKE, GUN, FAMILY\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, BOND\par \par \uc2 DOW, S&P, STOCKS, INFLATION, MIDEAST\par \par \uc2 INMATE, NORTHWESTERN, LAW, MCKINLEY\par \par \uc2 HARPER, PARKS, ARIZONA, ABORTION, POLITICS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We start this half hour with a closer look at the top political headlines this week, and joining us, our Deputy Political Director, Averi Harper and from Pittsburgh, ABC White House Correspondent Maryalice Parks. Good morning, to you both, always great to have you. So, Averi, let's start with you and that Arizona Supreme Court decision, going back to this anti-abortion law from the 1800s. Democrats really trying to use this as a top campaign issue.\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, it's no surprise that Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  was in the state yesterday. She was condemning Trump's abortion stance. She called him the architect of the healthcare crisis that we've seen after the overturning of Roe versus Wade. She urged Arizonans to come out and vote to restore reproductive rights in the state of Arizona. You have to remember, Arizona is one of 14 states where we could see abortion on the ballot and that could have huge political implications. We know Arizona is a battleground state on the presidential level. There's also a Senate race that's very competitive there and so, abortion could be an issue that drives voters to come out to the polls in a way that Democrats are hoping can help them score some wins up and down the ballot.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION BAN. \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  CALLS TO "REMEDY WHAT HAS HAPPENED"\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And because of that, I want to bring in Maryalice now. Maryalice, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's position on abortion, he is walking a very fine line as he tries to find a winning message on the issue, and our Rachel Scott really tried to push him on this.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's right. In recent election cycles, we've talked about whether Republicans have a Trump problem. Well, on abortion, Trump seems to have a Republican problem. I mean, look, he promised, going into his first term, that he was going to appoint anti-abortion judges, and yesterday we heard him again really brag about the fact that he did that. He said they successfully broke Roe V Wade. He said that it was working brilliantly, that the states were doing exactly what they were supposed to do. I mean, voters, we have seen over and over, really disagree and reject that idea.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as he was talking, I felt like I could hear Democrats starting to cut new ads. Plus, when he was pushed by our Rachel Scott about whether he would sign a national abortion ban, like he's talked about in the past, he tried to distance himself, but he was standing next to Republican House Speaker Mike Johnson, who recently has said that he wouldn't pursue a national ban, but has for years been a co-sponsor of legislation that would put in place a national abortion ban. I mean, House Speaker Mike Johnson also his name on a bill called the Life at Conception Act that if passed would really question the constitutionality of even ivf. So you're going to see Democrats in the lead-up to November continuing to hammer this question, if Republicans keep the House, if Trump wins, do they really think that Trump would veto a national ban if Republicans sent it to him.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S HUSH MONEY TRIAL BEGINS MONDAY. FORMER PRESIDENT'S FIRST CRIMINAL TRIAL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And while we're speaking of Former President Trump, Averi, let's go back to you because jury selection for his hush money trial is set to begin on Monday. How do we expect all of this to play out politically this week?\par \par \uc2 AVERI HARPER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, as this hush money trial gets under way, the courthouse really does become the campaign trail for Former President Trump, and we're going to see him try and take advantage of that. You know, yesterday in Florida he was asked about this trial. He said that all of his legal troubles are a witch hunt, he claimed, with zero evidence, that this is a method of election interference. And that's really a callout to his supporters, not only for them to support him in November, but to give to his campaign in the meantime. We know that millions of dollars of campaign donations have been used to pay for his legal bills. What remains to be seen is if this is going to expand his base in any way.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN ADMINISTRATION CANCELS MORE STUDENT DEBT. AFFECTS SOME 277,000 BORROWERS OWING $7.4 BILLION\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And while we're talking about how things play out politically, Maryalice, what about the current president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's administration announcement that it's canceling another round of student debt, affecting more than a quarter of a million borrowers, nearly 300,000 Americans waking up to emails that their loans were wiped clean.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, I think politically, this depends on how well they message it. I mean, I have talked to a lot of young voters who still view student loan debt forgiveness as a broken campaign promise. They feel like President Biden fell short, hasn't done enough. I mean, he actually has done, arguably, quite a lot. Even after the court struck down his first plan, he has, through more targeted programs, offered over $150 billion in relief, like you said, to over four million Americans. That's roughly one in ten of those Americans that hold student loan debt, so I think that if more and more Americans start to feel this, that will make a difference politically. I mean, obviously, Janai, it is controversial, there are some Americans that don't agree with the idea of forgiving student loan debt. But, look, the President needs to shore up those young voters. We have seen recent polling averages from FiveThirtyEight that show that his margin there has really dipped with young voters. And so this is definitely a play to make sure that he feels like he can say he's delivering on those campaign promises. Guys.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of work to be done by both candidates. Ladies, thank you both for being with us this morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240507ek4d0000d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT HARRIS VISITS ARIZONA BLAMES DONALD TRUMP FOR STATE'S NEW ABORTION RULING\b0\par\par\uc2 525 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS: SYDNEY STABBINGS\par \par \uc2 STABBING, MALL, ATTACK\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, TEHRAN, MISSILES, ATTACK, WARNING\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, TRUMP, SPEAKER\par \par \uc2 BUS, HONOLULU, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, CARJACKING, POLICE\par \par \uc2 TEEN, OFFICER, SHOT, FAKE, GUN, FAMILY\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, BOND\par \par \uc2 DOW, S&P, STOCKS, INFLATION, MIDEAST\par \par \uc2 INMATE, NORTHWESTERN, LAW, MCKINLEY\par \par \uc2 HARPER, PARKS, ARIZONA, ABORTION, POLITICS\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, JAILHOUSE, RANT, PHONE, SENTENCING\par \par \uc2 SPRING, SALES, TAX, RETAILERS\par \par \uc2 FROZONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 STABBING, AUSTRALIA, ALBANESE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, BIDEN, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. OFFICIALS: IRAN COULD BE SET TO ATTACK ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEHRAN SAID TO HAVE READIED MORE THAN 100 CRUISE MISSILES\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, ABORTION, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT HARRIS VISITS ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLAMES DONALD TRUMP FOR STATE'S NEW ABORTION RULING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, now to the presidential race and the renewed focus on abortion restrictions following that Arizona Supreme Court ruling.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  out front on this, telling voters former President Trump wants to take America back to the 1800s. ABC's senior White House correspondent Selina Wang is in Washington with more. Selina, good morning.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Whit, good morning to you. Vice President Harris, she is directly blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for Arizona's new abortion ruling. That battleground state upholding that 160-year-old law that bans abortion in all cases except to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, doctors and women across Arizona, they are left scrambling, anxious and confused. And the Vice President, she has a simple message that this is all \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's fault. She's blaming Trump for creating a health care crisis by appointing justices who overturned Roe versus Wade and warning that a second Trump term would mean more bans, more suffering, less freedom and that Trump won't stop until abortion is banned nationwide. Now, Democrats, they are betting that abortion is going to galvanize voters to the polls in November with a majority of Americans saying that it should be legal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Trump, he is well aware of the politics here and now saying that Arizona went too far. But that ban, it is set to go into effect in Arizona unless Republicans there repeal it. But ultimately, this could be left up to the voters there with abortion rights expected to be on the ballot in November. Guys?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Selina Wang for us, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 4 MINUTES, WHAT IS ARFID?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up, in our "GMA Morning Menu," "GMA" sitting down with the 8-year-old opening up on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  about her rare eating disorder and what parents need to know about the condition.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 12 MINUTES, DEALS & STEALS!\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, "Deals & Steals." Tory Johnson in the house ready to spruce up your home without breaking the bank. And florals, florals for spring. Gio is in DC.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240507ek4d0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN VP HARRIS TO VISIT STATE AS DEMOCRATS TRY TO TIE ISSUE TO TRUMP\b0\par\par\uc2 627 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS THE DEATH OF OJ SIMPSON\par \par \uc2 SIMPSON, DEATH, TRIAL, BROWN, GOLDMAN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, WINDS, TORNADO\par \par \uc2 MIDEAST, TENSIONS, EMBASSY, IRAN, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 WRAY, FISA, CONGRESS, RENEW, TERRORISM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HARRIS, MAYES, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Pierre, thank you for that. We're going to turn now to the battle over abortion rights. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is heading to Arizona after court decisions sent shock waves through the country upholding an 1864 law banning abortions with almost no exceptions. Our chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce has that story for us this morning. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS TO VISIT STATE AS DEMOCRATS TRY TO TIE ISSUE TO TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Well, the Biden campaign this morning is trying to seize the political momentum here as we see outrage and turmoil over Arizona's near total abortion ban. And now the White House today is dispatching their chief messenger on this issue, Vice President Harris.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning President Biden's re-election campaign leaning into the political fight over abortion after Arizona upheld a 160-year-old law banning abortion in all cases except to protect the life of the mother. The Biden campaign relying on a simple message, arguing this is all \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's fault.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Democrats already putting up these billboards saying abortion is banned in Arizona thanks to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He won't stop until it's banned nationwide.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 It does not have to be this way.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) During a visit to the critical battleground state today, the Vice President will flatly say that Trump is to blame, calling him "The architect of this health care crisis," for bragging about appointing the Justices who overturned Roe V. Wade. Harris saying a second Trump term would mean "More bans, more suffering, less freedom."\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With the vast majority of Americans saying abortion should be legal in all or most cases, the Biden campaign is hoping the issue will drive voters to the polls in November. But in the meantime, women and health care providers across Arizona are left scrambling.\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 We're talking about asking doctors to send women out to the parking lots and wait until they're almost dead before the doctor can provide care? That is insane. That is the very definition of insanity.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Our Rachel Scott speaking to Arizona's Democratic Attorney General who urged the state's legislature to swiftly repeal the Civil War era law, but Republicans blocked the effort. Her message now?\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 I would urge Arizonans who are pregnant to make a plan, and I can't believe I'm having to say that. But it's time to make plan for 60 days from now if something goes wrong, if you need an abortion, if you want an abortion, start thinking about California and Nevada and New Mexico or Colorado.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now ultimately voters could decide this issue in November when Arizona, and as many as 13 other states, could have abortion measures on the ballot. In fact just this morning ABC confirming that organizers in Colorado now say they have enough signatures to put the measure on the ballot there. In the meantime this ban in Arizona is set to take effect in the coming weeks unless Republicans there change course and agree to repeal it. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240504ek4c00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES OFFICER AND TEENAGER DIE IN SHOOTOUT/CHILDREN LEFT HOME ALONE\b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUCK, CRASH, PARKER, RUIZ, KENJURA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORM SWEEPS INTO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, BIDEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PRESSED ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ABORTION BAN, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 CARJACKING, MANHUNT, LEMMA, DE AGUASVIVAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: URGENT CARJACKING MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTOUT, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICER AND TEENAGER DIE IN SHOOTOUT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, new details about a deadly police shootout in Memphis.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities say officers were responding to a call about a suspicious vehicle. An 18-year-old suspect opening fire as they approached. An officer and the alleged gunman both killed in that shootout. Two other officers and a 17-year-old in the car were wounded.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN LEFT HOME ALONE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A mother in Houston is facing charges for allegedly leaving her two young children home alone while she went on a cruise.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities say Lakesha Woods Williams abandoned her 8-year-old son and 6-year-old daughter for days while she went on vacation. Deputies finding the children in a filthy apartment during a wellness check. They say the mother left a web camera and a cell phone, so she could check in on them.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, the former interpreter accused of stealing millions of dollars from Dodgers star Shohei Ohtani makes his first appearance in federal court. And remembering a legendary news anchor.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUCK, CRASH, PARKER, RUIZ, KENJURA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORM SWEEPS INTO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, BIDEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PRESSED ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ABORTION BAN, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 CARJACKING, MANHUNT, LEMMA, DE AGUASVIVAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: URGENT CARJACKING MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTOUT, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICER AND TEENAGER DIE IN SHOOTOUT\par \par \uc2 MIZUHARA, THEFT, OHTANI, MEASLES, MACNEIL, CAVALLI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" now, the former interpreter accused of stealing over $16 million from Dodgers star Shohei Ohtani appearing in federal court today in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ippei Mizuhara charged with bank fraud. He's accused of using the money to cover millions in gambling loses. The judge releasing him on bond, ordering him not to have any contact with Ohtani and barring him from gambling or going to casinos. The judge also ordered him to receive treatment for a gambling addiction.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, a new CDC warning about measles outbreaks across the US.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At least 121 cases report in 17 states so far this year. Because of vaccinations, measles had been considered eliminated in the US nearly 25 years ago. The CDC says the rapid increase in cases could threaten that status. 95% of the cases this year were patients not fully vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROBERTO CAVALLI, 1940-2024\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Two passings to note tonight. We learned today famed Italian fashion designer Roberto Cavalli has died.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One the biggest names in fashion, his distinctive trademark style both flamboyant and glamorous. His flashy creations attracting celebrity fans for decades. The company bearing his name playing tribute to a, quote, "life lived with love." Roberto Cavalli was 83.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROBERT MACNEIL, 1931-2024\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And legendary news anchor Robert MacNeil has died.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A giant in the industry, co-founder of what is now "The PBS Newshour," anchoring his own show before partnering with Jim Lehrer for the long-running "MacNeil-Lehrer Report." His career defined by dedication and commitment to journalism. Robert MacNeil was 93.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, who says penguins can't fly? The proof still ahead.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POLICE: URGENT CARJACKING MANHUNT OFFICIALS ASK FOR PUBLIC'S HELP TO CATCH SUSPECTS\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUCK, CRASH, PARKER, RUIZ, KENJURA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORM SWEEPS INTO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, BIDEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PRESSED ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ABORTION BAN, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 CARJACKING, MANHUNT, LEMMA, DE AGUASVIVAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: URGENT CARJACKING MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to that deadly carjacking north of Orlando.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities releasing video showing a masked man carrying a weapon, getting into the back seat of a white dodge Durango. The victim, a 31-year-old woman, now believed dead.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, an urgent search underway for multiple suspects. Here's ABC's Erielle Reshef.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS ASK FOR PUBLIC'S HELP TO CATCH SUSPECTS\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the urgent manhunt in central Florida for this masked gunman, caught in terrifying video appearing to carjack an SUV in broad daylight, now suspected of killing the woman who was inside.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF DENNIS LEMMA (SEMINOLE COUNTY FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 This wasn't just a random incident, a horrible, horrible frightening situation.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the height of rush hour, around 5:00 PM yesterday, the driver of this dodge Durango called her husband to say she was being followed by a green Acura, which rammed her back bumper. Later, the armed assailant is seen exiting that car, pointing a gun at the driver.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF DENNIS LEMMA (SEMINOLE COUNTY FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Tells her, we suspect, "Unlock the door," which she does. He jumps in the rear passenger seat behind the driver.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities say that vehicle took backroads to a new construction site. Witnesses reported hearing gunshots and seeing smoke from the SUV set ablaze.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF DENNIS LEMMA (SEMINOLE COUNTY FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 One person was deceased and found in that vehicle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The victim believed to be 31-year-old Katherine Altagracia Guerrero de Aguasvivas. Law enforcement now searching multiple suspects.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Authorities believe the victim may have been targeted, and they're asking anyone with information to come forward. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A truly disturbing case. Erielle, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FISA SPY PROGRAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE RENEWS SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And today on Capitol Hill, the House of Representatives voted to reauthorize a key law in the fight against terrorism after Donald Trump called on Republicans to kill it.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is section 702 of the so-called FISA law. It allows US intelligence agencies to spy on the communications of foreign nationals without a warrant. It passed after a compromise authorizing it for just two years, pushing any further debate into a possible Trump presidency if he were to win.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, the deadly police shoot-out in Memphis. An officer, an 18-year-old suspect both killed, two other officers wounded. And the mother facing charges for allegedly leaving her children home alone while she went on a cruise.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP\uc2  PRESSED ON ABORTION FMR. PRESIDENT: "WE BROKE ROE V. WADE"\b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUCK, CRASH, PARKER, RUIZ, KENJURA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORM SWEEPS INTO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, BIDEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PRESSED ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back here in the US, and the abortion battle front and center in the race for the White House. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  taking questions at Mar-a-Lago today. Our Rachel Scott asking the former President where he stands on abortion rights. Here's Rachel with how he responded.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FMR. PRESIDENT: "WE BROKE ROE V. WADE"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  telling me that though he once vowed to sign a federal abortion ban, it's now no longer necessary as he once again took credit for the Supreme Court's decision overturning Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) While you were in office, you said that you would sign a federal abortion ban if Congress send it to your desk. Why should Americans trust your word that you would not do it now if you were re-elected?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Because we don't need it any longer because we broke Roe v. Wade. And we did something that nobody thought was possible, we gave it back to the states.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump's about-face comes as he acknowledges abortion is now a losing issue for Republicans at the ballot box.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION OR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS COULD BE ON BALLOT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It will now be on the ballot on as many as 14 states this year, including several crucial battlegrounds. Over the years, Trump has taken positions on both sides of the issue.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm very pro-choice. I'm pro-life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today I asked where he stands right now. He would not say.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FMR. PRESIDENT: "THE STATES ARE WORKING VERY BRILLIANTLY"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Over the last few decades, Mr. President, you have both considered yourself pro-choice and pro-life, which one is it?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know exactly which one it is. And when I was in New York and when I was a Democrat also, just like \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , you know, \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  was a Democrat. We sort of followed a very similar path. But if you look at what we've done with Roe v. Wade, we did something that everyone said couldn't be done, and we got it done.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  standing next to embattled Speaker of the House Mike Johnson, who is facing threats to his leadership. It's a strong show of support from the former president. In the past, Johnson has endorsed a federal ban on abortion. Today, he did not address the issue. And, Whit, remember, Trump's first criminal trial begins on Monday. Today, the former president said he would testify. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG LEAP OF PENGUINS\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUCK, CRASH, PARKER, RUIZ, KENJURA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORM SWEEPS INTO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, BIDEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PRESSED ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ABORTION BAN, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 CARJACKING, MANHUNT, LEMMA, DE AGUASVIVAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: URGENT CARJACKING MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTOUT, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICER AND TEENAGER DIE IN SHOOTOUT\par \par \uc2 MIZUHARA, THEFT, OHTANI, MEASLES, MACNEIL, CAVALLI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 GREGORY, "SECRETS OF THE PENGUINS"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, call it the leap of the penguins. The surprising cliff dive seen on camera for the first time.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What you're about to see has never before been captured on video. At just 6 months old, these emperor penguin chicks marching to the ocean, crowding the edge of a 50-foot cliff in west Antarctica.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM DOCUSERIES, "SECRETS OF THE PENGUINS"\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (PHOTOGRAPHER NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC)\par \par \uc2 What on Earth is going on here?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) About 700 of them. Hesitating at first until one brave chick takes the plunge, splashing into the icy waters below.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (PHOTOGRAPHER NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC)\par \par \uc2 I cannot believe that. He's made it.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then, one by one and in groups, they jump.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (PHOTOGRAPHER NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC)\par \par \uc2 Here they go, here they go.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This first-of-its-kind footage captured just a few months ago by National Geographic photographer Bertie Gregory.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (PHOTOGRAPHER NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC)\par \par \uc2 I've only ever seen emperors jump in off the sea ice, and that's a couple of feet maximum.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Scientists say it's another sign of their resilience as sea ice continues to decline. The rite of passage known as fledging, their first trip from their colony to the ocean.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (PHOTOGRAPHER NATIONAL GEOGRAPHIC)\par \par \uc2 How's that for your first swimming lesson?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And these heroic high dives captured for the first time for all of us to enjoy.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just incredible images. The feature docuseries, "Secrets of the Penguins," and additional Earth Month content is available on our parent company's streaming platform \uc2 Disney\uc2 +. Thanks so much for watch tonight. I'm Whit Johnson in New York. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLE OVER ABORTION VP HARRIS TAKES ON TRUMP AFTER AZ NEAR-TOTAL BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUCK, CRASH, PARKER, RUIZ, KENJURA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORM SWEEPS INTO NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 IRAN, ISRAEL, BIDEN, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PRESSED ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ABORTION BAN, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Arizona tonight, just days after that court decision upholding a civil war-era ban on abortions. The Vice President blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the chaos, saying a second Trump term would be worse. Here's ABC's chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS TAKES ON TRUMP AFTER AZ NEAR-TOTAL BAN\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President Harris tonight touching down in what is now ground zero in the debate over reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Here in Arizona, they have turned the clock back to the 1800s to take away a woman's most fundamental right, the right to make decisions about her own body.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just days after the critical battleground state upheld a 160-year-old law banning abortion in all cases, except to protect the life of the mother, Harris, the Biden campaign's chief messenger on abortion, hammering a simple message, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  did this.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Just minutes ago, standing beside Speaker Johnson, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just said, the collection of state bans is, quote, "working the way it is supposed to."\par \par \uc2 CROWD (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Boo.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 And as much harm as he has already caused, a second Trump term would be even worse.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES THAT BAN OR RESTRICT ABORTION\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona one of 21 states to ban or severely restrict abortion rights since the supreme court overturned Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 This is 2024, not the 1800s. And we're not going back. We are not going back.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Biden campaign, hoping that the issue of abortion will drive voters to the polls in November, are going to do everything they can to get this message across. The Vice President tonight escalating her attacks, labeling these new restrictions in states across the country the, quote, "Trump abortion bans." Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce at the White House tonight, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the deadly crash. A stolen truck intentionally plowing into a Texas building. Powerful storms slamming northeast at this hour. And Israel bracing for an imminent attack from Iran that could come at any minute.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS: TRUCK CRASH INTO OFFICE INTENTIONAL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 First, the images coming in, a stolen tractor-trailer barreling its way through a Texas Public Safety Office. At least one person killed, more than a dozen injured. Authorities say the driver rammed the building on purpose. A deputy already chasing that stolen truck. What we're learning about the suspect and a possible motive. Marcus Moore at the scene.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWERFUL STORMS SLAM NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Heavy rain and strong winds up to 50 miles per hour hitting the northeast. Neighborhoods further south underwater. Cars washed away. Wind alerts from Georgia to Maine. Rob Marciano tracking it all.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRAN HAS 100+ MISSILES READY TO ATTACK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, tensions rising in the Middle East. Israel's iron dome intercepting dozens of rockets fired by \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 . At the same time, Israel bracing for a potential attack from Iran at any moment. The US warning Iran has more than 100 cruise missiles ready for a potential strike, retaliation for the deadly Israeli attack killing Iranian commanders in Syria. Britt Clennett in Israel. A high-stakes meeting at Mar-a-Lago. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Speaker Mike Johnson taking questions just moments ago. Rachel Scott pressing Trump on where he stands on abortion rights and how he responded.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS IN AZ TAKES ON TRUMP OVER ABORTION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Arizona's abortion battle in the national spotlight. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Arizona calling on lawmakers to repeal the state's 160-year-old abortion ban and blaming \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for the chaos surrounding the Supreme Court overturning Roe v. Wade. Mary Bruce at the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE: DEADLY CARJACKING MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Police searching for suspects wanted for a deadly carjacking in Florida. Chilling video shows an armed suspect wearing a mask, getting into the victim's SUV.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILDREN LEFT HOME ALONE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A mother in Texas facing charges, accused of leaving her two young children home alone while she went on a cruise.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROBERT MACNEIL 1931-2024\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tributes to legendary news anchor Robert MacNeil, the longtime anchor for \uc2 PBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA STRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the march of the penguins leading to a massive leap of faith and captured for the first time on video.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240416ek4c00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CHILI CRUNCH WARS FIGHT OVER WHO OWNS THE NAME OF POPULAR CONDIMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 957 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CHILI, WARS, CONDIMENT, OWNS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the food fight over a popular condiment with a top celebrity chef in the middle of it all. Eva Pilgrim is here with the chili crunch wars. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. This has really sparked a lot of feelings. People online criticizing David Chang's Momofuku for trying to trademark the word "chili crunch," saying it's like trying to own the word ketchup. But, Momofuku argued instead it's like trying to own the word "Heinz."\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a spicy showdown, a fight now sizzling over who owns the name of a popular Asian condiment.\par \par \uc2 DAVID CHANG (MOMOFUKU)\par \par \uc2 When I use chili crunch...\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Momofuku, founded by celebrity chef, David Chang, taking some heat for trying to trademark the name chili crunch.\par \par \uc2 @FORK_KNIFE (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This is not the way to go about trying to be better in business.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Chili crunch is a popular staple known to most as chili crisp. It's a roasted chili infused oil used on everything from fried eggs to ice cream. While Momofuku gained trademark right to chile crunch with an "E" last year, the food empire now trying to trademark chili crunch with an "I," sending out cease and desist letters to companies using that name. Michelle Tew, the founder of Homiah, a small business at makes a version of chili crisp that honors her Malaysian roots called Sambal Chili Crunch, received one of those letters.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE TEW (FOUNDER AND CEO HOMIAH)\par \par \uc2 I didn't think that he would trademark and actual product that anybody could make and anybody had the right to make.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Momofuku responding to the firestorm of heat online, telling ABC News, "Failure to defend our trademark against any size company would leave us without recourse against these larger players who often try to enter categories on the rise. Our intent has never been to stifle innovation in a category that we care deeply about. Our goal is and has been to find an amicable resolution."\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Momofuku saying they aren't trying to keep people from making or selling the much loved chili crisp, adding that when they created their product, they intentionally picked chili crunch as a name to differentiate it from the broader chili crisp category and to reflect the uniqueness of their brand. And you can see here, we've got a bunch of them sitting here at the desk. There's a lot in this category, many of them on shelves if you go to any Asian grocery store and even regular grocery stores these days. If you want more on this story, you can go to our website.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll be watching to see what happens with all that.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you (inaudible) spicy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12 INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN"\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Eva. Coming up in our "gma" Morning Menu, a big question for a lot of parents, what is going on in my teenager's brain? The answer is in our exclusive first look at a new documentary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:15 WNBA COMMISSIONER LIVE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, wnba commissioner, \uc2 Cathy Engelbert\uc2  joins us live to talk about the bright future of the women's game with stars like Caitlin Clark and Angel Reese days away from being drafted.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:43 BABY PENGUIN PLUNGE!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, look who's diving into Thursday. You don't want to miss more of these baby penguins taking the plunge.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21 DEALS AND STEALS SPRING BONANZA!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Tory Johnson is back with more "Deals & Steals." Hey, Tory.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael. Get ready to soak up the sun in our "Deals & Steals" spring bonanza. I've got terrific bargains for enjoying the outdoors, plus a must have for your next vacation, all starting at just 10 bucks. That's coming up right here on "gma."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, THURSDAY, APRIL 11\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BABY PENGUINS TAKE THE PLUNGE RARE CLIFF DIVING BEHAVIOR CAPTURED ON VIDEO FOR FIRST TIME EVER\b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CHILI, WARS, CONDIMENT, OWNS\par \par \uc2 "THE TEEN BRAIN", EXCLUSIVE, PARENTS, TEENS\par \par \uc2 ENGELBERT, WNBA, DRAFT\par \par \uc2 STOKE, CIPTON, SAND CLOUD, OUR PLACE, VINGLACE, ROSETTA STONE\par \par \uc2 BRED GOURMET\par \par \uc2 STEM CELL, DONOR, JEREMIAH, CRAFT, GIRALT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) teaser of this early in the show, baby penguins cliff diving captured on camera for the first time. Morgan Norwood has more of the story.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (NAT GEO EXPLORER)\par \par \uc2 This colony was about 10,000 strong, so a lot of noise, a lot of fun smells, and a lot of great characters. We spent two months camping alongside an emperor penguin colony.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nat Geo Explorer, Bertie Gregory has spent the last decade traveling to the far corners of the earth to capture creatures in the wild. This time, camping on the Antarctic peninsula to track a flock of baby penguins.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (NAT GEO EXPLORER)\par \par \uc2 The thing that gets my blood racing the most is the idea that if we just keep going around the next corner or the next corner, we might get to see something that no one has ever seen before.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that's just what happened...\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (NAT GEO EXPLORER)\par \par \uc2 It's called fledging when they take their first swim and normally, they jump off of sea ice, which is one or two feet high. We were noticing these trains of chicks were going past to a different place, so I launched the drone, flew it over there to see what was going on, and realized that they were stacking up at the edge of a huge 50 foot ice cliff. One by one, they started to jump off this 50 foot ice cliff and take their first swim in the southern ocean.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...for the first time ever, capturing this rare cliff diving behavior on video.\par \par \uc2 BERTIE GREGORY (NAT GEO EXPLORER)\par \par \uc2 They were falling and there were big chunks of ice floating in the water underneath them, so it's like falling onto a chunk of concrete. But, to my amazement, they were not just surviving, but kind of popping up going, I can swim. This is their first swim ever, the first swim of their lives.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So incredible. So, that footage will be featured in a new documentary coming out next year. But for now, for more amazing Earth Month content, you can check out the Our Home collection on \uc2 Disney\uc2  Plus. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is so cool. Thank you, Morgan. Coming up, award winning songwriter, Alice Randall on celebrating country music roots.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\b0\par\par\uc2 801 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, we have a heart-pounding rescue of a swimmer caught in a rip current. The life-saving efforts were caught on camera, after the poor man was pulled from the water with no pulse. Erielle Reshef is here now with more. Good morning to you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Robin. That 21-year-old is lucky to be alive after he was swept out by that rip current. Rescuers say his heart stopped for several terrifying minutes. The rescuer revived him caught on camera on this video. And it may be tough to watch, but he is okay.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the heart-pounding moments as rescuers rush to save this unconscious man who nearly drowned off the coast of Florida. Deputies say 21-year-old Felipe Desouza was swimming with a friend in an unstaffed area when they got caught in a rip current. This body camera footage picking up the frantic scene after he is pulled from the water. According to officials, the water carried Desouza about 100 yards off New Smyrna Beach.\par \par \uc2 VICTIM'S FRIEND (MALE)\par \par \uc2 One of my friends is in the ocean and he, he can't swim.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lifeguard Dalton Smith heard the call.\par \par \uc2 DALTON SMITH (LIFEGUARD VOLUSIA COUNTY BEACH SAFETY OCEAN RESCUE)\par \par \uc2 One of the gentlemen that was on the boogie board was too tired to walk himself, so I was carrying him out of the water. And he let me know that his friend was still in the water.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Smith and two other lifeguards pulling him to shore. Officials performing chest compressions before quickly moving him into the ambulance. Ty Tarnow was one of the paramedics on scene trying to revive him.\par \par \uc2 TY TARNOW (FIREFIGHTER / PARAMEDIC NEW SMYRNA BEACH FIRE DEPARTMENT)\par \par \uc2 We had no idea this young man was going to pull through.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tarnow says it took minutes to get a pulse as they arrived at the hospital. Rip currents cause 80% of coastline rescues.\par \par \uc2 DALTON SMITH (LIFEGUARD VOLUSIA COUNTY BEACH SAFETY OCEAN RESCUE)\par \par \uc2 I personally worked five gentlemen last year and none of them came to the positive end like this did.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The rescue team calling this a miracle, all reunited with Felipe just days ago.\par \par \uc2 DALTON SMITH (LIFEGUARD VOLUSIA COUNTY BEACH SAFETY OCEAN RESCUE)\par \par \uc2 We're obviously very happy with the outcome. It's great to see him.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, a relief to see that. A remarkable rescue. And as you there, Felipe reunited with all of the heroes who saved his life in the hospital. And good news this morning, and this is remarkable, he is making a full recovery.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is not the way it goes sometimes with rip currents. They're so incredibly dangerous. It's important to heed those warnings. But thankfully, he's okay.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that picture of them all in the hospital room. It's looks great.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know. Nothing like a good reunion.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that's right. Erielle, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 7:42, COSTCO GOLD RUSH\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up next, customers go to \uc2 Costco\uc2 , you know, to get paper towels, the famous hot dogs. Well, now, we'll tell you why customers are panning for gold at the big box store. That's right.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING US WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now overseas to the Middle East. The US is warning that Iran could retaliate against Israel in the coming days. Foreign correspondent Britt Clennett is on the scene in Jerusalem. Good morning, Britt.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Yeah, Israel is on high alert as threats from Iran escalate.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tehran issuing new warnings that it will retaliate for an attack on its consulate in Syria last week that killed a senior Iranian. Now, President Biden has pledged iron-clad US support in the event of any Iranian strike. And ABC News confirming that US Central Command General Michael Erik Kurilla is traveling to Israel to coordinate on this Iran threat. The US has been warning that a significant strike from Tehran is imminent. Israel's minister of defense, Yoav Gallant, vowing to respond quickly with attacks on its enemy's territory.\par \par \uc2 BRITT CLENNETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the \uc2 IDF\uc2  has pulled leave for its combat units and boosted its air defense. Israel, though, has not claimed responsibility for that Damascus attack that killed seven Revolutionary Guard members, including a top commander. Robin?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Britt, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JEREMIAH'S SECOND CHANCE TO SAVE A LIFE ROBIN'S NEPHEW ON HIS JOURNEY TO BECOME A STEM CELL DONOR\b0\par\par\uc2 1,725 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CHILI, WARS, CONDIMENT, OWNS\par \par \uc2 "THE TEEN BRAIN", EXCLUSIVE, PARENTS, TEENS\par \par \uc2 ENGELBERT, WNBA, DRAFT\par \par \uc2 STOKE, CIPTON, SAND CLOUD, OUR PLACE, VINGLACE, ROSETTA STONE\par \par \uc2 BRED GOURMET\par \par \uc2 STEM CELL, DONOR, JEREMIAH, CRAFT, GIRALT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with our series, "One Match, Second Chance." When we talk about second chances, this usually refers to the person in need of a stem cell transplant, but this time it's about a donor. This story is very, very close to my heart, it's my nephew Jeremiah, and here is his journey.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP: "GMA" JUNE 11, 2012\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sometimes treatment for cancer can lead to other serious medical issues, and that's what I'm facing right now.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This was the moment I shared my diagnosis of mds, Myelodysplastic syndrome...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is a rare blood disorder that affects the bone marrow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...and my need for a life-saving stem cell transplant. Thankfully, my eldest sister Sally-Ann was my perfect match.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She is going to be my donor, she's going to be my donor.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But 70 percent of patients don't have a fully-matched donor in their family and must rely on donations from strangers on the registry for their best chance at a cure. My sister's healthy cells giving me the gift of life.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR SERGIO GIRALT (BONE MARROW TRANSPLANT SPECIALIST MEMORIAL SLOAN)\par \par \uc2 After you recover from transplant, you actually may get her allergies, you actually will get her blood type. You won't get her taste for music though.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Promises, promises.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR SERGIO GIRALT (BONE MARROW TRANSPLANT SPECIALIST MEMORIAL SLOAN)\par \par \uc2 Promises, yeah. I think now is a good time to say go Sally, go.\par \par \uc2 SALLY-ANN ROBERTS (SISTER OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 There is nothing but joy in knowing that you have something in your body that can save another human being's life.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 My nephew, Jeremiah, who I lovingly call Little Jer, a kid who loved wearing his Spider-Man suit, watching on throughout the journey.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 I think what stands out to me most about that time is just my aunt's unwavering strength.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sally-Ann convincing her then teenage son to sign up for the registry.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 Basically, my mom volun-told me to sign up, right, like, kind of like a mandatory suggestion.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And to his surprise, shortly later, he got the call. He was a match, but he said no.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 Unfortunately, at the time, I just was thinking about me. It was acting selfishly. I didn't heed the call. Up until this point, I was very, very sure that that was going to be the biggest mistake of my life.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But he'd have a second chance. This past January, Jeremiah learning once again he's a match.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 Because I have been thinking about that person every single day, it was just impossible for me to not say yes.\par \par \uc2 SALLY-ANN ROBERTS (SISTER OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 He did not hesitate, he was ready.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This time, Jer's all in.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 It is the first day for the shots.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He'll need five days of injections to help stimulate his blood stem cells to prepare for donation day.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 All right, look at that. That's how you do it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nmdp, formerly Be The Match, facilitating it all, covering the costs for flights, hotel, transportation. Jeremiah traveling from New York to Houston for the big day.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 All right, I made it to the hotel and everything is fine. Definitely feeling some of those aches.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As donation day arrived, I couldn't help but check in on my nephew to wish him well.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Jer.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 Hey, auntie, hey.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those fears that you had the first time around, how are you feeling?\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 What I'm doing here versus what this person is going through, it's just incomparable.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're a super hero, you're a super hero.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 Hey, I'm trying to do the right thing for the second time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A temporary inconvenience for a life-saving impact.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm very proud of you. You know how much I love you.\par \par \uc2 JEREMIAH CRAFT (NEPHEW OF ROBIN/STEM CELL DONOR)\par \par \uc2 I'm just grateful to God that I can go from pretending to be a hero to growing older, learning what is important and actually saving a life. I'm very thankful.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Needless to say, I am so proud of Little Jer. The courage and candor to share the complete story. And I have to say, when we talked about doing the story, we he told me, we did this family Zoom prayer the last Saturday of every month and he said, "Hey, Auntie, I'm a match." I'm like, "Ah, that's great." And, of course, my little producer mind goes to work and I'm like, "Oh, we should do something to show the full circle." And he called me and he was a little upset, he was emotional. He said, "I didn't do it the first time." I'm like, "I never knew that." And he said, "But I want to make sure that people realize that I didn't do it, but I'm doing it now" to show that, yeah, you can be a little concerned, and that happens so many times...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...for various reasons, people decide not to do it. And he just wanted to show it's okay, he knows those fears, but if you just work through it. And it's so important for young people like my nephew because the research has shown that they are, the outcomes for the recipient are better when you have young donors like that.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, he feels lucky to have had the second chance?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's gotten a second chance, he's given this complete stranger a second chance. She's, all we know is that she lives in England. But, he is so relieved that he's gotten a second chance.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, he said he felt like it was his biggest regret and he thought about it every day since he said, "No."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm glad he said yes now. But, what's being done to make donating easier for those who do get the call?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I'm glad you said that because, you know, a lot of people can't take the time off from work and things like that. So nmdp, formerly Be The Match, they are working on a life-saving lead act with Congress to offer blood stem cell donors the same protections allowed that the family and medical leave act provides. And you can find out how to be a stem cell donor by scanning the qr code that's right there on your screen or by going to goodmorningamerica.com. I told you last time when we saw the piece on him being an actor, how that Superman or Spider-Man outfit that he kept on for, like, two years (inaudible). You all, he had it with him when he was donating...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, how nice.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...they brought, and I said, he always wanted to be a super hero and he is now, but he said no, he's just, like, the average person and just wanted to get the word out there that you, too, can do it, so.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're glad he shared.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Glad he did.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah. Way to go, Jer. Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And back here at home, charges against the former assistant principal at a Virginia school where a first-grade teacher was shot by a 6-year-old student last year. A grand jury report is offering new details about that incident. Our chief justice correspondent Pierre Thomas joins us with more. Good morning, Pierre.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. That assistant principal has yet to give a public response to these new charges accusing her of failing to protect her children and a shocking level of indifference.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the former assistant principal at Richneck Elementary, where a 6-year-old boy intentionally shot his teacher, facing criminal charges. Ebony Parker indicted, charged with eight counts of felony child neglect in an incident that nearly took the life of the first-grade teacher Abby Zwerner.\par \par \uc2 ABBY ZWERNER (FORMER TEACHER RICHNECK ELEMENTARY SCHOOL)\par \par \uc2 The look on the student's face when he pulled out the firearm is a haunting look.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A special grand jury in Virginia accusing Parker of ignoring repeated warnings.\par \par \uc2 DIANE TOSCANO (ATTORNEY FOR ABBY ZWERNER)\par \par \uc2 It confirms that there were multiple opportunities for the school administration to call the police.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE BOY'S PRIOR OFFENSES\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It began when Zwerner the morning of the shooting going to see Parker and allegedly telling Parker the child was in a violent mood. According to the grand jury's report, the boy who had previously choked a teacher and fellow student had just threatened to beat up a kindergartener. Parker did not respond, the report said, and never even looked away from her computer screen. A short time later, two students told another member of the school staff the child had a gun in his bag. The child's backpack was searched, but nothing was found. The grand jury says, Zwerner, still worried, told colleagues she thought she saw the boy put something in his pocket, which was also told to Parker. Still, no expansive search or pat down.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Then after recess, one of the boy's friends came up to another teacher and told her the child had a gun and showed him the bullets. At 1:58 PM, according to the grand jury, the boy turned to Zwerner, pulled a gun out of his pocket and, at less than six feet away, pulled the trigger.\par \par \uc2 DIANE TOSCANO (ATTORNEY FOR ABBY ZWERNER)\par \par \uc2 It was preventable. That's just what is heartbreaking.\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It could have been worse. According to the grand jury, the gun had seven more bullets but jammed. This is the second time this week an adult has been in court on charges after a child shoots someone after those Michigan parents was sentenced for their part in their son's murder of high school classmate, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Pierre, the Biden administration is announcing a new measure aimed at gun safety?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN ADMINISTRATION'S NEW GUN SAFETY MEASURE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPARTMENT MOVING TO CLOSE 'GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE'\par \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The DOJ is moving to close the so-called gun show loophole, authorizing the ATF to require that anyone selling guns commercially to register and do background checks on gun sales no matter the circumstances, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Pierre, thank you for your reporting. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN" NEW DOCUMENTARY AIMS TO HELP PARENTS UNDERSTAND THEIR KIDS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,089 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CHILI, WARS, CONDIMENT, OWNS\par \par \uc2 "THE TEEN BRAIN", EXCLUSIVE, PARENTS, TEENS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot of umbrellas out there in Times Square this morning. We're back with our "gma" Cover Story, an exclusive first look at the new documentary, "The Teen Brain." It's designed to break stereotypes and help parents understand their kids. Great to have Maggie Rulli here in the studio to tell us about it. Good morning, Maggie.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning. Yeah, in this film, we hear directly from teens in their own words and one of the things they say they want to know is why don't adults understand us? Well, this film not only shows them why, but also how their unique teen brains could actually be a super power.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP: "THE TEEN BRAIN"\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 So, you want to know what it feel likes to be a teen?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Thrilling, scary, stimulating, just a fraction of the emotions teens say they experience.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 A lot of it is like a roller coaster.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 Everything is just more extreme.\par \par \uc2 TIFFANY SHLAIN (DIRECTOR "THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 So, what is going on in the teen brain?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That's the big question asked and answered by director Tiffany Shlain in partnership with mindup.org in her exploratory new film, "The Teen Brain."\par \par \uc2 TIFFANY SHLAIN (DIRECTOR "THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 We talked to all the top neuroscientists in the space and then we talked to so many teenagers. We wanted to hear directly from teens, what do you want to know about your brain? What do you wish adults knew about you and what you're feeling?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In just ten minutes, one of the goals of the film is to destigmatize the stereotypes around those incredibly formative years.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 When you promote adolescence as a time of brokenness, adolescents will think they're broken.\par \par \uc2 ELLEN GALINSKY (AUTHOR "THE BREAKTHROUGH YEARS")\par \par \uc2 We are using an adult yard stick to understand teenagers. We wouldn't say that infants are deficit toddlers, but yet we think of teenagers as, you know, not quite adults and we measure them that way and that really affects how we talk to them.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW RESEARCH TO HELP PARENTS GUIDE AND UNDERSTAND THEIR KIDS\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ellen Galinsky, author of "The Breakthrough Years," reinforces how understanding a teen's brain can help parents guide and interact with teens in a better way and help them understand themselves.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 The medulla, which is this loud, emotional space, part of the limbic system, becomes much more sensitive during this period. It actually grows in size.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 Emotions feel so strong and it's all like, you know, I'm upset in this moment and it's hard to sort of see the bigger picture.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And experts say focusing on the brain can actually reveal those passions and pursuits that are most fulfilling, all while honoring those emotions that are the essence of the teen experience.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 Yes, this is a time when the highs are really high, but the lows are really low, but this is a time when you are just experiencing everything in a way that people go to movies to feel.\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Actress, Goldie Hawn, CEO and founder of MindUP says, "I have wanted to create a film on the adolescent brain because it's important for our teens, parents, and educators to understand that being a teen is an extraordinary time to be alive."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO FIND BALANCE BETWEEN INDEPENDENCE AND STRUCTURE\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, guys, what I just loved about this film was that it takes a more positive spin and it gives teens and their parents the tools to actually take advantage of this unique time in their lives.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, so how do parents help teens with that? How do they help them balance independence and structure?\par \par \uc2 MAGGIE RULLI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's always a struggle, but you know, Ellen Galinsky says parents are actually the most important people in their teens' lives, a little bit of pressure for us, but she also gives us the tools to take advantage of this. She says, first, check in on yourself, take pause before responding to a difficult situation. Second, consider your child's pointed of view. Third, share your expectations and your limits. Finally, problem solve together and let those moments be a lesson. "The Teen Brain" is out on Monday and for more information, you can go to letitripple.org.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Maggie.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's go over to Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's great having Maggie on this side of the pond for a change.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FLIPPING FOR THE BURGERS AT BRED GOURMET BELOVED BOSTON SPOT SERVING UP UNIQUE CREATIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,764 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CHILI, WARS, CONDIMENT, OWNS\par \par \uc2 "THE TEEN BRAIN", EXCLUSIVE, PARENTS, TEENS\par \par \uc2 ENGELBERT, WNBA, DRAFT\par \par \uc2 STOKE, CIPTON, SAND CLOUD, OUR PLACE, VINGLACE, ROSETTA STONE\par \par \uc2 BRED GOURMET\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our "Comfort Food" road trip is stopping in Boston this morning. Jess Sims is there at a spot known for making an American comfort food favorite, the burger. Good morning, Jess.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, y'all. I mean, is there anything more comforting than taking a big bite of a juicy burger? I don't think so. We are live here at Bred Gourmet, home of one of Boston's favorite burgers. But, before we dive into this delicious food, because we've been waiting, let's take a look at what makes this place so great.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Boston is flipping for the burgers at Bred Gourmet. Owner, Tambo Barrow has been running the burger joint for nearly a decade.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 You've got to get a good look at that. That's that Bred classic.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Known for their unique creations stacked with ingredients like plantains, bacon, pineapple, and crispy fried onions.\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The food here is outstanding, it's delicious. It never fails. The people here treat you like family. I come here weekly and will never stop.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There's comfort in variety for Bred Gourmet's menu. The restaurant even awarded Best of Boston in 2021.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 We started from scratch and to get Best of Boston, the city I grew up in, Boston's best burger, that means a lot to us.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am here with Bred Gourmet's owner, Tambo Barrow and his beautiful family, as well as the head chef and manager, Eudine Mahon. Of course, big shout out to all the family and friends that came out here, yes, in support of this incredible restaurant. So, Tambo, talk to me, you haven't always been in the restaurant business, you were actually in insurance. What inspired this transition?\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, well I was in insurance for a while and I always knew I wanted to do something that involved food. I was walking my dog one day and I saw this place and I had a big idea, and the rest is history after that.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. okay. Speaking of big, we're about to build this Maui burger. This is your favorite on the menu. Why?\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. So, this was the first burger that we created...\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 ...and, you know, it's all my favorite comfort food toppings in one, and, you know, I want to build this with you.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I want to build this with you. Let's go. What do we do first?\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 So, we're going to start off with a sweet barbecue sauce and we're going to put that on the bottom bun. You can be generous, don't be shy, don't be shy.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Definitely generous. I'm not shy.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 All right, cool. And so then, we're going to take my favorite topping, which is a fried sweet plantains, and I'm West Indian, my mother is from Trinidad, my father is from Barbados, so I saw plantains on every plate.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm going to put this on every burger moving forward, thank you.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely, absolutely. And from there, we're going to take the star of the show, which is the smoked prime beef patty.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, my gosh.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 There you go. And then from there, we're going to lay the applewood smoked bacon. You want to make sure that you, you know, make sure it doesn't topple over.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you said lay it down, so I'm being very gentle.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Just lay it down.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gentle, there we go.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. From there, we do the sliced pineapple and top with some crispy onions.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm going to be very generous with these because my gosh.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, go ahead. Go crazy.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 And then, we're going to take the sauce and get more generous on the top bun. Take it, boom. And you can dig in. I already had (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wait, okay. Before I take a bite, because I'm going to be out of business here once I start eating this. Eudine, talk to us about how cool is it to be part of the creative genius of these burgers and bringing what you and Tambo have to life on the menu?\par \par \uc2 EUDINE MAHON (MANAGER AND HEAD CHEF BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Honestly, it's been a very unique experience. I love being here. I always have ambition for food and beverage and this is just, like, a home away from home. I love, like, creating new ideas and seeing it come to life. And, honestly, it has been the best experience so far. I have a great team to work with. I have a great boss, great coworkers. We are like a family here. Everything is awesome.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I wouldn't eat anything or anywhere else if I worked here. Wow. Speaking of the other things on the menu, because it's not just burgers, talk to me, Tambo. What else do you have?\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 For sure. We have our powdered beignets, which I picked up when I went on my trip to New Orleans. The powdered beignets. We smoke our wings here. We have smoked, honey garlic wings. And then, of course, we have these cousin (inaudible) fries, which has become a fan favorite. Cousin (inaudible) is a rapper and he's our favorite cousin, so we had to make a fry after him.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course. Of course. Oh, Eudine, yes.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) so she's going to put our special sauce on there.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I can't believe there are fries under there.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Oh, man, for sure. And then, we top it off with the Scallions. There you go. Perfect.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is absolutely incredible. Well, thank you so much for, one, coming here super, super early and letting us crash the restaurant. As a little token of our appreciation...\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Oh, wow, wow.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...we have, yes, "Comfort Food America" tour presented to y'all. Now, I have a question, where are you going to hang this?\par \par \uc2 EUDINE MAHON (MANAGER AND HEAD CHEF BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Right here.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right here?\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Well, we might put it here, that's one of them, but I'm thinking about putting it in our new location coming in Cambridge in the fall of 2024.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. You heard it here first. Now, before we throw back, Michael, he has a special message for you.\par \par \uc2 TAMBO BARROW (OWNER BRED GOURMET)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, Mike, I'm still mad at you, man. I'm a big Patriots fan and I don't...\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mike, I'm gonna leave that to y'all. I'm going to...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, you know what, Jess? Tell him that he needs to get in line with all the other Patriots fans, but I understand.\par \par \uc2 JESS SIMS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He said you need to get in line with all the other Patriots fans.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, I do understand, I do understand. The burger looks fantastic. And, you know, tomorrow, Jess thank you so much for that. And tomorrow, we're bringing all of our favorite comfort food spots in New York here to our studio.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Uh-oh, uh-oh.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you're going to miss it. Yeah, we're gonna be eating good tomorrow. George, you ready for a burger in the morning? All right.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up, Robin's nephew, Jeremiah, Little Jer you call him...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Little Jer, Little Jer.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...yeah, he's giving a second chance at becoming a super hero. This is a story you don't want to miss, so you stay right there for more "GMA," we'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2