E\par \par \uc2 BRED GOURMET\par \par \uc2 STEM CELL, DONOR, JEREMIAH, CRAFT, GIRALT\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you. Wow, I've got tears in my eyes. Thank you, Jer, and thank you, everybody. Let's start with Las Vegas, shall we, because they finally made it to 80, but the latest they've hit 80 in 42 years, so it's been a bit of a cool winter.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILD TEMPERATURES: THIS AFTERNOON\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you see the warmth is not just there, but Phoenix hitting their 90s right on time, late March is about right. And they'll stay there, 95 tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TURNING COOLER: THIS WEEKEND\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It looks like Las Vegas, though, going to drop off after today and tomorrow. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ALICE RANDALL TALKS "MY BLACK COUNTRY" AWARD-WINNING SONGWRITER ON CELEBRATING COUNTRY MUSIC'S BLACK ROOTS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,021 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CHILI, WARS, CONDIMENT, OWNS\par \par \uc2 "THE TEEN BRAIN", EXCLUSIVE, PARENTS, TEENS\par \par \uc2 ENGELBERT, WNBA, DRAFT\par \par \uc2 STOKE, CIPTON, SAND CLOUD, OUR PLACE, VINGLACE, ROSETTA STONE\par \par \uc2 BRED GOURMET\par \par \uc2 STEM CELL, DONOR, JEREMIAH, CRAFT, GIRALT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 RANDALL, COUNTRY, "MY BLACK COUNTRY"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back now with award-winning songwriter, Alice Randall whose impact on country music and beyond runs deep. She's written a book and it's called "My Black Country: A Journey To Country Music's Black Past, Present, and Future." Deb, you had a chance to speak with her.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I did, Robin. You know country music, so you know of her, yet many don't know her name, but before "Cowboy Carter" had us tapping our feet, Alice Randall was the secret sauce behind so many country music stars. Well now, she wants you to know her story and those of so many other black Americans who've shaped country music.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For award-winning songwriter, novelist, and author, Alice Randall, country music is deeply personal.\par \par \uc2 ALICE RANDALL (PROF & WRITER-IN-RESIDENCE VANDERBILT UNIV/SONGWRITER)\par \par \uc2 I love country because country is optimistic. Even when it's (inaudible) and it's mournful, it dances. Country has hope in it.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In her new book, "My Black Country," Randall celebrates country music's black roots by introducing the first family of black country.\par \par \uc2 ALICE RANDALL (PROF & WRITER-IN-RESIDENCE VANDERBILT UNIV/SONGWRITER)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible), the papa, he was the Opry's first super star. Lil Harden Armstrong in 1930 recorded on Jimmy Rogers' "Blue Yodel Number Nine." Some people say that is the most iconic country single of all time. Then Ray Charles would drop in 1963 modern sounds in country and western music. That, many people think, is the most important country album of all time. Herb Jeffreys was the braun buckaroo. In the 1930s and 1940s, he made a series of black singing cowboy films. Charlie Pride, he was entertainer of the year in 1971. That's the first family of black country.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Randall also sharing the isolating experience of being a lone black woman songwriter in Nashville in the '80s and '90s.\par \par \uc2 ALICE RANDALL (PROF & WRITER-IN-RESIDENCE VANDERBILT UNIV/SONGWRITER)\par \par \uc2 It was hard. I was always the unexpected body in the room when I showed up.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But being an only didn't stop her. In 1994, Randall became the first black woman to co-write a number one country single, \uc2 Trisha Yearwood\uc2 's smash hit, "XXX's and OOO's." Yet, even with that success, Randall longed to have black musicians sing her songs.\par \par \uc2 ALICE RANDALL (PROF & WRITER-IN-RESIDENCE VANDERBILT UNIV/SONGWRITER)\par \par \uc2 It created a kind of profound frustration because when white singers were singing the songs, listeners believed all the heroes and sheroes in my songs were white, too. They did not see the portraits of black and brown and indigenous people that I had created.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now Beyonce's ground breaking album, "Cowboy Carter," she says, is changing the game.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON COUNTRY MUSIC'S BLACK ROOTS, HER EXPERIENCE AS A SONGWRITER, AND BEYONCE\par \par \uc2 ALICE RANDALL (PROF & WRITER-IN-RESIDENCE VANDERBILT UNIV/SONGWRITER)\par \par \uc2 I started listening to it over and over because it was, for me, an absolute Juneteenth. It was good news at long last. It was a family reunion and the whole family was being invited.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A family celebration. Randall's book "My Black Country" is out right now, loaded with her dream lineup of country singers. You heard one just now, actually, sung by Rhiannon Giddens called "The Ballad of Sally Ann." I thought you'd get a kick out of that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oooh, my sister's name.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It comes out tomorrow. It is quite, quite an album. We're going to get our country boots together, cowboy boots and hats, right?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm so glad that she did this book, and thank you for sharing it. Just the history, people will be more aware.\par \par \uc2 DEBORAH ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really amazing.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Gather your little ones tomorrow because we have an exciting first look at the new "Bluey" special before its big \uc2 Disney\uc2  Plus premiere on Sunday, so you have been volun-told to watch tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 There you go. Have a great day, everybody.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Bye, bye.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS SPRING BONANZA\b0\par\par\uc2 1,297 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CH