OLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, COURT, ABORTION, 1864, BAN, SHOWDOWN, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the latest on the showdown over abortion rights and the fallout in Arizona. That's in the wake of court decision that upheld an 1864 law banning the procedure with almost no exceptions. Let's go back to Rachel Scott there in Phoenix for us. Good morning, again, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you, again. And it has been a chaotic 48 hours here in Arizona. There was bipartisan outrage after the State Supreme Court ruled that an abortion ban passed during the civil war could go into effect. But, when state Democrats tried to bring a bill to the floor to repeal that law, it was Republicans who stood in the way, rejecting those efforts and so now, the state of Arizona is in limbo. That near-total abortion ban is expected to go into effect here in the state sometime within the next several weeks. The Biden campaign placing the blame on Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , saying that he owns the suffering and the chaos that we are seeing play out across the state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course, it was the former president who appointed three of the six Supreme Court Justices who overturned Roe versus Wade, clearing the way for 21 states to ban or further restrict access to abortion. But now, Trump says that the Arizona ban goes too far. Of course, this could be a defining issue in the November election. We know that abortion rights could be on the ballot in as many as 14 states, including several battlegrounds, including right here in Arizona, as well as Pennsylvania and Nevada. And the Vice President expected to be here in Arizona tomorrow. Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel. Thanks so much. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 07:30 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Clark, steps back, fires. You bet.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Back here on "GMA." Yes, Caitlin Clark honored last night. Iowa, what took them so long? They retired her in number 22. She's expected to go number one in the WNBA draft on Monday. We're going to hear from the woman who'll be announcing Clark's name. That's WNBA commissioner \uc2 Cathy Engelbert\uc2  on how the blockbuster women's March Madness is impacting the pro game, and the commissioner is going to join us live.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Completely transforming it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, it's got to be. Yes.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Uh-huh.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're looking forward to that. We're following a lot of headlines right now, including the major storm system moving east and north this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STORMS ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 At least seven tornadoes reported that left a trail of destruction in the south. Ginger's tracking the weather with seven states on flood alerts right now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES OF BRIDGE COLLAPSE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, right now, the Army Corps of Engineer released new Navy 3D sonar images of the Francis Scott Key Bridge wreckage site in Baltimore. The images show the underwater debris of the collapsed bridge. And the chair of the \uc2 NTSB\uc2  says, the agency is focusing its investigation on the ship's electrical system. Experts from Hyundai are here helping with the equipment in the engine room. They are focusing on the power system and the circuit breakers.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And check out the par 3 competition for pros and their families leading up to the master's. Bubba Watson's daughter, Dakota, on the putting green at one of the great traditions of golf.\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And she does it again. That's right. What a putt. She's following in her dad's footsteps.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, easy.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 He may be able to use her out there when the tournament kicks off. The 2024 Master's tees off this morning on \uc2 ESPN\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA WHAT'S NEXT\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we've got a lot more ahead, including the new way some people fighting inflation at \uc2 Costco\uc2 . That is all coming up, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEADLY STORMS SLAM THE SOUTH TORNADOES LEAVE TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION IN TEXAS AND LOUISIANA\b0\par\par\uc2 548 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 STORMS, TEXAS, LOUISIANA, TORNADOES, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8:00\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First a look at the top stories breaking at 8:00. We start with the storms across the south bringing at least seven tornadoes, heavy rain, and flooding. Let's go back to Rob Marciano on the scene in Slidell, Louisiana. Good morning, Rob.\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, George. This one came through around 10:00 in the morning, a tornado that blasted it, trees down everywhere, power lines. This one coming onto this truck and also tearing into this apartment building where the winds ripped apart some of the brick structure and the roof. Take a look at this drone video. The second story completely ripped off. People were hurt in this building. They were rushed to the hospital with no serious injuries, but everybody here is displaced. The business district also had businesses torn up there and it was very difficult to get around because of the flooding yesterday. Not just here, but across New Orleans. And then tornadoes kept going east and through Chunchula, Alabama. They had an ef-1 tornado there doing some damage. And we're not done just yet.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT: THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We still have a severe weather threat today. We had some severe flooding across parts of Tallahassee, from Jacksonville up through the Carolinas. A potential for severe storms this morning and then later today, Eastern Ohio up river up through Western Pennsylvania, we could see more in the way of tornadoes there. We obviously have a history with this thing as it pushes off to the east, into the northeast tonight with wind and rain through tomorrow morning, eventually getting out to sea on Saturday. But, we can't be done with this system soon enough. Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said that right, Rob. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THIRD ATTEMPT TO DELAY TRUMP "HUSH MONEY" TRIAL DENIED JURY SELECTION IN CASE SCHEDULED TO BEGIN ON MONDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 400 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We have the latest now on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's legal troubles.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIRD ATTEMPT TO DELAY TRUMP "HUSH MONEY" TRIAL DENIED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY SELECTION IN CASE SCHEDULED TO BEGIN ON MONDAY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Another attempt by the former president's legal team to delay his New York election inference case has been denied. Aaron Katersky is at the courthouse in lower Manhattan. Good morning, Aaron.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, George. All week, former President Trump's been trying to scuttle his criminal trial with this haphazard strategy that has his lawyers rushing to this courthouse with emergency appeals for delays. But three times in the last three days, judges here have turned him down.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump's latest request to postpone argued that the trial judge should be off the case. Trump's attorneys complaining of an unacceptable appearance of impropriety because Judge Juan Merchan's daughter did political work for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S LATEST ATTEMPT TO DELAY "HUSH MONEY" TRIAL\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They said this trial can only be done once and it must be done right because of the potential impact on the election. But prosecutors said the independent political activities of the judge's daughter are no reason to challenge his credibility. And a lawyer representing the judge said there's absolutely no evidence to show that Judge Merchan will stand to benefit from the outcome of the trial. Now, prosecutors also said delaying this case now would be incredibly disruptive. So, in all likelihood, jury selection will start on time, four days from now.\par \par \uc2 AARON KATERSKY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And former President Trump, Michael, will be standing trial on charges he falsified business records to cover up a long-denied affair from voters. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm sure you'll be watching it for us, Aaron. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the porch pirate crackdown in Florida. Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  signed a bill to make the Sunshine State the latest to raise penalties for stealing packages from outside homes as well as for retail theft. Melissa Adan is in Miami with more. Good morning, Melissa.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. So, the state of Florida is actually going to make it a felony if you steal $40 or more worth of property. The police chief here in Coral Gables tells me he welcomes this news as he sees hundreds of these cases here in his city. And he hopes that these stiffer criminal charges make a difference.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, they are the brazen thieves striking in broad daylight and in the night. This porch pirate in Sacramento disguised as a trash bag captured stealing a package. Some homeowners, like this one, have had enough, using a decoy package to catch this alleged thief.\par \par \uc2 THIEF (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Yo, yo, yo. Yo.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Florida, the governor cracking down. A new law going into effect this October. If you steal property worth more than $40, it will be considered a felony.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR RON DESANTIS (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Someone's going to have hell to pay for stealing.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The law replacing an already existing one, this time lowering the stolen property value from $100 to $40. It also includes stricter penalties for retail theft.\par \par \uc2 BOB BREWSTER (BUSINESS OWNER IN STUART FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Everything in our store is a candy store for a criminal, things they can grab, sell fast and then take from us.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In Coral Gables, the police chief welcoming it, sharing these videos of thieves in action.\par \par \uc2 CHIEF EDWARD HUDAK (CORAL GABLES POLICE DEPARTMENT)\par \par \uc2 We're able to make stronger cases against these repeat offenders, and also kind of giving other diversionary sentences from people who are facing felonies.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a growing trend across the country with at least nine other states making porch pirating a felony. And that's not all, according to the \uc2 National Retail Federation\uc2 , organized retail crime cost consumers $112 billion in 2022. The state topping the list, California. A proposed bill there calling for repeat shoplifters to serve jail time after a third conviction.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, last month in New York, the governor there announced a $45 million plan to fight back against organized retail crime theft. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Melissa, our thanks to you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARREST WARRANT ISSUED FOR RASHEE RICE CHIEF'S RECEIVER FACING CHARGES IN DALLAS HIGHWAY CHAIN REACTION\b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right now, the car crash involving Chiefs receiver Rashee Rice.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARREST WARRANT ISSUED FOR RASHEE RICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHIEF'S RECEIVER FACING CHARGES IN DALLAS HIGHWAY CHAIN REACTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Dallas police have issued arrest warrants for rice and the other driver accused of causing the chain-reaction crash. Chief national correspondent Matt Gutman has the details. Good morning, Matt.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning. Those arrest warrants were issued yesterday. And the Chiefs star receiver, who apologized for the incident, faces serious charges for that six-car crash, including aggravated assault. Dallas police telling me overnight that neither Rice nor the other driver is yet in custody.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  wide receiver Rashee Rice waking up a wanted man, criminally charged for his involvement in that Dallas highway crash that left four people injured.\par \par \uc2 KAYLA QUINN (CRASH VICTIM)\par \par \uc2 The impact was crazy. We could have flew out.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Dallas Police Department issuing arrest warrants Wednesday to both Rice, who they say was driving the Lamborghini, and 21-year-old Theodore Knox, allegedly behind the wheel of a Corvette. Police say the vehicles caused a chain-reaction collision involving four other vehicles. Kayla Quinn had her 4-year-old son in the back seat of that silver car, which was totaled.\par \par \uc2 KAYLA QUINN (CRASH VICTIM)\par \par \uc2 It was very traumatic.\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Authorities say that the occupants of the Lamborghini and the Corvette then ran from the scene without stopping to determine if anyone needed medical help or providing their information. They can allegedly be seen by this photo obtained by TMZ Sports walking down the highway away from the crash before authorities arrived.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DALLAS HIGHWAY CRASH\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both Rice and Knox now face one count of aggravated assault, one count of collision involving serious bodily injury and six counts of collision involving bodily injury. Rice posting on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  last week, "I take full responsibility for my part in this matter and will continue to cooperate with the necessary authorities. I sincerely apologize to everyone impacted in Saturday's accident." The \uc2 NFL\uc2  telling ABC News they "continue to monitor developments in the matter."\par \par \uc2 MATT GUTMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Rice's attorney has said his client has taken full responsibility for the crash and has been cooperative with authorities. But Dallas police decided on charges that could change the trajectory of Rice's career, especially that aggravated assault charge which carries a maximum at a 20-year sentence. Guys?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Matt, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RICE, ARREST, CAR CRASH, QUINN\par \par \uc2 DESANTIS, BREWSTER, HUDAK, PORCH PIRATE, THEFT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PORCH PIRATE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR SIGNS A BILL TO TOUGHEN PENALTIES FOR STEALING PACKAGES, RETAIL THEFT\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, RIP CURRENT, DESOUZA, SMITH, TARNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART-POUNDING RIP CURRENT RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SWIMMER SAVED FROM WATER & REVIVED BY PARAMEDICS\par \par \uc2 COSTCO, GOLD BARS, HERZOG, EDWARDS, BEAUREGARD, YANG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 PENGUINS, CLIFF DIVING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN", 8:12\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADOES AND FLOODING: TRAIL OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. Violent storms tearing through the south. At least seven reported tornadoes leaving a frightening trail of destruction.\par \par \uc2 DARIAN FAZLIC (TORNADO WITNESS)\par \par \uc2 That is a tornado two football fields away.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of homes and businesses were destroyed. New Orleans getting a month's worth of rain in just seven hours.\par \par \uc2 NEW ORLEANS RESIDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Come on, Pearl.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Ginger is tracking it all as the storm heads north with seven states waking up to flood alerts.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE "THE TEEN BRAIN": WHAT IS YOUR TEENAGER THINKING?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Inside "The Teen Brain." An exclusive look at a new documentary for anyone who has wondered what their teenager is thinking.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 A lot of it is like a roller coaster.\par \par \uc2 PARTICIPANT ("THE TEEN BRAIN")\par \par \uc2 Everything is just more extreme.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What it reveals and how it can help parents understand their kids.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WNBA COMMISSIONER LIVE: ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're going one-on-one with the commissioner of the wnba talking the future of women's basketball, how the Caitlin Clark effect is already giving the league a boost as we gear up for next week's wnba draft.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMFORT FOOD AMERICA: TASTE OF PARADISE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're bringing the sizzle to our "Comfort Food" Tour with a stop in Boston for a burger that's like a taste of paradise...\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The food here is outstanding. It's delicious. It never fails.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...as we say good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "gma."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, good morning, America. Our "Comfort Food" tour is making a stop at Bred Gourmet. Jess Sims is there to tell us all about the beloved burger joint. Nothing says breakfast or morning like a burger, that's right. That's all coming up.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're putting Jess to work already. Also ahead, one match second chance and the latest chapter in my stem cell transplant story. My dear sister, Sally-Ann's son, Jeremiah becoming a donor. Little Jer, that's what I call him. Little Jer tells his story, including his hesitation to donate that turned into a personal commitment to give the gift of life.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We are looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But now the latest on the showdown over abortion rights and the fallout in Arizona in the wake of the court decision that upheld an 1864 law banning the procedure with almost no exceptions.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Rachel Scott is in Phoenix with that, and how it could impact voters across the country in November. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you. There is outrage and frustration playing out here in Arizona. Almost immediately after the State Supreme Court said that that abortion ban passed during the Civil War could go into effect, we heard from Democrats and Republicans demanding that the law be repealed. But now, it is state Republicans that are reversing course, rejecting those efforts.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the intense political fight playing out in Arizona...\par \par \uc2 POLITICIANS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Shame on you.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...after the State Supreme Court's decision to reinstate a 160-year-old law banning abortions in all but one circumstance, for the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE STEPHANIE STAHL HAMILTON (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Should the 1864 ban on abortion remain the law in Arizona, people will die.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One day after the ruling, there was bipartisan outrage with state lawmakers on both sides pushing to repeal the law. But when Democrats in the statehouse trying to move forward with a vote, Republicans blocked it.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE TERESA MARTINEZ (REP) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 There is no reason to rush on this very important topic.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR ANNA HERNANDEZ (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 It was chaos. And all because our Republican majority refuses to do what they said they would do.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed three of the six Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade, clearing the way for 21 states to ban or restrict access to abortion. But now, Trump says, Arizona went too far.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Did Arizona go too far, sir?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, they did. And that will be straightened out. And as you know, it's all about states' rights. That will be straightened out.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just weeks ago, Trump was floating the idea of a national abortion ban, but now said he would not sign one.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 President Trump, would you sign a national abortion ban if Congress sent it to your desk?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And he said states should decide whether doctors should face punishment for performing abortions.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you think a doctor should be punished who performed abortions?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'll let that be to the states. You know, everything we're doing now with the states.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion providers like Dr. Jill Gibson could face fines and five years in prison under the ban.\par \par \uc2 JILL GIBSON (MEDICAL DIRECTOR PLANNED PARENTHOOD ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 How can we not have justices that recognize that a law that was enacted before Arizona was a state, before women had the right to vote, should be applicable in today's society?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Biden campaign says it's Trump that owns the suffering and chaos that's happening now. And soon, voters on this battleground state could have the final say with abortion rights expected to be on the ballot this November.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COULD HAVE ABORTION ACCESS ON THE 2024 BALLOT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion rights could be on the ballot in as many as 14 states this November, including battlegrounds like right here in Arizona, Pennsylvania, Nevada. Democrats, of course, counting on this issue to drive out their supporters this November. In fact, the Vice President will be in Arizona tomorrow as clinics in this state brace for that abortion ban to go into effect sometime in the next several weeks. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We will be watching. Okay, Rachel, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now Capitol Hill, where a key law in the fight against terrorism is in limbo. House Republicans blocked passage of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act after former President Trump called on them to kill it. And this comes as the \uc2 FBI\uc2  director is warning of an elevated terror threat. Selina Wang is on Capitol Hill. Good morning, Selina.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, George. That's right. House Republicans blocked that controversial surveillance law after Trump urged Republicans to kill the bill that would extend it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT IS FISA?\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, FISA gives the government authority to collect information on foreign nationals without a warrant and sometimes it swifts up communications of American private messages. Now, what happened in Congress is yet another example of the influence that Trump has over Republicans in Congress, and also it's yet another major blow to House Speaker Johnson, yet again failing to advance major legislation.\par \par \uc2 SELINA WANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, the White House and national security expert, they say that FISA is critical to protect America's national security. They say that, without it, we would lose vital information about threats to the homeland, threats to America's infrastructure, information on Russian war crimes, supply chain information, bringing drugs through the US border and much more. Now, \uc2 FBI\uc2  director, he is set to tell Congress today that he's concerned about groups carrying out attacks here in the homeland because of the conflict in the Middle East. He's also going to urge Congress to reauthorize FISA. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Selina, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CROMER, MARQUEZ, SMITH, FLOODING, TORNADOES, STORM\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HAMILTON, MARTINEZ, HERNANDEZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPUBLICAN LAWMAKERS BLOCK REPEAL OD 1864 ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 FISA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSE CONSERVATIVES BLOCK FOREIGN SURVEILLANCE BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPEAKER JOHNSON FACES GOP REVOLT AS FISA DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 DELAY, TRIAL, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST TENSIONS ESCALATING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. WARNS IRAN MAY RETALIATE AGAINST ISRAEL IN COMING DAYS\par \par \uc2 PARKER, ZWERNER, TOSCANO, GUN SHOW LOOPHOLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN TEACHER'S SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EX-ASSISTANT PRINCIPAL INDICTED ON EIGHT COUNTS OF FELONY CHILD NEGLECT\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MIZUHARA, THEFT, PLEA DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLEA DEAL IN MLB GAMBLING SCANDAL?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: OHTANI'S EX-INTERPRETER FACING FEDERAL CHARGES\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But first, let's go back to Gingers.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And this morning, we've got fog around. We've got the drizzle already happening. But like I said, the heavier rain is going to come in tonight. So, do look out in parts of the northeast for that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STRONG WINDS\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But with this storm, it's going to come with a considerable amount of wind. So, it's going to get really gusty. We're talking about gusts of 41 miles per hour. This is by early tomorrow morning. You'll be walking in going, ugh, in 45-mile-per-hour gusts there. Atlantic City, 50s. That's the kind that could even potentially impact some flights. Watch that early tomorrow. Your local weather in 30 seconds.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're diving into Thursday, and you don't want to miss the rest of this video. Yeah. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240430ek4b0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CHAOS AFTER ARIZONA ABORTION RULING DOCTORS, PATIENTS IN LIMBO AFTER NEAR-TOTAL BAN UPHELD\b0\par\par\uc2 605 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SIMPSON, CANCER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, FLOODING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS STORMS TAKE AIM AT NORTHEAST\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, RESTRICTIONS, ISRAEL, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WARNING TO U.S. PERSONNEL IN ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, GIBSON, MAYES, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHAOS AFTER ARIZONA ABORTION RULING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the abortion battle in Arizona after the state Supreme Court ruled a law from 1864 that banned nearly all abortions will take effect in a matter of weeks. State lawmakers left town without taking action. Doctors already describing chaos and confusion. ABC's Rachel Scott in Arizona tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCTORS, PATIENTS IN LIMBO AFTER NEAR-TOTAL BAN UPHELD\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, in Arizona, doctors describing chaos and confusion after the state's highest court upheld a 160-year-old law banning abortion in all cases, except to protect the life of the mother. Arizona's state legislature was expected to swiftly repeal the law, but Republicans blocked that effort.\par \par \uc2 POLITICIAN (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Shame on you.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Dr. Jill Gibson at \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  tells me the impact is already being felt.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What have you been experiencing the last 48 hours inside of this clinic?\par \par \uc2 DR JILL GIBSON (CHIEF MEDICAL DIRECTOR PLANNED PARENTHOOD ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Patients are already saying that they're looking for means of getting abortions through other means. Looking for pills online.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Arizona's Democratic Attorney General Kris Mayes says she won't enforce the law, but concedes she can't stop local prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 KRIS MAYES (ARIZONA ATTORNEY GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 I would urge Arizonans who are pregnant to make a plan. And I can't believe I'm having to say that, but it's time to make a plan for 60 days from now, if something goes wrong. If you need an abortion, if you want an abortion, start thinking about California and Nevada and New Mexico or Colorado.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION OR REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS COULD BE ON BALLOT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Voters could ultimately decide the issue in November when Arizona and as many as 13 other states could have abortion measures on the ballot. And the law has become a flashpoint in the race for the White House, where Arizona is a key battleground. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says he's proud to have appointed three of the five Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade. But sensing political quicksand, he now says abortion should be left to the states.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It was an incredible thing, an incredible achievement. We did that and now the states have it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, Trump says Arizona went too far. But President Biden says, by appointing the justices who helped overturn Roe, Trump cleared the way for 21 states to ban or severely restrict access to abortion. And tonight, in this state, these billboards going up, "Abortion is banned in Arizona thanks to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He won't stop until it's nationwide."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, there's a lot of uncertainty here in Arizona. The Supreme Court put that ruling on hold for 14 days. But tonight, the state's attorney general tells me that it could be an additional 45 days before that law goes into effect, because of a separate lawsuit. As for the White House, they want to keep this issue in the spotlight. The Vice President plans to visit Arizona tomorrow. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott in Phoenix tonight, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240415ek4b0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BEST SELLING AUTHOR LEIGH BARDUGO TALKS NEW BOOK, "THE FAMILIAR"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,026 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSAL STANDARD, RAINRAPS, VIM&VIGR, RYAN SIMKHAI, MALIBU SKYE, SOFTIES\par \par \uc2 DUNST, "CIVIL WAR"\par \par \uc2 FELLER, JUICE, SODA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLOBAL CLIMATE UPDATE: SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 CLEBURNE, HOUSTON, HOMESTYLE, 80 YEARS\par \par \uc2 BARDUGO, "THE FAMILIAR"\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with Leigh Bardugo, the number one "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " best-selling author behind "Ninth House" and "Hell Bent," which has sold more than 20 million copies around the world. Now, she's out with a new book, "The Familiar." Welcome, good to see you.\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Thank you for having me.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, tell us about "The Familiar." It's based on a family history?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Yes. "The Familiar" is set in late 16th century Spain, in Madrid. It's about a scullion, a kitchen maid who works in the house of an impoverished noble woman and she has little scraps of magic. She can unburn bread, she can make a grapevine grow...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Unburn bread?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, little things, little things, useful things if you have to get through the day. But, it's small magic until it's discovered by some very dangerous schemers in the court of King Phillip II. And one of them is a man named Gillian Sandanhill (PH) and once these two cross paths, they begin to form an alliance, but it is threatened at every turn by the inquisition.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, so how does it connect to your family history?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Okay, so 1492, the year for Spain, and they gave their Jewish population two options; you can convert to Christianity or you can leave, and you can leave only with what you can carry. You can't carry coin, no silver, no gold. Most of my ancestors decided to leave, they became exiles, but we know some remain and converted, and that branch of the family tree disappeared, so this book was a way of imagining it back into existence.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that's fascinating. Now, I've read that you write most of your books during the day, but this one at night?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I like to work in the day because writing is so solitary and it makes me feel like I'm part of the larger work force, but for some reason, this book wanted to be written at night, and I started to feel like there were ghosts looking over my shoulders. Like, my ancestors were sort of like, "Don't mess it up."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, okay. And, you know, so many people have watched "Shadow and Bone." What was it like seeing your work become imagined in a different way, I guess?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 I mean, like, it was true magic to see that happen, to walk onto a set and see those characters in costume, to see these things I had only dreamed come to life. And it was heart breaking, too, because there was so much story left to tell, so I'm grateful every day for our incredible cast, our incredible writers, and I hope that it will find a place someplace else.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As you know, you have a dedicated fan base. We've got some questions from some of your fans. Jay Stonefield (PH) writes, what advice do you have for other aspiring writers?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Okay, I have three pieces of advice. First of all, read outside of your comfort zone. It's going to make your own work better. Second, don't worry about the pressure. There is no expiration date on your talent. I didn't publish until I was 37. And third, stay off of social media.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Ah, that's good advice for anyone.\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 It really is, it really is. Beware, yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bee Falcone (PH) wants to know, what was on your playlist when writing "The Familiar?"\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 Well, I draft all of my books to a composer named Ludovico Einaudi. He is my favorite. And I also used a lot of period music, some of it composed on the (speaking in foreign language), which is what one of the competitors in this tournament for Phillip's attention plays to make magic of his own. And I also had some modern stuff, like Agnes Obel and Florence and The Machine, and even a little Stevie Nicks because I love Stevie.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Finally, Aleena Sunlight (PH) asks how would you describe "The Familiar" to someone who hasn't been introduced to your books at all?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH BARDUGO (AUTHOR "THE FAMILIAR")\par \par \uc2 I would describe it as one woman's ambition pitted against one of the most dangerous forces in history.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow, that is a sell. Thank you for coming in today. "The Familiar" is available now. You can keep reading along with us on our \uc2 Instagram\uc2  @gmabookclub. And we'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 No expiration date on your talent.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Exactly.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,554 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSAL STANDARD, RAINRAPS, VIM&VIGR, RYAN SIMKHAI, MALIBU SKYE, SOFTIES\par \par \uc2 DUNST, "CIVIL WAR"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do welcome you back to "gma." Our next guest known for her roles in "Spider-man," "Bring It On," as well as her Oscar nominated performance in "The Power of the Dog." Now, she is starring, you gotta see this action film, "Civil War." Kirsten Dunst, welcome back to "gma."\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Give it up for her. Come on, now. She got up early, she got up early and everything. Rave reviews already, 90 percent on Rotten Tomatoes. How do you describe the film?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Well, it's about war journalists and they're going from New York City to Washington, DC to photograph and interview the President, and we're in this dystopian kind of America where there's a civil war going on.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, you know, it's so very timely. Did you feel that when you were filming it?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 You know, he wrote it before January 6th, but it felt timely to me because when we were rehearsing, the war in Russia and Ukraine started, so it feels timely for the world, you know, not just specifically the United States. And what's clever about how Alex did this film is that it's not partisan, it's not putting any political agenda on the film, it really is, like, an action film disguised as, like, a real love letter to journalism.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you play a war photo journalist.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How did you prepare for it?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Well, as soon as I got the role, I was like, give me the camera that Lee uses because I wanted it to look like second nature, the way, you know, you wrap your strap around your wrist and hold all your equipment, and then watched a lot of documentaries. This Maria Coleman documentary, "Under The Wire" was the one that really spoke to me about this group of journalists and, you know, it's a very disturbing documentary, but to me it was kind of my north star of, like, how I feel like Lee and these people bond and are together in this.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's take a look at a clip.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP: "CIVIL WAR"\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I'm not angry about that, Jessie. I don't care what you do or don't know.\par \par \uc2 CAILEE SPAENY ("CIVIL WAR")\par \par \uc2 Okay, but you are angry with me.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 There is no version of this that isn't a mistake. I know because I'm it, Joe and Sammy are it.\par \par \uc2 CAILEE SPAENY ("CIVIL WAR")\par \par \uc2 It's my choice.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So intense. And I know we see, in the film, your husband, Jesse Plemons\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was reading the back story on how you got him to be in the film. Will you share?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Of course. We were doing rehearsals and the actor that was supposed to play the role dropped out and Alex was stressed and I was like, "Well, Jesse is here." Like, "He's here with the kids," you know, like.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I happen to know a guy.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, yeah, Alex and Jesse met and he read the script. Listen, his role is a horrendous role to play. Like, nobody wants to play that role, so I mean, I feel like he did his wife a favor. Do you know what I mean?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He got very into the sunglasses of it all, too.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 He did. I think there was, like, a weird psycho barrier thing going on that he used in that...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) His shield.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 ...and he went to a bunch of vintage stores in Atlanta and collected, like, tons of different pairs of sunglasses and tried them all on for me and Alex Garland, the director and that's, those are the...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You landed on those.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You won't forget them, trust me.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 No, you won't. No, you won't.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, you won't. Very excited for the film, very excited. Can I talk about "Bring It On?"\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, of course. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I can't believe, 25 years, 25 years.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. That makes me feel very old. It's amazing.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If, if, if...\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Okay.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...there was a reunion...\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...and I'm a little torn on this. I don't know if I want to see one or not, but if there was a reunion...\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...come on, you'd be in, right?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Of course I would. Like, what am I going to say, no? You know, but it would have to be such a good script. I mean, yeah, because those things can be sad sometimes if they're not good.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For lack of a better word, yeah.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was, when you were making that did you have any idea?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Have any idea?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 No, none at all. We were, like, left alone in San Diego to do our thing. Nobody even thought twice about us and I was just as shocked as anyone that this was, like, such a huge success. We weren't, we really didn't know, you know, the effect it has on our culture, you know?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, huge, huge.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. And you've been in this business nearly your entire life. And you think about "Bring It On," 25 years, "Interview With The Vampire," 30 years...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was just thinking about that.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...and that was your breakout role. So, what has been the greatest lesson that you've learned along the way?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 You know, now, looking back, I kind of grew up while making my own taste in films and discovering films, so that was kind of interesting. But, I think the biggest thing for me was doing "Interview With The Vampire," which was a very all male dominated set, and then going right from that to "Little Women," which was directed by a female, I think that, like, juxtaposition so young really informed my choices of working with a lot of females after. It was never a big thing for me, you know?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and I love how you make your choices. You don't have to take everything that comes across your desk. You can pick and choose.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I mean, I think that's the only way to have a long-lasting career is to, you know, be selective and follow your heart.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, be authentic (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Especially with two little ones, I mean, five and two. Come on.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I mean, yeah...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hands full.\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 ...yeah, I'm home a lot.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Got the sweatpants on, right?\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, exactly. That's exactly what I am. Like, from this to that. There is zero in between.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, you are a delight...\par \par \uc2 KIRSTEN DUNST (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...and a force of nature. Thank you always for making time for us. And "Civil War," you gotta see it, it is in theaters this Friday. Coming up, our "Comfort Food in America" tour making a stop in Michael's home town of Houston, Texas. Come on back.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yee haw.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR MOVE TO MAKE DRINKING WATER SAFER \uc2 EPA\uc2  ANNOUNCES NEW STANDARDS TO LIMIT "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to a major move this morning by the \uc2 Environmental Protection Agency\uc2  to make drinking water safer. Erielle Reshef is here with more. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Michael. This is big news. For first time, the \uc2 EPA\uc2  announced national and legally enforceable standards to limit six types of PFOS in drinking water. These types of chemicals are used in the manufacturing of many of the products that we use, like non-stick pans, waterproof clothing, and furniture. Research has raised concerns about the health risks of being exposed to high levels of PFOS over time, especially in our water and in our food.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) PFOS are often referred to as "forever chemicals" because they do not break down in the environment, which means they can seep into the soil and into water. They've been linked to cancer, liver damage, fertility, and thyroid problems, other health issues, as well. The Biden administration now allocating a billion dollars for states to test the water and says that the new regulations will reduce PFOS exposure for approximately 100 million people. Municipalities will have three years to monitor levels of these chemicals and an additional two years to be compliant with those standards or face possible fines and citations. Guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Erielle, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:15 CDC'S NEW MAMMOGRAM WARNING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up in our "GMA" Morning Menu, the CDC's new warning about mammograms and that women aren't getting them on time. Doctor Darien Sutton is here with those details.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12 ZENDAYA GETS CANDID\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, Zendaya with not one, but two new "Vogue" covers. She's getting candid about life in the spotlight as a young star and talking about Tom Holland.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21 DEALS AND STEALS SPRING BONANZA!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, Tory Johnson is here with more spring "Deals & Steals" all from small businesses, up to 61 percent off.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 KIRSTEN DUNST LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Lara is with a special guest. Hey, Lara.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I am. Kirsten Dunst is here to tell us all about her new movie. "Civil War" is getting rave reviews and we're excited to talk to you about that and so much more coming up on "Good Morning America." Don't go anywhere.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, WEDNESDAY, APRIL 10\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN NEW FALLOUT AFTER STATE SUPREME COURT REINSTATES NEAR-TOTAL BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First, a look at the top stories breaking at 8:00. We start with that bombshell ruling on abortion rights out of Arizona. The State Supreme Court decided to uphold an 1864 law, which bans the procedure with almost no exceptions. Let's go back to Rachel Scott. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George. Good morning to you, again. Arizona is now bracing for one of the strictest abortion bans in the nation to go into effect. This is a law that was passed during the civil war, 48 years before Arizona even became a state. It bans abortions in nearly all cases with one exception, to save the life of the mother. In a land mark decision, the Arizona State Supreme Court has now cleared the way for this to go into effect, and it is turning up the heat on an issue that could define this election.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The ruling refers to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 's decision overturning Roe v Wade 22 times. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  often boasts about appointing three of the six justices that overturned Roe. And just this week, he said states should make their own laws when it comes to abortion. President Biden calling this Arizona ban extreme, dangerous, and cruel. And the Vice President putting the blame squarely on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And so, while this ban will soon go into effect there in Arizona, the issue of abortion rights could soon be on the ballot in several key battleground states, including right there in Arizona, which means that voters could get the final say on all of this, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Could be. All right, Rachel. Our thanks to you, as always.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a00038\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 105 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) New York City, first 80 of the season, but things are about to change. I'll tell you about it. Your local weather, though, coming up in 30 seconds.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Stay right there. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a00031\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS SPRING BONANZA\b0\par\par\uc2 1,421 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 