\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSAL STANDARD, RAINRAPS, VIM&VIGR, RYAN SIMKHAI, MALIBU SKYE, SOFTIES\par \par \uc2 DUNST, "CIVIL WAR"\par \par \uc2 FELLER, JUICE, SODA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLOBAL CLIMATE UPDATE: SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Lara. In our rapidly warming world, we have an update from Copernicus. The oceans are still in unprecedented territory when it comes to the high temperatures. We've had those marine heat waves and that's not stopping on land either.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLOBAL TEMPERATURE RECORD: SURFACE AIR TEMP\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look at that yellow line. Red line was 2023, which was wild, right? Yellow, much above that already to start the year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMP DEPARTURE FROM AVERAGE: JANUARY - MARCH 2024\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And speaking of starting the year, Wisconsin, Michigan, New York, New Hampshire, Vermont, and Maine all had their second warmest start to the year, even though March in some places felt a little cooler, we were hot over the winter. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You were spilling, he was spilling his soda.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BEVERAGE BONANZA IS THE JUICE SODA WORTH THE SQUEEZE?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,100 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSAL STANDARD, RAINRAPS, VIM&VIGR, RYAN SIMKHAI, MALIBU SKYE, SOFTIES\par \par \uc2 DUNST, "CIVIL WAR"\par \par \uc2 FELLER, JUICE, SODA\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "gma." We are back now with the new beverage trend of juice sodas. Are they healthier than regular soda? Dietician and nutritionist, Maya Feller is with us right now. I love talking about this because a lot of people wonder about it. So, let me ask you, we are seeing these drinks pop up everywhere, what is the difference between juice soda and flavored sparkling water?\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Okay, so flavored sparkling water, like Spindrift, is literally seltzer water with a splash of real fruit and no sugar added. Juice soda can be flavored sparkling water with cane sugar and other juice concentrates...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so right there, that tells me...\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...that's the difference.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \u8230\'20\'26should go with this.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. I mean, I think if you're going to have a Spindrift, it's very much like this, a little bit of sparkling water and some lemon juice going everywhere. That's really what you're getting. Be mindful and intentional. Choose the things that have no added sugar.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEWARE OF ADDED SUGARS. ALWAYS CHECK LABELS\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Separately, if you're a person who likes things like orange juice and apple juice, opt for 100 percent juice. Why? Because that's really no added sugars there.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Does that mean it has to be fresh squeezed?\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 It doesn't have to be fresh squeezed, there's just no sugar added to it.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRINKING JUICE OR OTHER BEVERAGES WITH A MEAL MAY SLOW DOWN SUGAR ABSORPTION\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Try to go for four ounces. Pair it with a meal because that may help to slow down the sugar absorption into your bloodstream.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because you don't want your glucose spiking.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 To spike, that's exactly right.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 So, that's what I'm thinking when I'm looking at this 100 percent juice, always choosing that because there's no added sugar. And for some people, you know, they're going to choose this over a sugar sweetened beverage, like a traditional soda...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...and I say read the nutrition facts label, be an informed consumer...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...and know what you're drinking.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you want to just give people the heads up on the prebiotics because I think people are like, "Oh, they're healthy. I see prebiotic." You say tread lightly.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME BEVERAGE HEALTH CLAIMS ARE NOT GENERALLY ACCEPTED BY SCIENTISTS\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I say tread lightly. Listen, when you're having a prebiotic soda, know that it is a prebiotic soda. You're not actually adding any extreme nutrients to your overall day. If you want to have it, go for it, but it's not going to add nutrition to your overall day like these things here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SODA BEVERAGES WILL NOT ADD NUTRITIONAL VALUE TO YOUR DIET\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, all right. And is there, aside from the not adding, is there anything negative about it?\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 I wouldn't say that there's anything negative about it. It's a good alternative to sugar sweetened beverages for people who are looking for that...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...don't think that you're doing yourself this health favor...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because it says...\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Exactly.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...something that looks healthy.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Just because it has a health claim on it, listen, many scientists don't actually agree with those health claims...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...so, you know, we, as consumers...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do your homework.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Do your homework. We, as consumers, we've got to think twice before we put things in our mouth, especially when they're claiming to be good for our health.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, what do you do? Because I want to do what you do?\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness. Lara, I love that. Okay, what I do is this sparkling water with a little bit of lemon, lime.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 I also, truthfully, I'm a huge...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I like a Spindrift.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...I love a spindrift, and once in a while I may have a prebiotic soda, but I'm really aware...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you're feeling crazy.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 ...when I'm feeling crazy and when I'm aware that, listen, I'm having a prebiotic soda...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26it's an intentional and mindful choice.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And knowing there's sugar in there.\par \par \uc2 MAYA FELLER (REGISTERED DIETITIAN/NUTRITIONIST)\par \par \uc2 That's exactly right.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, I like it. I love these conversations. They really are so helpful. Thanks, Maya. We're going to throw it over to you, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SERVING UP SOUTHERN HOMESTYLE COOKING IN HOUSTON CLEBURNE CAFETERIA MAKING COMFORT CLASSICS FOR MORE THAN 80 YEARS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,566 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA, PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSAL STANDARD, RAINRAPS, VIM&VIGR, RYAN SIMKHAI, MALIBU SKYE, SOFTIES\par \par \uc2 DUNST, "CIVIL WAR"\par \par \uc2 FELLER, JUICE, SODA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLOBAL CLIMATE UPDATE: SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 CLEBURNE, HOUSTON, HOMESTYLE, 80 YEARS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I tried not to even look. I tried not to pay attention. You know, all week long, we are exploring some of best spots for comfort food across the country. This morning, our tour takes us to my hometown of Houston, Texas. That's right. Ike Ejiochi is there at a cafeteria that serves up classic southern dishes. And we've got to say it, good morning to you and everybody there, Ike.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Michael. Good morning, everybody. We are here at Cleburne Cafeteria, and as you can see, we have quite the loyal following with us, right? What's going on, guys? Now, this place has been open for business since 1941, and there's a real reason why people keep coming back. But, before we get to that delicious food, let's take a look at what makes this place our favorite for comfort food.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For home style, southern cooking, look no further than the Cleburne Cafeteria. From meat loaf and mashed potatoes to some fried chicken...\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I've been cooking all day in the kitchen, all morning in the kitchen.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...Texans lining up for a taste of Cleburne's most comforting dishes.\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The good food, vegetables and all the home cooking. When you can just come here and get it, it's so much easier.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Behind the line, owner George Mickelis...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 My dad taught me how to cook this roast beef, so I'm just going to cut it the way I was instructed to do many, many moons ago.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...running shifts for the business that has been in his family for more than 70 years. And for Houstonians, it's about more than about just food...\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We've been coming here four, five times a week since 1995.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...and its community is the heart of this classic cafeteria.\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This is why we come on Sundays after church.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we are here with George Mickelis, the owner of Cleburne Cafeteria. How you doing over here today?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 I am doing great, thank you. Good morning, thank you for being here.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, good morning. Let's walk and talk while we get into some food.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, when we talk and we think about cafeteria, it brings me back to those dusty chicken nuggets and old pizza from elementary school...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 No, (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...we don't have that here, okay.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 That's exactly right.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what makes a cafeteria perfect for comfort food?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think what it is, is you like to eat with your eyes...\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Of course.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 ...and when you come into a cafeteria, that's exactly what you're doing...\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 ...so, you're able to look at what you want to have, pick it out, and have it just the way your mom would serve you if you were at home.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, time to pick out some food. I see this fried...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...chicken here, going to need some of this fried chicken. What makes this so special?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think what it is, is you start off with a fresh bird. We make a buttermilk batter from scratch with fresh eggs. We dredge it through a nice seasoned flour and we fry it at 360 degrees...\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 ...in peanut oil, and I think that's the finest oil you can use for frying chicken, and it's delicious.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, what is this Thanksgiving every day here? We've got turkey, cranberry sauce. What's going on?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. That's our featured dish every day. It is Thanksgiving every day here at the Cleburne. We do an old braised and roasted turkey breast, which keeps it moist and delicious. We serve it every day of the year and people can come and celebrate Thanksgiving every day here at Cleburne.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, you can't have Thanksgiving without some sides, so tell me a little bit about these sides here. What are we eating?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Well, no question. Well, comfort food wouldn't be comfort food without macaroni and cheese, mashed potatoes, green beans, black eyed peas, and, of course, candied yams. We do everything from scratch. We go to the farmer's market every day to pick out fresh vegetables and offer them here, on the counter at Cleburne Cafeteria every day.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, did you miss something here? You've got all the food in the world over here.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 No, no. Yeah, we really do. We stack it deep, we sell it cheap. It's delicious. You can't go wrong at Cleburne Cafeteria.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's take a bite right now.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Okay.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I've got to take a bite. This chicken looks ridiculous, guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Okay. Good, good. You love it, don't you, Ike?\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's the morning, but I can have this any hour of the day.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 You could, you could, absolutely. Thank you so much. Macaroni and cheese.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I don't want to be the only one. Guys, come on.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Come on, everybody dig in.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This food is ridiculous, guys. Can we give it up for George, guys? This is (inaudible). Come here. This guy right here, he's been doing so much work here and we got a little surprise for you. Listen, I see a whole bunch of pictures on the wall, all right...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...I wanted to add a little bit to the wall. For you, for keeping this place open for over 80 years, your entire family, we wanted to commemorate you with something. It's not a Grammy, it's not an Emmy, it's something a little better. It's our "gma" Comfort Food plaque.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is going on the wall.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, yes, yes. Thank you. This guy's good.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for being a staple in this place for 80 years. It's phenomenal and I hope it goes on for 80 more years, all right.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE MICKELIS (OWNER CLEBURNE CAFETERIA)\par \par \uc2 Thank you very much. We are very honored. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 IKE EJIOCHI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back to you back in New York.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Ike. I asked George if anything was missing? Yeah, a plate for us here in the studio. That's what's missing, Ike. Man, all right. That was fantastic, though. Great place down in Houston, Cleburne. So, tomorrow, we're going to be live in Boston at one of the top spots there for a comfort classic, the burger.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oooh.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, come on. I will happily taste test.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, coming up, we have "\uc2 New York Times\uc2 " best-selling author, Leigh Bardugo here live. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POP NEWS\b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks, Robin. We will be watching that. And we will begin "Pop News" now with the first official look for the trailer for the "Joker: Folie A Deux." The sequel starring Lady Gaga as Harley Quinn and Joaquin Phoenix back in his Oscar winning role as the Joker is fierce. Check it out.\par \par \uc2 MOVIE CLIP: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX")\par \par \uc2 We use music to make us whole, to balance the fractures within ourselves.\par \par \uc2 LADY GAGA ("JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX")\par \par \uc2 Let's get out of here.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, they're madly in love, emphasis on mad. The studio debuted the trailer during Las Vegas CinemaCon where director, Todd Phillips told the audience he cast Gaga after seeing her perform in "A Star is Born" in which he was a producer. He went on to say that while he never talked about the movie as a musical specifically, it just turned out that music became an essential element in the making of this picture. The original "Joker" raked in over $1 billion at the box office when it debuted back in 2018.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How much?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) B, B, as in...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...with a B, yeah. And this one looks fantastic.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It does.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Joker: Folie A Deux" will hit theaters October 4th, that's five years to the day after the first one came out. It seems like a kind of a buckle your seat belt...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, it does.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "BRIDGET JONES" RETURNING FOR NEW INSTALLMENT\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...kind of film, right? Along for the ride. Hey, also this morning, you guys, Renee Zellweger has decided that she has another "Bridget Jones" in her. She will return to the title role in the fourth installment of the franchise. The new movie will be called "Bridget Jones Mad About The Boy." And, yes, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hugh Grant?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...Hugh Grant is back, and Daniel (inaudible), Emma Thompson is back. She was in the third rendition of the film, that was in 2016, so it's been a while. Also in this rendition, Chiwetel Ejiofor and "White Lotus" standout Leo Woodall. You guys, he played Jack in season two. The fourth movie we'll see Jones navigating work, family, and love as a 51-year-old single mother. It is now in production. We cannot, we missed her. I missed ya. I missed ya, Renee. I missed ya, Bridget. Welcome back.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They keep going to that well.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, well because it works. Yeah, a lot of money. I can't remember what the number was, but that, very successful franchise, so...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LENNY KRAVITZ IS OUR "GYMSPIRATION"\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...not surprising. And then finally, guys, what does a rock star wear to the gym? This is not a joke, just check this out. Go, Lenny, yes. He is our "gymspiration" on this hump day, skipping the Lululemons in favor of leather. His \uc2 Instagram\uc2  video has fans captivated on so many levels. He's wearing shades, combat boots, and let's talk about the reps. Did I mention Lenny turns 60 on May 26th? Lenny writes in part, "Never been better. There are no short cuts so seize your day." And that is your hump day moment.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's a great moment of, like, celebrities just like us.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. I thought it was George when I first saw the video.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Couldn't help myself.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 152 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 UNIVERSAL STANDARD, RAINRAPS, VIM&VIGR, RYAN SIMKHAI, MALIBU SKYE, SOFTIES\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "gma," live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 "JOKER", "BRIDGET JONES", KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "JOKER: FOLIE A DEUX" RELEASES FIRST TRAILER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, let's go to Ginger. Hey, Ginger.\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, if the leather pants make you do that, I will be wearing those today to the gym. Let's look at what's happening, though, today along the Gulf Coast. We just got brand new pictures in from Katy, Texas, damage there to a building. There have been a lot of wind reports, and there will be tornadoes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER OUTBREAK: TODAY AND TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's a new tornado watch that includes New Orleans and Jackson. So, today strong tornadoes possible with gusts above 75 miles per hour in some of those straight line wind events throughout parts of Louisiana, Mississippi, and Alabama, but beyond that, even into the Florida panhandle later tonight, but it's really throughout the day today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then, we'll move to the northeast. There are two pockets, Cleveland to Lexington gets it tomorrow, Savannah to Tampa, that's Thursday.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT: THURSDAY NIGHT\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then, we twist up to the northeast and dump a lot of rain, so we've got an elevated risk of flash flooding that includes Scranton, down to Washington, DC and Philadelphia. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ZENDAYA OPENS UP IN VOGUE "DUNE: PART TWO" STAR ON FAME, FASHION, AND FAMILY\b0\par\par\uc2 682 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Time for our "gma" Cover Story. Zendaya, star of the upcoming "Challengers" movie, co-host of the Met Gala, opens up in "Vogue" about fashion, fame, and starting a family. Lara's got all the details.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, I do, George. Good morning to you. So, Zendaya got very personal with "Vogue" about what it's like to be a full time child actress and what she wants for her own family one day. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, 27-year-old Zendaya is at the front of not one, but two "Vogue" covers as she embarks on co-chairing this year's Met Gala, joining JLo, Bad Bunny, and Chris Hemsworth.\par \par \uc2 CHLOE MALLE (EDITOR VOGUE.COM)\par \par \uc2 Carlijn Jacobs photographed the British "Vogue" cover and Annie Leibovitz photographed the American "Vogue" cover, and it's really fun to see how different the two pictures are.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Opening up to "Vogue" about her career and becoming what she calls the breadwinner of her family very early on, saying, as a kid, "there was a lot of role-reversal happening and just kind of becoming grown, really." Adding she was expected to be "this perfect being and be everything that everyone needs me to be and live up to all of these expectations," a sentiment she shared with Serena Williams during a Zoom with "Vogue." Williams asking Zendaya, what was the other option for you? What were your goals growing up? Zendaya replying, "It's something that I'm figuring out now. I don't know how much of a choice I had. I'm almost going through my angsty teenager phase now because I didn't really have the time to do it before."\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Sharing the limelight by her side is "Spider-man" co-star and boyfriend, Tom Holland, whose career she witnessed take off. "I definitely watched his life kind of change in front of him, but he handled it really beautifully." And when it comes to balancing fame and having a family, Zendaya says, "because I don't necessarily want my kids to have to deal with this, am I going to be a public-facing person forever?" Telling "Vogue" her dream scenario would be to "make things and pop out when I need to pop out, and then have a safe and protected life with my family."\par \par \uc2 CHLOE MALLE (EDITOR VOGUE.COM)\par \par \uc2 Family is a very important part of her identity, it seems, and that's definitely something she wants to prioritize going forward.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And she was so candid in that interview. Up next for her boyfriend, Tom Holland, he is starring in "Romeo and Juliet" in London's West End and Zendaya says she will be there to support him every step of the way. Her British and American "Vogue" May 2024 issues will be available on newsstands nationwide April 23rd.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) My girls are fascinated with that couple.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Agreed, agreed. She's really nice.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm. Let's go to Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep, everything about her.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CDC'S NEW MAMMOGRAM WARNING NEW REPORT FINDS MANY WOMEN NOT GETTING PROCEDURE IN A TIMELY MANNER\b0\par\par\uc2 957 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 EPA\uc2 , PFOS, DRINKING WATER, STANDARDS, "FOREVER CHEMICALS"\par \par \uc2 ZENDAYA, VOGUE, "DUNE", FASHION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 SUTTON, MAMMOGRAMS, CDC, WARNING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, a new CDC report about mammograms and if women are up to date or getting their screenings at all. Our medical correspondent, Doctor Darien Sutton is here. We've got to break this down, 40,000...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Some really (inaudible) numbers.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...40,000 breast cancer deaths a year here in the US. We know that screenings are so vital, so what's going on with this report?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OBSTACLES FOR WOMEN FACING SOCIAL CHALLENGES\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Screenings are so vital and so important, so what's concerning about this new report that I have been understanding myself is that the numbers are not where they should be. One in four women overall don't get their timely mammograms and one in three women, Robin, more than that, 33 percent, those women with significant social health barriers, are not getting their recommended mammogram. So what are those health barriers? That is in that world of what we call social determinants of health, the things in our life that affect our health that are not just medical, including things like job security, food insecurity, lack of transportation, and cost barriers. And we're finding that those are the reasons that are keeping women away from mammograms, which are so vital.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. They are the gold standard still.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gold standard.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, and the guidelines on who should be getting a mammogram, those always seem to be changing.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They are, and also they can be confusing...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...which can prevent women from getting their recommended screenings, so I think it's important to understand what are the guidelines today? So, after reviewing them with the US Preventative Service Task Force, it was before, starting at the age of 50, but today, and soon to be approved, women should start getting their mammograms at 40, and then every other year after that. And, Robin, if you have a significant family history or if you're personally at risk, it's important to talk to your physician about what your recommendations might be. It might be more frequent, it might start earlier, and it's always important to remember that an early diagnosis, or catching it early, always has a better prognosis.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. And every time we do a segment, I hear from the men. Men get breast cancer too. It happens to them, as well.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're absolutely right. The risk is lower for us, but the risk...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Sure\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...is still there, and I think that if you have a family history, or if you have specific genetic risk factors that you might be aware of in your family, you have to have a conversation with your doctor because the recommendations, although they're not general, they can change, depending on what your risk factors are.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It impacted my big brother, and I know Michael had the same issue, as well. So, okay, you're hearing all this information...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...you're taking it all in...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...what should you do?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET FREE OR LOW-COST CARE\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, first and foremost, of course, having a conversation with your provider about your risk factors, talking openly about your family history and your personal risk factors, for example smoking or any diagnosis of cancer, and then also understanding what opportunities are out there for you. Many don't realize this, but Medicare and most private insurance coverage covers mammograms starting at the age of 40. If you don't have health care coverage or you are not able to afford, National Early Detection Program, you can simply search it in your browser, and it can provide resources in your community. These mammograms, Robin, decrease the risk of death after diagnosis of cancer by more than 40 percent, so they are forever important.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and there's, I'm so glad, there's so much information out there for people who think that they don't qualify or they can't, there's so many organizations that want to help...\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...them get a mammogram. All right, see you on "GMA3?"\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR DARIEN SUTTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) See me on "gma3."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, let's get some "Pop News" now with Lara.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0003c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FAA\uc2  INVESTIGATES NEW BOEING CLAIMS WHISTLEBLOWER SAYS 787 DREAMLINERS COULD BREAK APART\b0\par\par\uc2 480 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT, REINSTATES, BAN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, 787, WHISTLEBLOWER, SALEHPOUR, GANYARD\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to the \uc2 FAA\uc2  investigating claims from a new \uc2 Boeing\uc2  whistleblower. The employee saying engineering issues could cause some \uc2 Boeing\uc2  planes to break apart. Let's go back to our transportation correspondent, Gio Benitez with those details. Good morning, again, Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning, again. Yeah, the whistleblower says that he's told \uc2 Boeing\uc2  executives about all of this, but that they aren't listening, and now he's speaking out.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the \uc2 FAA\uc2  is investigating claims from a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  whistleblower who says there are engineering issues with 787 Dreamliners that he says could cause the planes to break apart after decades of use. One of his biggest claims, that parts of the plane's fuselage are being fastened together improperly. That engineer, Sam Salehpour, speaking out overnight.\par \par \uc2 SAM SALEHPOUR (ENGINEER)\par \par \uc2 I'm doing this not because I want \uc2 Boeing\uc2  to fail, but because I want it to succeed and prevent the crashes from happening.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Salehpour has not yet provided any documented evidence and \uc2 Boeing\uc2  is firing back in a lengthy statement saying in part, "These claims about the structural integrity of the 787 are inaccurate. The issues raised have been subject to rigorous engineering examination under \uc2 FAA\uc2  oversight. This analysis has validated that these issues do not present any safety concerns and the aircraft will maintain its service life over several decades." In 2021 and 2022, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  slowed production and stopped delivering 787's for nearly two years because of these exact concerns. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  found a solution and the \uc2 FAA\uc2  signed off on it, deliveries resumed in 2022.\par \par \uc2 STEPHEN GANYARD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We don't know what facts this whistleblower has presented to the \uc2 FAA\uc2 . \uc2 Boeing\uc2  says that these issues were taken care of years ago, so right now, the onus is on the \uc2 FAA\uc2  to tell the flying public is this a new problem or has it already been dealt with.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the whistleblower says that he's going to testify next week on Capitol Hill with evidence. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, Gio.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a00039\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, MATTHEWS, MYRE, BEAUSOLEIL, ST. JULIANA\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCED, NEGLIGENCE, GUNS, VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, MCCOLLUM, CRAFT, MCARDLE, IANNACE, JONES, ELEANOR\par \par \uc2 BABIES, SAVANNAH, RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. Abortion rights showdown. Arizona now bracing for one of the strictest abortion bans in the country after the State Supreme Court revived a 160-year-old law. President Biden calls it extreme and dangerous. What it all means for voters in November.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC WARNING: DID YOU GET A MAMMOGRAM?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Did you get a mammogram? The urgent new warning from the CDC. Are enough women getting screened on time or at all? Plus, how often you should get checked.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOUBLE COVERS WITH VOGUE: ZENDAYA\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Zendaya shining on the cover of British and American "Vogue." The stunning photos. Plus, she's talking about the pressure she puts on herself, her relationship with Tom Holland, plus her one-on-one with the GOAT, Serena Williams.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROCK STAR "GYMSPIRATION": LENNY KRAVITZ\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Lenny Kravitz taking gym fashion to rock star level.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE: KIRSTEN DUNST!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Kirsten Dunst is live in Times Square, talking about her buzzing new movie.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMFORT FOOD AMERICA: ORDER UP!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And order up. Our "Comfort Food America" tour pulls into my hometown, Houston, serving up what customers love.\par \par \uc2 RESTAURANT GOER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Delicious home cooking.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're there live as we say good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "gma."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. "Comfort Food America" hits my hometown of Houston. There's a lot of food on that table for our guy, Ike Ejiochi. He's at Cleburne Cafeteria, which has been serving up the classics for more than 80 years. There is a lot of great food there to eat. I have been and I can tell you from experience.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So, you know of what you speak? Yes, you do.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, I do.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also ahead, juice sodas. Yeah, they're popular, but are they healthy think for you? Maya Feller will be here to break it down and let you know.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a00037\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 7:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 393 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 STORMS, RAIN, FLOODING, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, POLICE, VIDEO, REED, TRAFFIC STOP, COHEN\par \par \uc2 BOEING, \uc2 FAA\uc2 , DREAMLINERS, SALEHPOUR, BANKS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , TRIAL, TACTICS, APPEALS, JURY\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FED, REPORT, MORTGAGES, APR, STAMPS\par \par \uc2 VANDERVEER, STANFORD, RETIRE, BASKETBALL, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Back here on "GMA." A favorite of ours here at "GMA," especially Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Go into our "GMA" vault and you'll see what we mean. Lady Gaga in "A Star Is Born." And now she's back on the big screen in the new "Joker" movie. Lara has a look coming up in "Pop News."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Looking forward to that. Following a lot of headlines right now, including Arizona bracing for one of the strictest abortion bans in the country. The State Supreme Court decided to uphold an 1864 law that bans the procedure with almost no exceptions. This law was during the Civil War, 48 years before Arizona even became a state. This national issue could define the presidential election.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2  DIRECTOR ON ISIS-K THREAT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also right now, \uc2 FBI\uc2  Director is warning that an attack on the US by ISIS-K is of increasing concern. \uc2 Christopher Wray\uc2  told the \uc2 American Bar Association\uc2  the October 7th attack on Israel will, quote, "Feed a pipeline of radicalization for years to come."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUNCHABLES IN SCHOOLS?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, Consumer Reports is urging schools not to serve Lunchables to students. Consumer Reports found they are very high in sodium, higher than the versions sold in supermarkets.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIGER WOODS GEARING UP FOR THE MASTERS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Tiger Woods is giving himself a thumbs up ahead of the Master's tournament, which tees off tomorrow. The golf superstar is confident that he can win another green jacket despite the injuries that largely sidelined him for the past year.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're looking forward to watching him get out there with the rest of the guys and compete. And we got a lot more ahead, including the \uc2 EPA\uc2 's new rules about so called forever chemicals in drinking water. That's all coming up, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a00032\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 617 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America. Another state now bracing for one of the strictest abortion bans in the country. Abortion rights showdown. New fallout after Arizona's State Supreme Court revived a 160-year-old law. President Biden calling it extreme and dangerous, as 21 states have now banned or restricted access to abortion since the Supreme Court overturned Roe V. Wade. And what it all means for voters in November.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEWLY RELEASED BODYCAM VIDEO\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Newly released Chicago police body cam video.\par \par \uc2 POLICE OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Open the door now.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The urgent investigation underway to find out how this traffic stop turned deadly, with 96 shots fired in 41 seconds.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC SENTENCING\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Historic sentencing. The first American parents convicted for their child's deadly school shooting, sentenced to 10 to 15 years in prison.\par \par \uc2 REINA ST. JULIANA (SISTER OF HANNA ST. JULIANA)\par \par \uc2 Hanna didn't even have 15 years to live.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The victims' families with emotional responses in court.\par \par \uc2 NICOLE BEAUSOLEIL (MOTHER OF MADISYN BALDWIN)\par \par \uc2 When you texted Ethan, don't do it, I was texting Madisyn, I love you, please call mom.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What the Crumbleys said in court, and we hear from the prosecutor in a morning exclusive.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW REGULATIONS FOR "FOREVER" CHEMICALS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New regulations for forever chemicals in drinking water. The major move this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT NEW WARNING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Did you get a mammogram? The urgent new warning from the CDC. Are enough women getting screened on time or at all? Plus, how often you should get checked.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW BOEING WHISTLEBLOWER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New \uc2 Boeing\uc2  whistleblower, saying there are serious engineering issues with one of \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's most popular planes that could cause it to break apart.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SORORITY SISTERS TO THE RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Sorority sisters to the rescue. When five college students saw a car plunge off a bridge with a mom and her two young children inside.\par \par \uc2 CORI CRAFT (MOTHER SAVED BY SORORITY SISTERS)\par \par \uc2 I was scared I was gonna lose the little one.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How the brave young women leaped into action.\par \par \uc2 ELEANOR (FRESHMAN UNIVERSITY OF GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 They're breathing. They're breathing.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the emotional reunion this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TARA VANDERVEER SAYS GOODBYE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 After a legendary season, the legendary winningest head coach in all of college basketball.\par \par \uc2 BASKETBALL GAME ANNOUNCER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 So much love for their head coach.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tara VanDerveer is leaving the court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. 38 years. 38 years at Stanford. And this is what she said. She said, "The joy for me was in the journey of each season, seeing a group of young women work hard for each other and form an unbreakable bond." The many countless lives that she has impacted.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She made a big, big impact. We have a lot of news this morning. New inflation numbers are gonna be out today. Rebecca Jarvis is gonna be here to break down what it means for car loans, credit cards and mortgage rates.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, Ginger is tracking the severe weather outbreak with tornado watches and warnings right now.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN NEW FALLOUT AFTER STATE SUPREME COURT REINSTATES NEAR TOTAL BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 750 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, ARIZONA, HOBBS, BURCH, GOODRICK, TIEN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First the bombshell ruling on abortion rights out of Arizona. The State Supreme Court decided to uphold an 1864 law that bans the procedure with almost no exceptions. Rachel Scott starts us off. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA ABORTION RIGHTS SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT AFTER STATE SUPREME COURT REINSTATES NEAR TOTAL BAN\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning to you This is a law that was passed during the Civil War, 48 years before Arizona even became a state. But in a landmark decision the Arizona Supreme Court Justices have now cleared the way for that ban to go into effect. And it is turning up the heat on an issue that could define this election.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Arizona is bracing for one of the strictest abortion bans in the country after the State Supreme Court revived a 160-year-old law.\par \par \uc2 GOV KATIE HOBBS (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 The near total Civil War era ban that continues to hang over our heads, only serves to create more chaos for women and doctors in our state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The law was written in 1864 before Arizona was even a state, and before women had the right to vote. No exceptions for rape or incest, only to protect the mother's life. The ruling by the Arizona court referring 22 times to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 's decision overturning Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has boasted of appointing three of the six justices who overturned Roe. Just this week he said states should make their own laws when comes to abortion.\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The states will determine, by vote or legislation or perhaps both, and whatever they decide must be the law of the land, in this case the law of the state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) President Biden calling the ban extreme, dangerous and cruel. Biden and Trump both know that abortion rights has won in all six states where it has been on the ballot, including conservative states likes Kansas, Kentucky and Ohio. This November it could be on the ballot in 14 states, including battleground Arizona.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And overnight several Republicans in that state distancing themselves from the ruling. GOP Senate candidate Kari Lake, who once vocally supported the law, now saying it's "Out of step with Arizonans." And Republican Congressman Juan Ciscomani calling the decision a "Disaster for women and providers."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Frustration felt on both sides of the aisle. Arizona Democratic lawmaker Eva Burch, recently had an abortion after she learned her pregnancy was nonviable.\par \par \uc2 STATE SEN EVA BURCH (DEM) (ARIZONA)\par \par \uc2 Somebody gave me a procedure so that I wouldn't have to experience another miscarriage, the pain, the mess, the discomfort. And now we're talking about whether or not we should put that doctor in jail.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Doctors who perform abortions could face up to five years in prison.\par \par \uc2 GABRIELLE GOODRICK (MEDIAL DIRECTOR CAMELBACK FAMILY PLANNING)\par \par \uc2 The need for reproductive health care and abortion care doesn't go away in a state where it's made illegal. The legality of it doesn't affect the needs.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Shelly Tien is an OB/GYN specializing in high risk pregnancies in Arizona, she also works as an abortion provider in three states.\par \par \uc2 DR. SHELLY TIEN (ABORTION CARE PROVIDER PLANNED PARENTHOOD SOUTH EAST N. FL)\par \par \uc2 These decisions should only be left up to patients, and to completely rob patients and families from being able to make these decisions, it's truly, truly, it's terrible. It's cruel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) On the other side of this, anti-abortion rights groups are celebrating this decision, insisting that it protects the lives of countless unborn children. The justices in Arizona have now put this ruling on hold for 14 days, so abortion clinics in that state tell us that they still plan to continue to provide their services for a short period of time, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rachel, it is very clear that this issue is going to be at the center of this presidential election. Rachel Scott, thanks very much. Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4a0002u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP: AZ ABORTION BAN WENT TOO FAR ARIZONA GOP LAWMAKERS FIGHT EFFORT TO REPEAL 1864 BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TORNADOES, EVACUATION\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, BETHEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTOUT AT CROWDED RAMADAN EVENT\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, BIDEN, ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: AZ ABORTION BAN WENT TOO FAR\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, growing backlash after Arizona's Supreme Court upheld a law from 1864 that criminalizes all abortions, except to save the mother's life. Republican lawmakers in the state blocking democratic efforts to repeal it. The issue sure to be a flashpoint in the race for the White House. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who, just this week, said states should decide their own abortion policy, now saying Arizona went too far. ABC's Rachel Scott is in Phoenix tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARIZONA GOP LAWMAKERS FIGHT EFFORT TO REPEAL 1864 BAN\par \par \uc2 POLITICIAN (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Shame on you. Shame on you.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, outrage in Arizona. Republican lawmakers in the state Capitol blocking Democrats' efforts to roll back a 160-year-old law banning abortion with only one exception, to save the life of the mother.\par \par \uc2 POLITICIANS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Save women's lives.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It comes 24 hours after the Arizona Supreme Court upheld the law written before Arizona was even a state and before women had the right to vote. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who, just this week, said states should decide their own abortion policy, today saying Arizona went too far.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Did Arizona go too far, sir?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, they did, and that will be straightened out. And, as you know, it's all about states' rights. That will be straightened out.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It comes as Trump tries to recast his own position on abortion, sensing it's become a losing issue for Republicans. He now says he's proud of appointing three of the six Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade, but that abortion policy should be up to the states.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It was an incredible thing, an incredible achievement. We did that. And now, the states have it, and the states are putting out what they want. It's the will of the people.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just weeks ago, Trump was floating the idea of a national ban on abortion. But today, he said, he would not sign one.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 President Trump, would you sign a national abortion ban if Congress sent it to your desk? Would you sign...\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Over the years, Trump's position on abortion has swung back and forth\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm very pro-choice. I'm pro-life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump once said there should be some sort of punishment for women who get abortions, a position he quickly walked back. Today, he refused to say whether he believes doctors should face punishment for performing abortions, as they do right now in Arizona and other states.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you think a doctor should be punished for performing abortions?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'd let that be to the states. You know, everything we're doing now is states.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, the Biden campaign saying \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  set out to overturn abortion rights in America, and he did, insisting Trump "owns the suffering and chaos happening right now." And when asked his message to the people of Arizona, a key campaign battleground, tonight, President Biden was blunt, "Elect me."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott with us now from Phoenix. And, Rachel, as you noted there, Republican lawmakers blocking Democrats' efforts to repeal that 160-year-old abortion ban. So, bottom line here, where do things stand right now in Arizona?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, Arizona is in a state of limbo. The Supreme Court here in Arizona put that ruling on hold for 14 days. Democrats and Republicans were racing to try to repeal that law before it went into effect. Well, tonight, Republicans blocking those efforts. The Democratic Governor \uc2 Katie Hobbs\uc2  calling their actions unconscionable, saying that the Republican majority had a chance to do the right thing and, tonight, they failed. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240415ek4a00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, tornado strikes and severe storms as we come on the air. The shootout at a crowded Ramadan celebration in Philadelphia. And the abortion battle in Arizona. President Biden and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  both weighing in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY STORMS STRIKE IN THE SOUTH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 First, those deadly storms sweeping across the south. Confirmed tornadoes in Texas and Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 STORM CHASER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Big, big tornado.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 More than 50 people rescued from an apartment complex. Watches posted in several states along the Gulf Coast. Heavy rain, flooding, and winds gusting up to 70 miles per hour. The system next taking aim at the East Coast, then pushing up the northeast. Rob Marciano timing it all out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MULTIPLE PEOPLE SHOT AT RAMADAN EVENT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking news. The images coming in. Police racing to the scene of a shooting in Philadelphia. At least three people shot during a celebration marking the end of Ramadan. About 1,000 people there. Adults rushing to get children to safety. Stephanie Ramos in Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: AZ ABORTION RULING WENT TOO FAR\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, facing major backlash to Arizona's strict abortion ban, Republican lawmakers in the state blocking Democratic efforts to repeal the 160-year-old law. The issue again dominating the race for the White House. President Biden has called the law extreme and dangerous. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , who takes credit for the Supreme Court overturning Roe v. Wade, saying the Arizona law goes too far. Rachel Scott in Phoenix tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONSUMERS HIT BY NEW INFLATION PAIN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A crucial setback for the American economy. Inflation up 3.5% from one year ago, its highest point in six months. American families paying more for gas, rent, and clothes. Could this delay an interest rate cut?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 EPA\uc2  LIMITING 'FOREVER CHEMICALS'\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 For the first time, the \uc2 EPA\uc2  reducing so-called forever chemicals. A major step to protect drinking water across the US.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FMR. SCHOOL OFFICIAL CHARGED IN SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, a special grand jury in Virginia indicting a former assistant principle at an elementary school for child neglect after a first grader shot and wounded his teacher. Prosecutors accusing her of ignoring other teachers who warned the child may have a gun.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT MANHUNT FOR FORMER OFFICER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 An urgent manhunt underway tonight. Police searching for one of their own former officers, considered armed and dangerous. The news coming in late today. ABC News confirming an arrest warrant has been issued for \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  star Rashee Rice following that high-speed crash in Dallas.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA STRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "America Strong" tonight. The heroes on the home-front during World War II honoring Rosie the Riveters.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240415ek4a00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 VATICAN ISSUES STATEMENT ON "HUMAN DIGNITY" CHURCH CALLS GENDER FLUIDITY, GENDER CHANGE, AND SURROGACY THREATS\b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TERROR THREAT, MERCURIO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MAN CHARGED IN ALLEGED TERROR PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCUSED OF PLANNING TO CARRY OUT ATTACKS ON CHURCHES IN SUPPORT OF \uc2 ISIS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER OUTBREAK TAKES AIM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS ACROSS SOUTH & MIDWEST AT RISK FOR TORNADOES & HUGE HAIL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , DELAY, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAST-DITCH LEGAL MANEUVERS IN TRUMP "HUSH MONEY" CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM ATTEMPTING TO DELAY START OF TRIAL\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HARRIS, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: ABORTION SHOULD BE LEFT TO STATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT DRAWS CRITICISM FROM ALLIES WHO WANT NATIONAL BAN\par \par \uc2 SCAM, E-ZPASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: E-ZPASS SCAM WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: USERS GETTING PHONY TEXTS ASKING FOR MONEY\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, INFLATION, INTEREST RATES, DIMON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ARE 8% INTEREST RATES IN OUR FUTURE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING FROM HEAD OF AMERICA'S BIGGEST BANK\par \par \uc2 MARCH MADNESS, FINALS, NEWTON, EDEY, CLINGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UCONN GOES BACK-TO-BACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUSKIES BEAT PURDUE TO WIN SECOND STRAIGHT NATIONAL TITLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 HURLEY, NCAA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UCONN COACH DAN HURLEY ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUSKIES BEAT PURDUE TO WIN SECOND STRAIGHT NATIONAL TITLE\par \par \uc2 WALLEN, ASWAD, ARREST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORGAN WALLEN ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTRY STAR ACCUSED OF THROWING CHAIR FROM NASHVILLE ROOFTOP BAR\par \par \uc2 SOLAR ECLIPSE, EDELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD OF GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIMONE GORRINDO TALKS "THE WIVES" 8:37\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT: TERROR TAKEDOWN\par \par \uc2 IDAHO, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , TERROR, CHURCHES, MERCURIO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 MICHIGAN, SCHOOL, CRUMBLEY, SENTENCING, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 VATICAN, GENDER, SURROGACY, STATEMENT, ISSUES\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn now to the Vatican's new statement on issues like surrogacy, abortion, and more. Our foreign correspondent, James Longman joins us with more on that. Good morning, James.\par \par \uc2 JAMES LONGMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, good morning, Rebecca. \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has been accused by some of being too liberal and by others of being not liberal enough. This latest affirmation of Catholic doctrine is reigniting that debate. Now, the issues, this document is called "Human Dignity" and it outlines their opposition to sex change surgery and to gender identity. They say that anyone who chooses to change their sex that they were assigned with at birth risks essentially playing God. They also outline their opposition to abortion and on surrogacy, they say that it is a violation of both the woman and the child.\par \par \uc2 JAMES LONGMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, last year \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  did say that transgender people would be welcome to be baptized in the church. He also opened the possibility for same sex unions to have their unions blessed in the church. I think it's safe to say that he's tried to have a theme of forgiveness and tolerance as part of his papacy, but this text shows the Catholic doctrine is not changing. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, James, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:44 SALT SUBSTITUTES AND YOUR HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up in our "GMA" Morning Menu, the new report on salt substitutes. Doctor Darien Sutton breaks down how they can help you live longer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:12 AI AND SCHOOL WORK\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, is using ai at school cheating? We'll tell you how parents and educators, what do you think, Michael? How parents and educators can learn from the new tool.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:30 COMFORT FOOD AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus, we're in Denver this morning for our "Comfort Food America" series, checking out the delicious tacos from a favorite restaurant in the mile high city.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:21 DEALS AND STEALS!\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Lara is with Tory Johnson. Hey, Lara.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael. Yeah, big bargains are blossoming today. Tory's "Deals & Steals" spring bonanza is kicking off three days of super savings starting this morning, just $7 they're starting at. And did we mention there's a leg massager? Oh, you're going to get a real close-up of that. Yeah, there you go, Sal. All that and more coming up on "gma."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, TUESDAY, APRIL 9\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek490000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP: ABORTION SHOULD BE LEFT TO STATES FORMER PRESIDENT DRAWS CRITICISM FROM ALLIES WHO WANT NATIONAL BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 716 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TERROR THREAT, MERCURIO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MAN CHARGED IN ALLEGED TERROR PLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCUSED OF PLANNING TO CARRY OUT ATTACKS ON CHURCHES IN SUPPORT OF ISIS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER OUTBREAK TAKES AIM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MILLIONS ACROSS SOUTH & MIDWEST AT RISK FOR TORNADOES & HUGE HAIL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , DELAY, TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAST-DITCH LEGAL MANEUVERS IN TRUMP "HUSH MONEY" CASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT'S LEGAL TEAM ATTEMPTING TO DELAY START OF TRIAL\par \par \uc2 ABORTION BAN, TRUMP, HARRIS, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: ABORTION SHOULD BE LEFT TO STATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT DRAWS CRITICISM FROM ALLIES WHO WANT NATIONAL BAN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is under fire from all sides on abortion rights. The former president now says the issue should be for the states to decide, prompting the members of his own party to disagree. Democrats say Trump is backing the country's strictest bans on abortion. Rachel Scott has the story. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Goerge, good morning to you. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made it clear, this is all about politics. He has been trying to find a winning message on this issue. So, after months of floating the idea of a possible 15-week national abortion ban, he now says the decision should be left up the states, sparking backlash on both sides.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is facing criticism from his own party after declaring that the issue of portion should be up to individual states.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 The states will determine by vote or legislation or perhaps both. And whatever they decide must be the law of the land, in this case the law of the state.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But as President, Trump appointed three justices who supported overturning Roe. And during his video announcement, saying he's proudly the person responsible for the Supreme Court's decision. The Vice President firing back.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Proudly responsible that one in three women of reproductive age now live in a state with an abortion ban. If he were to be put back in a position where he could sign off on a law, he would sign off on a national abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The former president making it clear politics is at the heart of his decision, keenly aware abortion rights had won in all six states where it had been on the ballot, including conservative states like Kansas, Kentucky, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 You must follow your heart on this issue. But remember, you must also win elections.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But many on the right outraged that Trump declined to endorse a national abortion plan. His former vice president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , calling his announcement a slap in the face to millions of pro-life Americans who voted for Trump. And close ally Senator Lindsay Graham saying, he respectfully disagrees. President Biden pointing out 21 states have banned or restricted access to abortion since the fall of Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just endorsed every state ban on reproductive care nationwide.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trump says that he does support exceptions for rape, incest and to save the life of the mother. He did not say if he also supports exceptions for health of the mother, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Rachel, this does leave open a lot of questions about what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  would actually do if he were elected president again.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, it is notable that the former president did not say what he would do on this issue if he were to be elected, whether he would sign a national abortion ban into law if it came on to his desk or whether even he supports access to medication abortion. Of course, Trump himself has been on all sides of this issue over the years, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what he did as president is what counts. Okay, Rachel, thanks very much. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240429ek4900005\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/2021 to 06/30/2026\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Source\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li5